INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('c953b884-7f4','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Here it is — everything lives in one repo root in this works','fastchat',80,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-22 01:40:40','{}','{"boundary_index": 56, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nThe user presented the full `opensciencelab` repo and redirected the assistant from \"add ROADMAP.md / git init\" to: **\"find the last code implemented and begin working on the last phase which was last worked upon.\"** The standing intent is to continue development of the project, picking up exactly where the previous implementation session left off. No \"never do X\" constraints were stated. The user expects the assistant to identify the concrete unfinished work and implement it, not offer further meta-options.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- **Two-product platform**: Structure & design (Boltz-2/Chai-1/RFdiffusion/ProteinMPNN) + molecular scoring/optimization (QED-lite \u2192 MACE/ChGNet \u2192 OpenEvolve evolutionary search).\n- **Phase 0 (complete)**: Pure-contract layer \u2014 `base.py` (Adapter ABC, Bundle, Artifact, registry), `manifest.py` (Manifest, Budget, RunDirectory), `services.py` (4 service facades + shared Budget), `preflight.py` (red-line guardrails), `report.py` (5-section memo). No heavy deps. Legacy shims at `evaluators.py` and `agents/`.\n- **Phase 1 (mostly complete)**: `backends.py` (real Boltz-2 CLI, Chai-1, ProteinMPNN wrappers; `BackendNotAvailable` fallback to offline artifact), `gpucheck.py` (torch matmul verification for ROCm/gfx1151), `cli.py` (demo/preflight/score/registry/gpucheck subcommands), `docker/Dockerfile` (ROCm PyTorch base, HSA_GFX arg), `docker/docker-run.sh` (`/dev/kfd`+`/dev/dri` plumbing).\n- **Phase 2 (last phase worked on \u2014 IN PROGRESS)**: Real QM tiers (PysCF tier-2, MACE on top) + real OpenEvolve loop. Code already exists in the tree: `backends.py` has Phase 2 QM engine stubs (lines ~20, ~387), `adapters/scoring.py` has T0/T1/T2 tiered scoring with MACE/ChGNet paths, `adapters/optimize.py` has the OpenEvolve real-path + offline fallback. Grep confirms Phase 2 references in README line 197 and backends.py lines 20 & 387. **This is the phase to finish.**\n- **GPU target**: AMD Strix Halo, gfx1151, native ROCm (not Vulkan). `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.5.1` primary, `11.0.2` fallback.\n- **Design policy for heavy backends**: Adapters call `backends.py`; on `BackendNotAvailable` they emit a deterministic offline placeholder artifact and record the failure reason in the manifest patch so the pipeline still completes auditable end-to-end.\n- **RFdiffusion deliberately excluded** from the default Docker image (its pip install pulls NVIDIA torch, clobbering ROCm torch). ProteinMPNN covers the design contract.\n- **Scoring tiers**: T0 = RDKit-free SMILES-lite QED (every candidate in inner loop); T1 = MACE/ChGNet; T2 = full scoring.\n- **Optimize adapter**: Dual-path \u2014 real OpenEvolve `run_evolution` when importable + LLM config present; otherwise offline deterministic fallback behind the same `run(...)` contract.\n- **Single `NotImplementedError`**: `base.py` line 151 is the only one in the entire tree (per grep).\n- **No execution tool in this session**: The assistant explicitly noted it cannot run `pytest` or `smoke_run.py`. Verification must be static (read/audit-based).\n- **`openevolve_roadmap.md`** lives at workspace root (`/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/openevolve_roadmap.md`), NOT inside the repo. A read attempt inside the repo path failed.\n\n**Artifacts and files**\n\n| Path | Role | Status this session |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/base.py` | Adapter ABC, Bundle, Artifact, registry. Line 151 = sole `NotImplementedError`. | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/backends.py` | Real Boltz-2/Chai-1/ProteinMPNN wrappers + **Phase 2 QM engine stubs** (lazy, optional). | **Read in full.** Phase 2 markers at lines ~20, ~387. |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/gpucheck.py` | torch matmul GPU verification for ROCm. | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/cli.py` | Subcommands: demo, preflight, score, registry, gpucheck. | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/tests.py` | pytest suite (registry, base, manifest, services, preflight, report). | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/services.py` | Service facades \u2014 thin owner of Budget, pulls adapter from registry, calls `Adapter.run`. | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/manifest.py` | Run provenance + budget. Manifest = single source of truth. | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/preflight.py` | Preflight guardrails: budget estimate, seed pinning, evaluator smoke test. | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/__init__.py` | Package init; states design rules (one adapter layer, provenance first). | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/scoring.py` | T0/T1/T2 tiered scoring adapters (QED-lite, MACE, ChGNet). | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/optimize.py` | OpenEvolve-backed optimizer (real path + offline deterministic fallback). | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/structure.py` | Boltz2Adapter + Chai1Adapter (real + offline). | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/design.py` | RFdiffusion + ProteinMPNN design adapters. | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/docker/Dockerfile` | ROCm PyTorch base, HSA_GFX build arg. | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/docker/docker-run.sh` | `/dev/kfd`+`/dev/dri` GPU plumbing, arg forwarding. | Read (prior session). |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/smoke_run.py` | One-shot end-to-end smoke check (demo, score, preflight, registry, services, manifest, report). | **Read header + structure.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/README.md` | Project description; Phase 2 referenced at line 197. | **Read in full.** |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/pyproject.toml` | Project metadata: `opensciencelab 0.0.1`, Apache-2.0, Python \u22653.9. | **Read in full.** |\n| `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/openevolve_roadmap.md` | Draft v0.1 roadmap (2026-08-20). Product/phase breakdown. | Read (prior session); **NOT inside the repo**. |\n| `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/evaluators.py`, `agents/` | Phase 0 shims redirecting to `base.py`/`manifest.py`/`adapters/evaluators.py`. | Listed; not re-read. |\n\nFull repo file listing confirmed via `list_files` (recursive): includes `.gitignore`, `LICENSE`, `README.md`, all `opensciencelab/` package files, `docker/` files, `smoke_run.py`, `pyproject.toml`.\n\n**Errors and fixes**\n\n- **Typo path (recurring)**: Assistant tried `\u2026/opensciencelad` (missing `l`) three separate times across the session. Each time got `File does not exist`. Correct path is `\u2026/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/`. Self-correction each time; no user feedback needed.\n- **`openevolve_roadmap.md` wrong path**: Attempted to read it inside the repo at `\u2026/opensciencelab/openevolve_roadmap.md`; got `File does not exist`. It actually lives at `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/openevolve_roadmap.md` (workspace root).\n- **Web fetch 403**: A `web_fetch` call to an Aliyun OSS proxy URL returned HTTP 403. No retry; not critical.\n- **No execution tool**: Assistant explicitly noted it cannot run `pytest` or `smoke_run.py` in this session. Pivoted to static audit approach.\n- **User redirect (from prior session)**: Assistant had framed next step as \"git init + ROADMAP.md\"; user overrode to \"find the last code and continue the last phase.\"\n\n**All user messages**\n\n1. *[Long message presenting full repo tree]* \u2014 Described Phase 0 (contract layer) and Phase 1 (real backends + GPU runtime) with file-by-file annotations. Noted `evaluators.py` and `agents/` are thin shims. Ended with: \"Want me to add a top-level `ROADMAP.md` with the phase breakdown, or push this to a git init so it''s diffable?\"\n2. *\"find the last code implemented and begin working on the last phase which was last worked upon\"* (sic \u2014 \"lphase\" = \"last phase\")\n3. *(No further user messages in the recent turns \u2014 the assistant has been autonomously surveying.)*\n\n**Pending tasks**\n\n- **Complete Phase 2** \u2014 the last phase worked on. Concretely: audit `", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, list_files, read_file, sleep_for, todo_write, web_fetch", "user_messages": ["Here it is \u2014 everything lives in one repo root in this workspace: **`/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/`** **Phase 0 \u2014 the contract layer** (framework, no heavy deps): ``` opensciencelab/ \u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml # package config, opt-in extras \u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md LICENSE .gitignore \u251c\u2500\u2500 smoke_run.py # one-shot end-to-end check \u2514\u2500\u2500 opensciencelab/ \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py # public API (services, types, registry) \u251c\u2500\u2500 __main__.py # python -m opensciencelab \u251c\u2500\u2500 base.py # Adapter contract, Bundle, Artifact, registry \u251c\u2500\u2500 manifest.py # Manifest, Budget, seeds, RunDirectory \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py # the f\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787362255.31405, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('9f9b5444-b8e','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','let''s begin working on phase 2 of this project: /home/iconba','cowork',377,NULL,'[]',0,1,NULL,NULL,'OpenScienceLab Phase 2 Development',0,'2026-08-22 05:09:43','{}','{"boundary_index": 370, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nThe user wants to complete **Phase 2** of the OpenScienceLab project at `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/`. Phase 2 scope (README line 197): **\"real QM (PySCF tier-2, MACE on top) + real OpenEvolve loop.\"** Concretely: verify and harden the real (non-offline) backend paths for Tier 1 scoring (MACE/CHGNet), Tier 2 scoring (PySCF), and the OpenEvolve-backed real path in the optimization adapter. Phase 0 (contracts, offline adapters, demo, tests, CLI) is **[DONE]** with 26/26 tests passing.\n\n**Standing constraint:** The system is **NOT in plan mode** \u2014 `propose_plan` was rejected with `\"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\"`. All work proceeds directly to implementation. Do NOT call `propose_plan`.\n\n**2. Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- **OpenScienceLab**: open-source, locally-runnable drug-discovery/materials-science pipeline. OpenEvolve-style evolutionary search + quantum chemistry, unified via a single adapter layer with auditable provenance and budgeted compute. No cloud, no API keys. Zero-dep core (`dependencies = []`).\n- **Scoring is tiered**: Tier 0 (fast local). Tier 1 (`score.tier1.mace` / `score.tier1.chgnet`) \u2192 `energy_eV_flipped`. Tier 2 uses PySCF (HF energy in eV, `energy_eV_flipped`).\n- **Real-backend pattern** (`backends.py`): the **only place** a heavy dependency is touched. On `BackendNotAvailable`, the adapter falls back to an offline artifact / surrogate value and records the error in the manifest so a run still completes and is auditable.\n- **Surrogate fallback (BUG FOUND AND FIXED, prior session)**: In the MACE adapter (~line 214-216) and CHGNet adapter (~line 272), when `BackendNotAvailable` was raised mid-candidate-loop, `metric` was set to `None` and then `round(metric, 4)` would crash, killing the entire `_exec`. The PySCF adapter handled this correctly with a proxy fallback. **Fix applied**: both MACE and CHGNet now compute a surrogate offline value (`-0.05 * n_heavy_atoms`) and set `method` to a descriptive fallback string, matching the PySCF pattern.\n- **Tier-1/2 adapters otherwise verified correct**: `scoring.py` calls `backends.mace_energy`, `backends.chgnet_energy`, `backends.pyscf_*` with correct signatures. `_candidate_numbers_and_coords(cand)` resolves a Candidate into `(numbers, coords)` arrays.\n- **Optimization adapter** (`optimize.py`, ~849 lines): single contract `run(...) -> Bundle`. Two paths:\n  - **Real path**: `_run_openevolve` (~lines 408\u2013545) delegates to `openevolve.run_evolution`. Uses `_OPENEVOLVE_EVALUATOR_SRC` string constant for the subprocess evaluator. Config resolved via `OPENSCIENCELAB_OPENEVOLVE_CONFIG` env-var or package default.\n  - **Fallback/local path** (`_hill_climb`, ~lines 545\u2013700): island-based hill climbing, no external LLM.\n  - **`_exec` fallback guard** (~lines 360\u2013412): any real-path exception \u2192 `manifest.record_error(...)`, then falls back to hill-climbing.\n- **Helper functions in optimize.py** (discovered this session): `_candidates_from_code` (line ~299), `_list_files_rel` (line ~753), `_top_from_best_code` (line ~772), `_resolve_population` (line ~782). `_resolve_population` parses lines of code as SMILES candidates. `_top_from_best_code` builds a top-k list from a best_code string.\n- **Program materialization** (lines 290-399): `_smiles_like` checks a token for SMILES-likeness; `_candidates_from_code` extracts molecule candidates from a program string.\n- **`_openevolve_config_obj` bug \u2014 FIXED (prior session)**: Used `cfg.llm.rebuild_models()` after setting `primary_model`/`api_key` to ensure `llm.models` is populated (hard gate in OpenEvolve).\n- **OpenEvolve API** (`algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve`): `from openevolve import run_evolution`. `evaluator` accepts `str`/`Path`/`Callable`. Entry point calls `evaluate(program_path)` expecting a dict with `combined_score`. Our `_OPENEVOLVE_EVALUATOR_SRC` satisfies that contract.\n- **Environment**: Python **3.14.4** (`/usr/bin/python3`). **No venv.** ALL heavy deps MISSING (pyscf, mace.calculators, chgnet, openevolve, torch, ase, rdkit). Tests must pass with zero heavy deps.\n- **Test plan**: Write stub-injection tests that mock `backends.mace_energy`, `backends.chgnet_energy`, `backends.pyscf_*`, and `openevolve.run_evolution` to verify the real-branch wiring without the heavy deps.\n- **Base.py structure** (from this session''s reading): 242 lines total. Defines `Budget`, `Adapter.run(...)` (charges budget, stamps artifacts, records call), `Adapter._exec(...)` (abstract), `registry` dict. `Adapter.run` wraps `_exec` in try/except for `BudgetExceeded` and general exceptions.\n- **Services.py** (214 lines): `score()` facade calls `registry[\"score.tier0.rdkit\"].run(...)`, tier-1/2 similarly. `optimize()` facade calls `registry[\"optimize.openevolve\"].run(...)`. Each facade owns a `Budget` and resolves the adapter by name from the registry.\n- **Existing test patterns** (tests.py, 424 lines): `_svc(tmp_path)` helper at line 118 creates a temp workspace and returns a dict of service facades. Tests use `pytest` + `tmp_path`. 26 existing tests covering registry, budget, tier-0 scoring, design, optimize (hill-climb path), manifest, CLI.\n\n**3. Artifacts and files**\n\n| Path | Role / Status |\n|---|---|\n| `opensciencelab/README.md` | Overview, architecture, roadmap. Phase 2 at line 197. |\n| `opensciencelab/pyproject.toml` | `dependencies = []`. Optional extras line 17+. |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/backends.py` (634 lines) | Real backends: `mace_available`(545), `mace_energy`(~523), `chgnet_*`(~560\u2013590), `pyscf_*`(~590\u2013634). Defines `BackendNotAvailable`. **Verified correct.** |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/scoring.py` (409 lines) | Tiered scoring adapters. **EDITED (prior session)**: MACE fallback (~line 214) and CHGNet fallback (~line 272) fixed to use surrogate value instead of `None`. PySCF path was already correct. Tier-0 at lines 1\u2013160, MACE at ~160\u2013258, CHGNet at ~259\u2013340, PySCF at ~340\u2013409. |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/adapters/optimize.py` (~849 lines) | **TARGET FILE** (no edits yet). `_import_openevolve`(110). `_openevolve_config_obj`(~123+). `_pareto_front`(58). `_smiles_like`(~299). `_candidates_from_code`(~299+). `_OPENEVOLVE_EVALUATOR_SRC`(~191\u2013410). `_exec` fallback guard(~360\u2013412). `_run_openevolve`(~408\u2013545). `_hill_climb`(~545\u2013700). `_list_files_rel`(~753). `_top_from_best_code`(~772). `_resolve_population`(~782). Manifest construction(~700\u2013849). |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/tests.py` (424 lines) | Existing test suite. `_svc(tmp_path)` helper at line 118. 26/26 passing. **Phase 2 tests NOT YET ADDED.** |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/base.py` (242 lines) | Adapter contract, registry, `Budget`, `record_error` patterns. `Adapter.run` wraps `_exec`, charges budget, stamps artifacts on manifest. |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/services.py` (214 lines) | Service-level wrappers: `design()`, `score()`, `optimize()`. Each owns a `Budget`, resolves adapter from `registry`. |\n| `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/manifest.py` | Manifest with `record_error`, `merge_patch`, `seeds`. |\n\n**4. Errors and fixes**\n\n1. **`replace_in_file` failure (MACE adapter, first attempt, prior session)**: The `old` string in the replacement call didn''t exactly match the file content (likely whitespace or comment differences). **Fix**: Read the actual lines (199\u2013258) via `read_file_lines`, then constructed the correct `old` string and successfully applied the fix.\n2. **Latent crash bug \u2014 `round(None, 4)` in MACE/CHGNet tier-1 fallback (prior session)**: When `BackendNotAvailable` was raised mid-candidate-loop, `metric` was set to `None`, and a subsequent `round(metric, 4)` would raise `TypeError`, killing the entire `_exec`. **Fix**: Both MACE and CHGNet fallbacks now set `metric = -0.05 * n_heavy_atoms` and `method = \"surrogate-offline (MACE/CHGNet failed: <error>)\"` instead of `None`/`\"n/a\"`.\n3. **No new errors this session segment.** All actions were context-gathering reads.\n\n**5. All user messages**\n\n1. *(From prior sessions, carried in compaction)* Initial request to complete Phase 2 of OpenScienceLab.\n2. *(From prior sessions)* \"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\" (rejection of `propose_plan`).\n3. *(This segment)* No new explicit user messages \u2014 all turns are the assistant working autonomously to continue Phase 2 implementation. The user''s standing instruction remains: complete Phase 2 directly, no plan mode.\n\n**6. Pending tasks**\n\n- **Re-run the existing test suite** (`python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py -q`) after the MACE/CHGNet bug fixes to confirm 26/26 still pass.\n- **Write Phase 2 stub-injection tests** in `opensciencelab/opensciencelab/tests.py`:\n  - Mock `backends.mace_available()` \u2192 `True`, `backends.mace_energy()` \u2192 known value; verify tier-1 MACE real-branch scoring", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file_lines", "user_messages": ["let''s begin working on phase 2 of this project: /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787375327.663093, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
