INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('c0faa1cf-c41','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/metered-web-broker','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','01-gateway-build-prompt.md — the Broker.fetch orchestrator, ','builder',335,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Gateway Broker.fetch orchestrator build',0,'2026-08-27 03:40:41','{}','{"boundary_index": 253, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully trace through the \"conversation since\" section and fold in the previous compaction summary to produce a fresh, structured summary.\n\nThe conversation since covers:\n1. The assistant was working on rewriting the terminal-class invariant describe block in broker.test.ts. The em-dash in the describe header was causing exact match issues.\n2. The assistant tried various approaches (replace_in_file with various patterns, apply_unified_diff, read_file) and eventually decided to rewrite the whole test file with write_file.\n3. Before running, the assistant verified the Broker API by reading broker.ts and index.ts.\n4. The assistant discovered bugs in the test itself:\n   - `budget.byTenant` doesn''t exist \u2014 `byTenant` is on `AuditLedger`, not `BudgetEngine`. Used in 3 places (lines 85, 226, and one more).\n   - The \"charged once\" assertion should be ledger-based.\n5. The assistant added `summarize` import.\n6. The assistant fixed the assertions to use ledger.entries and summarize.\n7. The vitest.config.ts doesn''t exist at packages/gateway/vitest.config.ts (not a file). The root vitest.config.ts exists.\n8. The assistant set up todos and checked package.json scripts.\n9. `npx vitest run` failed because vitest wasn''t installed (\"Could not resolve ''vitest/config''\"). Actually the error was about vitest@4.1.11 being installed via exec but config uses vitest/config.\n10. The assistant checked node_modules \u2014 not present. Installed dependencies via npm install.\n11. After install, ran tests again. Now two source-level compile errors:\n    - Duplicate member \"policy\" in BudgetEngine class body (budget/src/engine.ts) \u2014 `this.policy = ...` and `get policy()` collide.\n    - A second error in rails/src/rails.ts (lines 188-207 shown).\n12. The assistant diagnosed:\n    - BudgetEngine: private field `policy` collides with getter `get policy()` \u2014 rename field to `_policy`.\n    - RailRegistry: `get optional(id: string)` \u2014 a getter can''t take params \u2014 convert to method `optional(id: string)`.\n13. The assistant fixed:\n    - budget/src/engine.ts: replaced `this.policy` with `this._policy` and `private readonly policy:` with `private readonly _policy:`.\n    - rails/src/rails.ts: converted `get optional(id: string): PaymentRail` to method `optional(id: string): PaymentRail | undefined`.\n14. Then fixed `defaultPolicy(clock)` \u2192 `defaultPolicy` in the test (4 places) because `defaultPolicy` is a frozen constant object, not a function.\n15. Ran tests from repo root: 5 pass, 8 fail.\n16. The failures point to real broker source bugs. The most recent shown failure is at lines 202-206 (a fulfilled test), and another at line 212-213.\n17. The assistant read broker.ts run method (lines 126-222) to sort out test bugs vs source bugs.\n\nLet me capture the key code revealed:\n\nFrom index.ts:\n```\nexport {\n  Broker,\n  type OriginClient,\n  type OriginResponse,\n  type BrokerOptions,\n  type BrokerIdentityOptions,\n  type TerminalKind,\n} from ''./broker.js'';\n```\n\nFrom broker.ts imports (lines 1-120):\n- BudgetError, HeaderRecord, IdentityError, PaymentRequiredError, RailError, isBrokerError, makeFetchId, systemClock, Clock, FetchOutcome, FailureClass, PaymentRail, etc.\n\nbroker.ts fetch signature (lines 126-133):\n```\nasync fetch(params: {\n  url: UrlString;\n  fetchId?: string;\n  headers?: HeaderRecord;\n  tenantId?: string;\n  rand?: () => number;\n}): Promise<FetchOutcome> {\n  const fetchId = params.fetchId ?? makeFetchId(params.rand);\n  const exi\u2026\n```\n\nSo `fetch` uses `params.fetchId ?? makeFetchId(params.rand)`.\n\nOriginDenied signature (from earlier, lines 298-304):\n```\nprivate originDenied(\n  fetchId: string,\n  tenantId: string,\n  url: string,\n  httpStatus: number,\n  identityPresent: boolean\n): FetchOutcome {\n  let failureClass: FailureClass;\n  let message: string;\n  let code: string;\n  \u2026\n```\n\nBudgetEngine (budget/src/engine.ts):\n- Line 89: `private readonly _policy: BudgetPolicy;` (after fix, was `policy`)\n- Line 93: `this._policy = options?.policy ?? defaultPolicy;` (after fix)\n- get policy(): BudgetPolicy { return this._policy; }\n- There''s a currency check around lines 112-114: `if (price.currency !== this._policy.currency) { ... Tenant currency mismatch ... }`\n\nInMemoryRail (rails/src/rails.ts):\n- Line 28: `export class InMemoryRail implements PaymentRail {`\n- Line 29: `readonly id: string;`\n- Line 30: `private readonly settlementSeed: string = '''';`\n- Line 31: `private readonly failureMode: ''none'' | ''quote'' | ''authorize'' | ''settle'';`\n- Line 33-34: constructor(options: { id: string; priceMicros: ... })\n\nRailRegistry:\n- Line 165: `settle(req: PaymentRequest, authorization: RailAuthorization): Promise<RailSettlement> {`\n- `get(id: string)`, `optional(id: string)` (now method), `ids()`\n- `optional` now: `optional(id: string): PaymentRail | undefined { return this.rails.get(id); }`\n\nAuditLedger (audit/src/ledger.ts):\n- Line 59: `byTenant(tenantId: string): LedgerEntry[]`\n- Uses `ledger.entries`, `reconcile`, `summarize`.\n- LedgerEntry fields include: priceMicros, currency, rail, licenseId, keyId, settlementRef, startedAt, etc.\n\nbudget/src/policy.ts:\n- defaultPolicy is a frozen constant object with fields perCallCeilingMicros, hourlyTenantCeilingMicros, dailyTenantCeilingMicros, etc.\n- `defaultPolicy` is NOT a function taking (clock).\n\nNow the failing tests. The assistant saw 5 pass, 8 fail. The failures shown:\n- `Broker.fetch \u2014 fulfilled > charges the meter once, records exactly one row, and reconciles` (FAILED)\n- `Broker.fetch \u2014 fulfilled > records identity on a...` \n- Failure at line 202-206 (broker construction), another at 212-213.\n\nThe assistant was reading the run method (lines 126-222) to sort out test bugs vs real source bugs. This is where the conversation ended \u2014 mid-analysis of the run method.\n\nLet me capture the todos:\n1. Rewrite terminal-class invariant describe block in broker.test.ts \u2014 done\n2. Verify test matches the real Broker/budget/rails/audit APIs \u2014 done\n3. Run the gateway test suite and make it green \u2014 in_progress\n4. Record final broker test notes in phase file \u2014 pending\n\nThe workspace/root: `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker`\n\nThe plan file: `metered-web-broker-build-plan.md` was mentioned in grep output. Actually the path was `metered-web-broker-build-plan.md` \u2014 let me note it''s a plan/build plan markdown. The prior summary referenced \"phase file\". Let me note it generically as the build-plan markdown.\n\nNow let me write the structured summary.\n\nFor the \"Errors and fixes\" section, list:\n1. Terminal-class invariant describe block \u2014 replace_in_file failing due to em-dash in header. Fixed by rewriting whole file via write_file, then targeted replacements.\n2. `budget.byTenant` \u2014 doesn''t exist; byTenant is on AuditLedger. Fixed test to use ledger.entries and summarize.\n3. defaultPolicy(clock) \u2014 defaultPolicy is a frozen constant object, not a function. Fixed by removing (clock) arg in 4 places.\n4. Duplicate member \"policy\" in BudgetEngine \u2014 private field `policy` collided with getter `get policy()`. Fixed by renaming field to `_policy` (sed).\n5. `get optional(id: string)` in RailRegistry \u2014 getter can''t take params. Fixed by converting to method `optional(id: string)`.\n\nCurrent work: Reading