s a lot of content, and I need to figure out what actually happened (the real actions) versus what the model was reasoning about.\n\nLet me look at the tool results more carefully. The \"conversation since\" appears to contain actual tool result outputs. Let me identify the real events:\n\nFrom the reasoning, the model identified:\n1. A determinism bug: pack() scans agent_dir with rglob(\"*\") and re-ingests its own previously-written .bundle output, so repeated packing is non-deterministic when output is inside the tree.\n2. Fix: exclude the output path in _scan_and_hash, then by basename, then by suffix (.bundle).\n3. validator.py: extract bug with files/ prefix\n4. schema.py: canonical_json_without_sign bug\n\nBut actually, I''m now confused about what''s real. The task says \"Write a structured summary of the conversation below.\" The \"conversation\" is what''s shown. But the content shows a model that was reasoning extensively without emitting answers.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. I think what''s happening here is:\n\nThe previous compaction was done by a model (\"dcode-proxy\") that ran out of budget. Its reasoning is preserved. Then the actual conversation tools continued. The content I''m seeing includes:\n- The previous summary''s content\n- The previous model''s reasoning\n- Subsequent tool results (the actual work that was done)\n\nActually, I realize the structure might be that the entire thing from the previous summary through the tool results is the \"conversation below\" that I need to summarize, and I need to fold in the previous summary''s still-relevant content.\n\nWait, no. Let me re-read the very first line: \"Produce ALL of the following sections... 1. Primary request...\"\n\nAnd before that: \"[previous compaction summary \u2014 fold its still-relevant content into the new summary]\"\n\nSo the previous compaction summary is the block that starts with \"Let me carefully reconstruct...\" \u2014 no wait, that''s the reasoning.\n\nOK here''s my best understanding:\n- The PREVIOUS compaction summary is what I''m told to fold in. It''s the content ending with \"...Let me figure out the current state.\"\n- The reasoning block (\"Let me carefully reconstruct the conversation...\") is the dcode-proxy''s reasoning that never produced an answer.\n- The content after that (the tool calls) is the \"conversation since\" \u2014 actual work done.\n\nActually, I think I''m overcomplicating this. Let me just treat everything as the context and produce a good 8-section summary based on the ACTUAL work that was done, as evidenced by the tool results.\n\nThe key realization: I have detailed tool results showing what was actually done. Let me extract the concrete facts:\n\nREAL ACTIONS (from tool results):\n1. validator.py is 334 lines, had unused imports gzip, io, and redundant bundle param\n2. Wrote smoke test, found all files \"absent\" and signature fails\n3. Fixed _extract to strip files/ prefix\n4. Removed gzip, io dead imports\n5. canonical_json_without_sign bug in schema.py \u2014 sets dumped[\"sign\"]=None on local dict but serializes self.with_deterministic_order().model_dump() instead, so sign not nulled\n6. Fixed canonical_json_without_sign\n7. Test harness bugs with tarfile in Python 3.12 (no tardata attribute)\n8. build_bundle treats dict values as bytes but they''re functions \u2014 fixed to apply as functions\n9. tar-rebuild harness produces malformed archives \u2014 fixed to rewrite ti.size\n10. signature failure cases correctly reject\n11. _check_signature bundle param unused \u2014 removed\n12. \"manifest has no signature block\" error added twice \u2014 removed redundant duplicate check\n\nThen there''s the bigger chunk which is the DETERMINISM BUG investigation and fix:\n\n13. Determinism test failure at index 11\n14. Investigation: pack() scans agent_dir with rglob(\"*\") and re-ingests its own output\n15. First fix: exclude current output path\n16. Still failing (out_a different name still ingested)\n17. Fix: exclude by basename\n18. Still failing\n19. Final fix: exclude by suffix (.bundle) \u2014 exclude in _scan_and_hash\n20. Determinism fixed\n21. Two remaining failures: manifest.json missing in _extract\n22. Fix: extract bug \u2014 files/ prefix handling\n\nWait, I need to be careful about what actually got fixed vs what was being considered. Let me look at the actual final tool results.\n\nThe last several tool results show:\n- validator.py content (160-219, 120-164, 86-131)\n- The model was investigating verify() raising VerifyError vs returning result.valid=False\n- Failure: verify() raises VerifyError instead of returning result.valid=False when manifest is corrupt\n- \"The real bug is at line 131: _extract(raw) is outside the try block, so a corrupt manifest propagates a VerifyError instead of being collected into errors\"\n\nSo the CURRENT state (what''s in progress) is:\n- Investigating verify() at line 131 \u2014 _extract(raw) is outside the try block\n- Need to fix verify() to catch _extract errors and collect into errors list instead of raising\n\nLet me also note the very last tool result:\n```\n[assistant \u2192 read_file] {\"path\": \"src/agpack/artifact/validator.py\", \"start_line\": 86, \"end_line\": 131, \"total_lines\": 329, \"content\": \" 86\\t f\\\"signature_ok={self.signature_ok}, errors={self.errors!r})\\\"\\n 87\\t )\\n 88\\t\\n 89\\t\\n 90\\tdef verify(\\n 91\\t bundle: object,\\n 92\\t *,\\n 93\\t max_cap_scopes: Optional[set[str]] = None,\\n 94\\t) -> VerifyResult:\\n 95\\t \\\"\\\"\\\"Verify a bundle *without executing anything* (\\u00a7R)\u2026\n```\n\nSo validator.py is now 329 lines (was 334 \u2014 wait, it changed). Actually earlier it said 334, then 329. Hmm. The line count changed because fixes were applied. Let me note it''s around 329 lines.\n\nWait, the reasoning said 334 lines multiple times. But the final read shows 329 lines. And in the middle, there were edits. Let me not over-index on exact line counts but note the file is ~329 lines.\n\nOK so now let me understand the FINAL state properly:\n\nThe determinism bug was fixed in packager.py (_scan_and_hash now excludes by .bundle suffix).\nDeterminism test now passes (11 passed).\nTwo failures remained: test_tampered_manifest_is_rejected and test_signature_survives_recompression, both hitting \"manifest.json missing\" in _extract.\n\nWait, but then later it says determinism is fixed and two failures remain, both hitting manifest.json missing. And then the model examined _extract and the tests.\n\nThen the final investigation is about verify() at line 131: _extract(raw) is outside the try block.\n\nHmm, but \"manifest.json missing\" in _extract \u2014 let me think. The failure is that verify() raises VerifyError instead of returning result.valid=False. The model found that _extract is outside the try block at line 131, so a corrupt manifest (missing manifest.json or unparseable) propagates VerifyError rather than being collected into errors.\n\nSo the CURRENT in-progress work is fixing verify() to move _extract into the try block (or wrap it) so that manifest corruption is collected as errors.\n\nLet me now also reconcile the two \"manifest.json missing\" failures with the verify() raising issue. Actually, I think these are the same root cause: when a test builds a malformed archive (rebuild harness), _extract fails with \"manifest.json missing\" or similar, and because _extract is outside the try block, it raises instead of being collected.\n\nActually wait. Let me re-read: \"Two real issues. Failure 1: verify() raises VerifyError instead of returning result.valid=False when the manifest is corrupt. Failure 2: the test''s rebuild harness produces a malformed archive.\"\n\nSo:\n- Failure 1: verify() should collect _extract errors into errors, not raise. This is the validator bug at line 131.\n- Failure 2: test''s rebuild harness produces malformed archives. This is a TEST harness bug (test-side), where the rebuilt archive is malformed.\n\nAnd then: \"The real bug is at line 131: _extract(raw) is outside the try block, so a corrupt manifest propagates a VerifyError instead of being collected into errors.\"\n\nSo the fix in progress is: move _extract into the try block in verify().\n\nLet me now also figure out: what about the test harness for rebuild producing malformed archives? The model said \"Failure 2: the test''s rebuild harness produces a malformed archive.\" This suggests the test needs fixing too (rewrite ti.size etc.), but actually earlier in the summary it said the harness was already fixed to rewrite ti.size. Hmm.\n\nLet me focus on the concrete end state and current work.\n\nActually, I realize I should be careful. The content is a mix of:\n1. Reasoning (not necessarily actioned)\n2. Actual tool results (the real actions)\n\nThe tool results that matter are the actual shell/test runs and file edits. Let me enumerate the file edits (replace_in_file) that are shown:\n\n1. schema.py canonical_json_without_sign fix (mentioned, \"Fixed canonical_json_without_sign()\")\n2. validator.py: removed unused bundle param from _check_signature\n3. validator.py: removed redundant duplicate \"no signature block\" check\n4. tests/test_artifact_bundle.py: multiple fixes\n   - POLICY_YAML/MAX_CAP_YAML: tool_scopes \u2192 scopes\n   - Fix over-cap test corrupt policy body\n   - Determinism test: freeze clock\n   - Determinism test: add debug, then restore\n   - packager.py: _scan_and_hash signature and exclusion\n   - packager.py: pack() pass output to _scan_and_hash\n   - packager.py: exclude by basename\n   - packager.py: exclude by suffix\n   - validator.py: verify() fix (in progress at line", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest tests/_dbg_det.py -s -q 2>&1 | tail -25  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && cp tests/test_artifact_bundle.py /tmp/_bak.py && python3 - << ''PYEOF'' p=\"tests/test_artifact_bundle.py\" s=open(p)  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest \"tests/test_artifact_bundle.py::test_deterministic_bytes_within_second\" -s -q 2>&1 | grep -E \"C  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python3 << ''PYEOF'' import gzip, io, tarfile from pathlib import Path from agpack.artifact import p  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest \"tests/test_artifact_bundle.py::test_deterministic_bytes_within_second\" -s -q 2>&1 | grep -E \"C  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && rm -f tests/_dbg_det.py && python3 -m pytest tests/test_artifact_bundle.py -v 2>&1 | tail -20  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest \"tests/test_artifact_bundle.py::test_deterministic_bytes_within_second\" -s -q 2>&1 | grep -E \"L  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest tests/test_artifact_bundle.py -v 2>&1 | tail -20  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest tests/test_artifact_bundle.py -v 2>&1 | grep -E \"PASSED|FAILED\" | head -30  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python3 -m pytest \"tests/test_artifact_bundle.py::test_tampered_manifest_is_rejected\" \"tests/test_artifact_bundle  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: explore, grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell", "user_messages": ["You are the lead engineer starting the `agpack` project (open-source, portable, verifiable agent runtime). The repo is currently at SCAFFOLD ONLY: every Python module is a stub whose docstrings/comments define the intended surface and no real implementation exists yet. Work inside the existing layout and keep every module a stub until told otherwise \u2014 we are establishing the skeleton, conventions, and test harness first, filling in behavior next. ## The project (from README.md) - A neutral runtime that loads an agent as ONE MOVABLE ARTIFACT: code, system prompt, tool manifest, memory contract\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787835883.3738508, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
