n\nThe user hasn''t chosen. So the immediate next step is for the user to decide which thread to move.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user asked \"what is next to do?\" twice. The first time, the assistant gave the pyproject deps fix + pytest run, which the user did. The second time, the assistant re-read the next-steps prompts and offered options. The user''s last message is \"what is next to do?\" and the assistant responded with the options but no choice was made.\n\nSo the current state: verification is complete, the deps are declared, pytest is 203 passed. The next step is undecided \u2014 the user needs to pick a work stream.\n\nLet me also note the outstanding offer: \"a fresh-virtualenv pip install . + re-run to prove a clean install.\" The assistant offered this but it''s not clearly been requested.\n\nLet me now think about what I should capture for the \"pending tasks\":\n- Optional: fresh venv pip install . + re-run (offered, not confirmed)\n- Decision needed: which work stream to move into (agpack continuation vs metered-web-broker vs drug-discovery)\n- The metered-web-broker: \"Prove it before writing code. The repo is read-only \u2014 you cannot run npm inside it.\"\n\nLet me structure the summary.\n\nNow, one thing to verify: the count breakdown. Let me recheck:\n- trust_audit = 29\n- trust_delegation = 29\n- trust_signing = 24\n- sandbox_limits = 30 (22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3) \u2014 wait, 22 + 3\u00d73 = 22+9 = 31, but they wrote 30. Let me re-read: \"test_sandbox_limits.py = 30 (22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3)\". Hmm 22+9=31. But the total said 30. Actually the assistant wrote \"22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3\" but then 29+29+24 + 30+25+28+25 + 13. Let me just use 30 as the reported number. Actually there''s a discrepancy in my note, but the reported count for test_sandbox_limits.py is 30. I''ll note 30.\n\nActually, let me recompute the total: 29+29+24 = 82. 30+25+28+25 = 108. 82+108+13 = 203. Yes, 203. Good.\n\nWait, sandbox is 30+25+28+25 = 108. And earlier the \"34\" in the brain_note was \"sandbox = limits 34", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/1472646f-019/verify_agpack_tests.md\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_note, grep, list_files, read_file, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["Let''s go over what was built from the last builder session for the agpack project", "what should be the next prompt to continue the work which was done to progress the project?", "review the last session done on this project in the builder persona", "review the latest work done", "What is next to do in this project?", "create the prompt for what should be done next", "What is left to do in this project? : Done. Phase complete. ## Summary The sandbox suite is **fully implemented and green: 108 tests, all passing**. **This session''s work:** - **`test_sandbox_host.py`** \u2014 was 14 tests; grew to **25** by adding 11 gate-reject tests exercising the new `limits.check()` meter gate (the core deliverable): - Reject on fuel / memory / wall-time overruns \u2192 `FuelExhausted` / `MemoryExhausted` / `Timeout` - The host captures the `LimitError` and returns it on `RunResult.limit` instead of propagating - The wall-clock-kill-while-fuel-within-budget case sets `fuel_meter_b\u2026", "Create a prompt on the next task needed to get done", "It seemed the builder session reached its max iterations. Did it finish the work?", "give me a prompt to check. then also add if it''s not done what to do and if it is what to do next", "Check the work of the last session. I believe it worked on branch A. See if the next task is branch b: Next-steps prompt: metered-web-broker-next-steps-prompt.md Four priorities, sequenced so the load-bearing work comes first: P1 \u2014 wire ONE real 402 \u2192 settle \u2192 200 round-trip. The bearing thesis. Verify a real metered origin (don''t assume x402 names), read the PaymentRail seam, implement a spec-agnostic rail, add replay/nonce guards, and prove the loop on real bytes. P2 \u2014 add the finality flag, in the same pass. test/claimed \u2192 conditional outcome; only reconcile().ok === true \u2192 true fulfilled.\u2026", "Done. The full test suite is green: **203 passed** (was 10 failed / 72 passed on import). **What I fixed this session:** *Delegation suite* (`src/agpack/trust/delegation.py` + test): - Removed the redundant `isinstance(token.scope, Scope)` step in the Scope gate so the real \"closed set\" check fires \u2014 a bare string scope is now refused as intended. - Fixed 3 chain test-setup bugs (root-at-tail triggering the wrong check, and a non-cycle token_id setup). *Audit suite* (`src/agpack/trust/audit.py` + test): - `validate()` now names the offending field + kind in its error message (added `_detail_b\u2026", "Check the last session to see if the work got done", "What is next to do?", "Done. Both parts verified. **Manifest fixed** \u2014 `[project.dependencies]` in `pyproject.toml` now declares the three runtime deps the code actually uses: ```toml dependencies = [ \"pydantic>=2\", # bundle schema + policy model validation (validator, schema) \"cryptography>=42\", # Ed25519 signing of bundle manifests (trust layer) \"PyYAML>=6\", # policy-component verification (validator._check_within_max_cap) ] ``` - I confirmed by grep that `pydantic` and `yaml` are the only external runtime imports at module load (`artifact/validator.py:35`, `artifact/packager.py:59`, `artifact/schema.py:54`), so \u2026", "what is next to do?"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787965013.5870225, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
