ss?: FailureClass;\n86\\t reason: string;\n87\\t origin?: {\u2026\n```\n\nWait, that was the FIRST read (earlier in the previous summary). But that read showed `status: FetchStatus` and `failureClass?`. Hmm, but the comment says \"Present iff status !== ''fulfilled''\". \n\nThen in this session, the assistant said: \"outcome.status is ''fulfilled'' | ''denied'' | ''error'', and the terminal class lives in outcome.failureClass\". So FetchStatus = ''fulfilled'' | ''denied'' | ''error''.\n\nWait, but that contradicts \"Present iff status !== ''fulfilled''\". If status is fulfilled/denied/error, then failureClass present iff status is ''denied'' or ''error'', not ''fulfilled''. The comment might be slightly off, or I''m misreading. Anyway, the key decision: map responses using `failureClass` (terminal class), not a `status` value of ''payment-required'' etc.\n\nAlso:\n- `defaultPolicy` from `@mwb/budget` \u2014 has `currency` field (used in builder: `currency: defaultPolicy.currency`). No `perCallCeilingMicros` on defaultPolicy directly \u2014 the per-call ceiling is passed as an option.\n- `BudgetEngine` constructor takes options including `perCallCeilingMicros`? Actually the builder passes per-call ceiling. Let me note: `defaultPolicy` is spread then override `perCallCeilingMicros`.\n\nActually, from an earlier read: `grep defaultPolicy fields \u2192 perCallCeilingMicros currency budget spendLimit`. So defaultPolicy might have these as defaults but they''re overridable. The builder spreads `defaultPolicy` and overrides `perCallCeilingMicros`.\n\n- `AuditLedger` has `toRows()` method (not `rows()`), `record(...)`. Exports: `reconcile, summarize, renderDashboard`.\n- `MeteredOrigin implements OriginClient` \u2014 `fetch(req: PaymentRequest) -> Promise<OriginResponse>`. OriginResponse: `{ httpStatus, headers, body }` from the self-origin `fetch`. Actually in MeteredOrigin.fetch: returns `{ httpStatus: res.status, headers: headerRecord(res), body: await res.text() }`.\n- `UrlString` branded via `url()` from `@mwb/core` (exported as `url`).\n- `HeaderRecord` type.\n\nLet me also note the broker.fetch price mechanism: price 0 vs 5000. The `InMemoryRail` settlementSeed defaults ''self''. The broker preflight. These were", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- packages/gateway/src/server.ts\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker echo \"=== FetchStatus / FailureClass ===\"; grep -nE \"type FetchStatus|FetchStatus =|type FailureClass|Fa  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker echo \"=== rails index exports ===\"; cat packages/rails/src/index.ts echo; echo \"=== does core re-export   [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker echo \"=== core index full ===\"; sed -n ''1,40p'' packages/core/src/index.ts echo \"=== how broker imports P  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker echo \"=== broker constructor signature ===\"; grep -nE \"constructor|interface BrokerOptions|identity|orig  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker echo \"=== FetchOutcome type ===\"; grep -nE \"FetchOutcome|fetchId|status|failureClass|quote|price|body|te  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker npx tsc -p packages/gateway/tsconfig.json --noEmit 2>&1 | head -40 echo \"TYPECHECK_EXIT=${PIPESTATUS[0]}  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker npx tsc -p packages/gateway/tsconfig.json --noEmit 2>&1 | head -40 echo \"TYPECHECK_EXIT=${PIPESTATUS[0]}  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker grep -nE \"url\\(|UrlString|export (class|function|type|interface|const)\" packages/core/src/index.ts | hea  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker grep -nE \"url\\(|function url|UrlString|export type UrlString|export const url|export function url\" packa  [ok]\n- cd