fetch origin: extracts host-only (url.split(\"://\",1)[-1].split(\"/\",1)[0]), compares against origins param\n- audit record: subject=short verb (e.g. \"net.fetch\"), detail[\"scope\"]=full name (e.g. \"agpack/net.fetch\"), detail[\"fuel_delta\"]=int\n- `FakeLedger` exists in tests\n- `_policy_for(*names, **params)` builds policy; params are spread as top-level keys; `from_raw` reads raw.get(\"origins\") etc.\n- net.fetch allowed origins are host-only\n\nNow let me think about what''s the actual current state precisely. The last few commands:\n- `replace_in_file` on test_sandbox_imports.py replaced `test_all_scopes_have_the_expected_fuel_table` \u2014 but the content I replaced it with was \"incoherent\" per my own note\n- Then I ran two python -c inspection commands\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the last `replace_in_file` changed the test to key on `detail[\"scope\"]`. Then I ran inspection commands to verify. The output got cut off.\n\nSo the current work is: finalizing the new tests in test_sandbox_imports.py, specifically getting `test_all_scopes_have_the_expected_fuel_table` right, and cleaning up the garbled `test_fuel_meter_buggy_wall_time_flag_is_not_on_import_call`.\n\nLet me think about the pending work:\n- Fix remaining test_sandbox_imports.py tests to get 25+ passing\n- Then test_sandbox_host.py to 25+\n- Then README update\n- Then final verification run\n\nLet me also note: the DoD requires 25+ tests each for imports and host. Currently imports=20, host=14. Need to add 5+ to imports, 11+ to host.\n\nAlso I should check: the `test_fuel_meter_buggy_wall_time_flag_is_not_on_import_call` test is garbled/incoherent and needs rewriting. And I need to make sure I don''t have the \"removal\" issue where replacing accidentally removed `test_successful_call_records_scope_and_resource`.\n\nWait, there''s a note: \"I accidentally removed the `test_successful_call_records_scope_and_resource` test when replacing.\" So I need to watch for that \u2014 it may need to be restored.\n\nLet me reconstruct the current file state of test_sandbox_imports.py. Originally 298 lines, 20 tests. I appended ~8 tests. Then several edits/replacements happened. The current line count was 441 at one point.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The task is to write a compaction summary, not to continue the work. But I need to capture the state accurately so the coworker can continue.\n\nLet me be precise about what I know vs. what I need to verify by re-reading.\n\nState of test_sandbox_imports.py:\n- Was 298 lines, 20 tests\n- I appended ~8 tests to get toward 25+\n- Multiple edits to fix fuel_delta values and origins\n- One test (test_all_scopes_have_the_expected_fuel_table) is currently being debugged\n- One test (test_fuel_meter_buggy_wall_time_flag_is_not_on_import_call) is garbled\n- Concern: test_successful_call_records_scope_and_resource may have been accidentally removed\n\nI should note the coworker needs to re-read test_sandbox_imports.py to get its true current state, because the edits have been messy.\n\nFor host.py, the wiring is done. Let me confirm the current state \u2014 the last verification of host.py edits was \"My edits are done; the suite passed.\" Actually the 64 passed run was BEFORE I added tests, and included host/limits/imports. Wait no \u2014 let me recheck order.\n\nOrder of events:\n1. Read README\n2. Plan rejected\n3. Set todos\n4. Multiple replace_in_file on host.py (wiring limits.check)\n5. `pytest ... host limits imports` \u2192 64 passed\n6. Per-file counts: host 14, imports 20, limits 30, capabilities 25 = 89\n7. Read test_sandbox_imports.py\n8. read_file imports.py fuel table\n9. sed net_fetch\n10. sed build_imports\n11. read limits.py exports\n12. read host.py dispatch\n13. read limits.py check gate\n14. grep _died_on\n15. read host.py _died_on\n16. read imports.py memory/random/emit\n17. replace test_sandbox_imports.py (append ~8 tests)\n18. replace test (fuel_meter_buggy wall) \u2014 nonsensical\n19. replac