INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('2ba12f01-eb4','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/agpack','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','agpack-prompt-step3.md in the primary scratch directory.','builder',336,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Trust Layer Builder Prompt Review',0,'2026-08-28 18:55:27','{}','{"boundary_index": 211, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me analyze this conversation carefully. This is a continuation of a compaction process for an AI coworker working on the `agpack` project, specifically the \"Trust Layer\" (Phase 3).\n\nThere''s a previous compaction summary, and a \"conversation since\" section. I need to fold the still-relevant content from the previous summary into the new summary.\n\nLet me trace through what happened:\n\n**Context from previous summary (folded in):**\n- Project: `agpack` \u2014 \"Portable, verifiable agent runtime with a secure WASM tool sandbox.\"\n- Working on Step 3 \"Trust Layer\"\n- Three modules to implement: `audit.py`, `signing.py`, `delegation.py`\n- These were stubs that raised NotImplementedError\n- Constraints: build on actual source, don''t invent APIs, don''t claim green without real test run\n\n**New actions since last compaction:**\n\n1. Fixed imports in delegation.py \u2014 changed `from sandbox.capabilities import` to `from agpack.sandbox.capabilities import` (and limits). The convention is `from agpack.sandbox.*`, not bare `sandbox`.\n\n2. Fixed `_scope_in_closed_set` bug \u2014 `Scope` is a str-backed Enum, so `isinstance(scope, str)` matches everything. Fixed by checking valid cases.\n\n3. Fixed `_namespace_of` bug (dot name not in scope in error branch) and f-string nested quotes bug in `_validate_resource`.\n\n4. `ChainHop` doesn''t have `.replace()` method \u2014 `replace` is a standalone function in dataclasses, not an auto-generated method. Used `replace()` standalone function correctly.\n\n5. Confirmed all three modules work via smoke tests.\n\n6. Updated todos \u2014 all 6 done:\n   - Write Phase notes file\n   - Implement audit.py\n   - Implement signing.py\n   - Implement delegation.py\n   - (presumably write tests)\n   - (presumably run tests)\n\n7. Listed files:\n   - `src/agpack/trust/`: `__init__.py`, `_phase3.md`, `audit.py`, `delegation.py`, `signing.py`\n   - `tests/`: `__init__.py`, `test_artifact_bundle.py`, `test_sandbox_capabilities.py`, `test_sandbox_host.py`, `test_sandbox_imports.py`, `test_sandbox_limits.py`\n\n8. No test file for trust modules existed yet.\n\n9. Read phase file `_phase3.md`.\n\n10. Confirmed `cryptography` is NOT a dependency (commented out), added it to pyproject.toml dependencies.\n\n11. Confirmed `schema.py` uses pydantic (already used), pydantic 2.13.4 installed.\n\n12. Wrote `tests/test_trust_signing.py`.\n\n13. Wrote `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 had to rewrite the whole file because disk content didn''t match intended content (there was some broken/verbose helper code, and the file ended up at 391 lines).\n\nLet me look more carefully at the delegation.py details. The file is 483-486 lines. Key elements:\n- `ChainHop` dataclass with fields `sig`, and references to `iss`, `sub`, `scope`, `resource`, `budget`, `expires`, `max_scopes`, `capabilities`\n- `MAX_SCOPES = 1`\n- `SCHEME_ED25519 = \"ed25519\"`\n- `_scope_in_closed_set(scope)` \u2014 validates scope is in closed set\n- `_hop_canonical` \u2014 used in smoke test import\n- `_validate_resource`\n- `_namespace_of`\n- 8-step verify (from previous summary)\n\nFrom the tests written:\n- `ChainHop` has `sig` field\n- Functions: `verify`, `DelegationViolation`, `_hop_canonical`, `_base_sub_hop`, `_valid_token`, `_base_root_hop`\n- `token_id` matching for chain line tail\n- Test helpers: `_KEYS`, `_NOW`\n\nLet me extract the public API for tests. From delegation test:\n- `verify(tok, logical_now_unix=_NOW, keys=_KEYS)` \n- `DelegationViolation`\n- `_hop_canonical` imported\n\nNow, the key question: what is the CURRENT WORK state?\n\nThe very last action was:\n```\n[assistant \u2192 write_file] {\"path\": \"tests/test_trust_delegation.py\", \"content\": \"...\"}\n[tool result] tests/test_trust_delegation.py\n```\n\nAnd there was a `[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer.]` note at the top.\n\nSo the current work is: the assistant just finished writing `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`. It also wrote `tests/test_trust_signing.py`. It was mid-way through writing test files. Presumably it needs to write `tests/test_trust_audit.py` next, then run all tests.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The assistant wrote:\n- `tests/test_trust_signing.py` (complete, 391 lines? No wait)\n- `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`\n\nActually let me re-check. In the conversation:\n- First `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_signing.py` \u2014 content shown\n- Then `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 content shown but then \"The disk file doesn''t match what I intended \u2014 it''s a different (broken) version. Let me just rewrite the entire file cleanly\"\n- Then another `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`\n\nSo `tests/test_trust_signing.py` is done, and `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` was just rewritten cleanly (last action).\n\nThe `test_trust_delegation.py` ended up 391 lines based on the read_file showing total_lines: 391. Wait, but that read happened BEFORE the final rewrite. Let me re-check the order:\n\n1. `[assistant \u2192 write_file] tests/test_trust_delegation.py` (first attempt)\n2. `[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file]` \u2014 \"I left some broken/verbose helper code... Let me clean up\" \u2014 ERROR: \"Expected 1 replacement(s), found 0\"\n3. `[assistant \u2192 read_file]` start_line 255 max 25 \u2014 shows 391 total lines\n4. `[assistant \u2192 write_file] tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 \"The disk file doesn''t