vention: `from agpack.sandbox.*` NOT bare `sandbox`\n2. `Scope` is str-backed Enum \u2014 `isinstance(scope, str)` matches everything (bug in `_scope_in_closed_set`)\n3. `replace` is standalone function in dataclasses, not `.replace()` method\n4. `_validate_resource` f-string nested quotes bug\n5. `_namespace_of` dot-name-in-error-branch bug\n6. cryptography was a commented-out dependency, now added\n\n**Constraints from previous summary (folded in):**\n- Build on actual source\n- Don''t invent APIs\n- Don''t claim green without a real test run\n- Scratch directory OUTSIDE granted scope \u2014 agpack-prompt-step3.md couldn''t be read; grounded work on source\n\nLet me now think about the test requirements. The previous summary said \"25+ tests each, all green\". Let me check \u2014 did I verify that? The signing test was written but was it run? The delegation test was rewritten. Neither has been run via pytest yet in this conversation. So the tests are written but NOT confirmed green.\n\nActually, let me re-read. There''s no pytest run in the conversation since. The smoke tests used inline `python -c` commands, not pytest. So the actual test files (test_trust_signing.py, test_trust_delegation.py) have NOT been run yet. And test_trust_audit.py doesn''t exist yet.\n\nSo pending tasks:\n- Write `tests/test_trust_audit.py`\n- Run all 3 test files with pytest\n- Confirm all green\n\nLet me structure the summary now.\n\nActually, I need to be careful about the [dcode-proxy] note at the top. It says \"the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.\" This is a meta-note about a previous failure. It''s not really part of the working content, but I should note it as context \u2014 it indicates there was a prior turn where the model ran out of budget. This isn''t really load-bearing for continuing the work, but it''s context about session health. I''ll leave it out or note it briefly. Actually, it''s an error/issue note. But it''s about the proxy layer, not the agpack work. I''ll skip it as it''s not relevant to the task continuation \u2014 or I could note it. Given the instruction to \"preserve everything load-bearing,\" and this is about the session budget, it''s arguably not load-bearing for the agpack task. I''ll omit it to keep focus, or mention it minimally. I''ll omit it since it''s infra noise.\n\nLet me also reconsider the test file line counts. The signing test \u2014 I don''t have a read of it, so I don''t know its line count. The delegation test was 391 lines (before final rewrite) and then rewritten. The final rewrite content wasn''t shown in full.\n\nNow let me write concrete, load-bearing content.\n\nLet me structure:\n\n1. Primary request and intent\n2. Key concepts and decisions\n3. Artifacts and files\n4. Errors and fixes\n5. All user messages\n6. Pending tasks\n7. Current work\n8. Next step\n\nFor user messages \u2014 in this conversation, there are NO explicit user messages visible. The \"[assistant \u2192 ...]\" and \"[tool result]\" are all assistant/tool actions. There''s no user text. The only \"user\" content is the system instruction at the very top asking to produce the summary. So the \"All user messages\" section would note there were no substantive user messages in this segment. That''s an important audit note.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nFor the public API, let me be careful to only state what''s confirmed. Let me note the confirmed APIs from imports that were actually executed successfully in smoke tests:\n- `from agpack.trust.signing import ...` \u2014 worked\n- `from agpack.trust.delegation import DelegationToken, ChainHop, verify, DelegationViolation, _hop_canonical` \u2014 worked\n- `from agpack.trust.audit import ...` \u2014 worked (in earlier, PYTHONPATH=src)\n\nLet me write the summary.\n\nActually, for the delegation.py public API, let me extract more carefully. From the read_file output and tests:\n- `ChainHop` \u2014 frozen dataclass, field `sig`\n- `DelegationToken`\n- `verify(token, *, logical_now_unix=None, keys=None)` \u2014 returns something truthy or raises `DelegationViolation`\n- `DelegationViolation`\n- `_hop_canonical` (underscore, internal, but imported in test)\n- `_namespace_of`, `_validate_resource`, `_scope_in_closed_set` (", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- tests/test_trust_delegation.py\n- tests/test_trust_signing.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from dataclasses import dataclass, replace @dataclass(frozen=True) class A: x: int a =  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from dataclasses import dataclass, replace @dataclass(frozen=True) class A: x: int a =  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from dataclasses import replace from agpack.sandbox.capabilities import Scope from agp  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && grep -n \"_scope_in_closed_set\\|_scope\\|Scope\\|import.*Enum\\|from enum\" src/agpack/trust/delegation.py | head -20  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from dataclasses import replace from agpack.sandbox.capabilities import Scope from agp  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from dataclasses import replace from agpack.sandbox.capabilities import Scope from agp  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== __init__.py ===\" && cat src/agpack/trust/__init__.py && echo \"\" && echo \"=== audit.py exports ===\" && g  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && grep -n \"cryptography\\|ed25519\\|dependencies\" pyproject.toml | head; echo \"---\"; PYTHONPATH=src python -c \"import  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && grep -n \"import pydantic\\|from pydantic\\|import json\\|def canonical_json_without_sign\\|def to_canonical\" src/agpa  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && PYTHONPATH=src python -c \"import pydantic; print(''pydantic'', pydantic.__version__)\"  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["agpack-prompt-step3.md in the primary scratch directory. The prompt (Builder Prompt #2 \u2014 Step 3, the Trust Layer) is built from the actual contract files, and it flags a real inconsistency I caught while reading. What it covers \u2014 three modules, each with its own build + tests: audit.py (build first, least security-sensitive): the AuditLedger container, AuditRecord schema, replay(), and the LedgerCorrupt failure. Anchored on three load-bearing properties to test before implementing: append-only + fixed ordinal, input redaction (args_sha256_prefix16, never store full args), logical-clock time, \u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787942964.2532694, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('1d5e5635-ce5','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/agpack','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','Reproduce the suite — copy agpack into a writable scratch di','builder',204,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'trust suite reproduction and fix',0,'2026-08-28 21:58:29','{}','{"boundary_index": 156, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation to produce a comprehensive structured summary. This is a long turn sequence with a previous compaction summary to fold in.\n\nLet me work through what happened.\n\n**From the previous compaction summary (fold in still-relevant content):**\n- Project: reproduce trust suite in scratch dir, install deps, run pytest, save output.\n- Branch A: suite broken \u2192 fix it.\n- Suspect: `test_trust_signing.test_canonical_manifest_bytes_is_stable` builds AgentBundleManifest with components missing cid/kind/file fields, SHOULD raise pydantic error \u2192 errors instead of passing.\n- Standing constraint: fix the TEST to construct valid manifest; do NOT weaken schema.\n- Branch B: if suite reproduces GREEN \u2192 Step 4 Portability.\n- Constraints: never claim green without reproduced output; fix test not schema; keep guardrails on (guard.py).\n\n**Conversation since:**\n\nThe user gave a new message: \"Branch A into the audit + delegation suites\"\n\nThis is the key \u2014 the user extended Branch A to also cover the audit and delegation test suites, not just signing.\n\nThe assistant then:\n1. Read audit.py (multiple sections: 1-115, 100-204, 200-379, 380-440, etc.)\n2. Read test_trust_audit.py (1-60, 140-259, 158-187, etc.)\n3. Read test_trust_delegation.py (1-120, 121-373, 1-160, 158-187, 168-267, 262-373)\n4. Read delegation.py (multiple sections)\n5. Read capabilities.py (Scope, CapabilityPolicy)\n6. Ran various pytest commands\n7. Ran grep commands to verify assumptions\n\nThen the assistant did diagnosis and applied fixes:\n\n**Audit fixes:**\n1. `test_validate_rejects_missing_required_field`: validate() documented to name ordinal, kind, offending detail key, but error message drops field name. Needed `_detail_bad` helper. The assistant added `_detail_bad` helper to audit.py and updated 2 check sites.\n   - Applied replace_in_file to audit.py (adding `_detail_bad` function and `_detail_ok` related).\n   - Applied replace_in_file to audit.py (updating check sites to use `_detail_bad`).\n   - Verified with grep.\n2. `test_validate_rejects_unknown_kind`: test wrongly expects `AuditRecord(...kind=\"banana\")` construction to raise (Literal not enforced at construction). Production validate() is the gate. Fixed test to exercise validate() instead.\n   - Applied replace_in_file to test_trust_audit.py.\n\n**Delegation fixes:**\n- Scope: step-1 redundantly does `isinstance(scope, Scope)`, making step-2''s `_scope_in_closed_set` (\"closed Scope\") dead code. Remove the redundant step-1 check so the existing step-2 gate fires.\n- 3 chain tests + hop-signature + policy: test-setup bugs (sub at chain head instead of root, missing key registry slot, wrong CapabilityPolicy constructor).\n\nThe conversation ends with the assistant reading delegation.py 336-360 and reading test_trust_delegation.py 1-160, and running a grep for namespace constants `_NSPACES = (\"mem\", \"fs\", \"net\")` and `_RESOURCE_MIN_LABELS = 3`. The last action was a grep confirming namespace constants.\n\nSo the assistant is in the middle of fixing delegation tests. It has NOT yet applied the delegation test fixes \u2014 it''s still in diagnosis/setup phase, confirming resource strings and reading the test file. The grep at the very end confirmed `_NSPACES = (\"mem\", \"fs\", \"net\")` and `_RESOURCE_MIN_LABELS = 3`.\n\nLet me be precise about what state things are in at the end.\n\nLooking at the sequence:\n- The assistant said \"Diagnosis complete\" and \"Let me apply the production changes first (audit, then delegation).\"\n- Applied audit.py changes (2 replaces)\n- Ran audit suite: 1 F remaining (test_validate_rejects_unknown_kind)\n- Applied test_trust_audit.py fix\n- Updated todos\n- Read delegation tests\n- Grepped for the 6 delegation test names\n- Read delegation test bodies (158-187, 168-267, 262-373)\n- Ran grep for namespace constants\n- The very last action was: grep confirming `_NSPACES = (\"mem\", \"fs\", \"net\")` and `_RESOURCE_MIN_LABELS = 3`\n\nSo at the end, the delegation fixes are NOT YET applied. The assistant is finishing its diagnosis of delegation, confirming the resource string constants needed to fix the test-setup bugs. It''s about to apply delegation test fixes.\n\nWait, let me re-examine. There''s ambiguity in the tool call sequence. The final grep shows namespace constants. This is the assistant confirming details before making edits. So the delegation fixes are pending.\n\nLet me enumerate the delegation test bugs identified:\n\nFrom the diagnosis section:\n- Scope: step-1 redundantly does `isinstance(scope, Scope)`, making step-2''s `_scope_in_closed_set` (\"closed Scope\") dead code. Remove the redundant step-1 check so the existing step-2 gate fires.\n- 3 chain tests + hop-signature + policy: test-setup bugs (sub at chain head instead of root, missing key registry slot, wrong CapabilityPolicy constructor).\n\nWait, this \"Scope\" fix is a PRODUCTION code fix (removing redundant step-1 check in delegation.py). Hmm, but that''s modifying production code. Let me think about whether that''s test-only or production.\n\nActually the diagnosis says: \"Step-1 redundantly does isinstance(scope, Scope)... making step-2''s _scope_in_closed_set dead code. Remove the redundant step-1 check so the existing step-2 gate fires.\" This is modifying delegation.py (production). But wait \u2014 is this the right call? Let me think.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user constraint was: fix the TEST, don''t weaken schema (for signing). But now for delegation/audit, the assistant is making a mix of production fixes and test fixes. Let me check which is which.\n\nFor audit:\n- `_detail_bad` helper added to audit.py \u2014 this is a production fix (adding functionality that was \"documented but not implemented\").\n- test_validate_rejects_unknown_kind \u2014 test fix.\n\nFor delegation:\n- Scope step-1 check removal \u2014 production fix to delegation.py.\n- 3 chain tests + hop-signature + policy \u2014 test fixes.\n\nHmm, so the assistant has been making BOTH production and test fixes across the audit + delegation suites. This is a significant development. But the user''s original instruction was \"Branch A\" which was about fixing the suite. The constraint for signing was \"fix the test not schema.\" But the assistant apparently decided that for audit, the validate() function genuinely needs a `_detail_bad` helper to match its documented contract, and for delegation, the redundant step-1 check needs removal.\n\nWait, I need to be careful here. Let me re-read the constraint from the previous summary: \"never claim green without reproduced output; fix test not schema; keep guardrails on (guard.py).\" And \"fix the TEST to construct valid manifest; do NOT weaken schema.\"\n\nThe \"fix test not schema\" constraint was specifically about the signing test where the assistant was tempted to weaken the pydantic schema. For the audit test, the situation was different: the validate() function''s error message genuinely didn''t name the offending field as documented, and the unknown_kind test genuinely expected construction-time validation that wasn''t there. The assistant decided these were legitimate code gaps OR test misreads.\n\nActually, I should preserve this nuance in the summary: the assistant made production changes to audit.py (added `_detail_bad` helper, updated check sites) and delegation.py (removing redundant scope step-1 check), plus test changes to test_trust_audit.py (unknown_kind). And it''s about to make delegation test changes.\n\nBut wait \u2014 I need to double check: did the assistant actually apply the delegation.py scope fix? Let me look at the tool calls again. \n\nThe assistant said \"Let me apply the production changes first (audit, then delegation).\" then applied audit.py changes. Then ran audit. Then fixed test_trust_audit.py. Then updated todos. Then read delegation tests. Then grepped. Then read delegation test bodies. Then grep namespace constants.\n\nI do NOT see a replace_in_file on delegation.py in the visible tool calls. So the delegation.py scope fix has NOT been applied yet. The assistant only applied audit.py changes and test_trust_audit.py changes so far.\n\nHold on. Let me re-read more carefully. The diagnosis said \"Let me apply the production changes first (audit, then delegation).\" But the actual tool calls only show audit.py changes. So either:\n(a) The delegation.py scope fix is still pending, OR\n(b) It was applied but not shown.\n\nGiven the tool call sequence I can see, only audit.py test_trust_audit.py were modified. The delegation scope production fix appears pending. But actually, since the assistant said it would apply production changes \"first (audit, then delegation)\" and then got caught up in the audit fix (found unknown_kind was a test issue), then moved to reading delegation tests... \n\nActually, looking at the very end, the assistant is STILL reading delegation test files and confirming namespace constants. So it''s in the middle of the delegation diagnosis/fix phase. The delegation scope production fix and delegation test fixes have NOT been applied.\n\nHmm, but actually I realize I should reconsider whether the scope step-1 removal is really needed. Let me think about the actual failing tests.\n\nThe 5 failing delegation tests were:\n1. test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised\n2. test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root\n3. test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub\n4. test_chain_line_no_cycles\n5. test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected\n\n(Plus test_policy_type_available, but I need to check if that was actually failing. The assistant''s note said \"test_policy_type_available ... would raise TypeError \u2014 which is actually what the test name suggests. But the summary flagged it as a failure. Let me run the delegation suite fresh to get the real current failures.\")\n\nWait, there''s confusion about test_policy_type_available. Let me look. The assistant''s grep found 6 test names in test_trust_delegation.py at lines 168, 226, 239, 254, 272, 363. So there are 6 tests. But it said \"5 delegation tests fail (the 6th, test_types_closed_scope_must_be_scope_member, currently passes).\" \n\nHmm wait, that''s confusing. Let me look at the grep results:\n- `grep -n \"def test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised|def test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root|def test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub|def test_chain_line_...\"` returned matches at lines 168, 226, 239, 254, 272, 363. So 6 matches.\n- Then `grep -n \"def test_.*delegation.py\"` returned 0 matches.\n- Then \"That''s my 6 tests.\"\n- Then \"Let me read the scope test, the chain tests, and the policy test bodies.\"\n- Then read 158-187 (which contains test_types_closed_scope_must_be_scope_member and test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised).\n- Then read 168-267.\n- Then read 262-373 (contains test_hop_signature_must_verify, test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected, test_policy_type_available, and the 3 chain tests).\n\nWait, I''m getting confused by the tool calls. Let me look at what test names appear:\n\nFrom the first grep (lines 168, 226, 239, 254, 272, 363):\nThe pattern was `test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised|test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root|test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub|test_chain_line_no_cycles|test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected|test_policy_type_available` \u2014 6 patterns, 6 matches. So:\n- test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised = line 168\n- test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root = line 226\n- test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub = line 239\n- test_chain_line_no_cycles = line 254\n- test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected = line 272\n- test_policy_type_available = line 363\n\nSo these 6 are the named tests. The diagnosis said \"5 delegation tests fail\" \u2014 so 5 of these 6 fail, 1 passes. Which one passes? Probably test_policy_type_available passes (it expects TypeError from CapabilityPolicy(scope=...), which IS raised). And the other 5 fail.\n\nActually, the assistant''s earlier note said \"test_policy_type_available ... would raise TypeError \u2014 which is actually what the test name suggests. But the summary flagged it as a failure.\" So the summary listed it as failing, but on fresh inspection, the test might already pass. So it''s one of the 5 that fails vs 6th that passes.\n\nHmm, but actually the summary said 8 failures: 2 audit + 6 delegation. The 6 delegation were: test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised, test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root, test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub, test_chain_line_no_cycles, test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected, test", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"--- AuditRecord( usages ---\" && grep -rn \"AuditRecord(\" src tests | head -n 30 && echo \"--- _detail_ok usag  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== delegation.py defs ===\" && grep -n \"^def \\|^class \\|def verify\\|def __\" src/agpack/trust/delegation.py   [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python -m pytest tests/test_trust_delegation.py tests/test_trust_audit.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 40  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python -m pytest tests/test_trust_delegation.py::test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised tests/test_trust_delegati  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== asserts on old audit msg ===\" && grep -rn