lError ===\" && grep -nE \"export (function|class|const|type  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && echo \"=== fromB64url return ===\" && sed -n ''1,40p'' packages/core/src/util.ts | grep -nE \"fromB64url|e  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_recall, grep, list_files, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write", "user_messages": ["Rails \u2014 partially \u2713 BridgeRail + BridgeClientShape exist as a wire shape for an external bridge (ap2-x402-bridge / AP2 rail-adapter-x402) \u2713 server.ts already supports a real origin via ORIGIN_URL (proxies the settled request to the real URL over HTTP) \u2713 No real rail is actually wired \u2014 buildRail() returns InMemoryRail by default; the self-402/x402/PPC path is stubbed for the future. This is the one genuinely outstanding piece. Real gaps worth flagging (honest) No top-level README.md \u2014 there''s DEPLOY.md and the talking-points, but nothing that describes the project at a glance. deploy.yml only\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787951077.4310439, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
