he one that matters for \"green CI.\"\n\nWait, actually re-reading \u2014 why does deploy.yml even run on push? It publishes a container image. That''s the deploy workflow. The CI workflow (ci.yml) runs tests. Both need to be green per the user''s \"ship it\" so \"green CI becomes real.\"\n\nActually, the deploy.yml failing dispatch means the GHCR publish never happens, which is fine for CI but means the deploy pipeline is broken. The user wants both green.\n\nOK. Now, the immediate state: bisecting deploy.yml. Let me now also capture the file content of deploy.yml since it''s important and load-bearing. Let me reconstruct it from the read_file output and the replace operations.\n\nFrom the reads:\n- Lines 1-76 (original), with a header comment, `name: deploy`, `on: push: branches: [main]` + pull_request probably, and a permissions block.\n- build-and-publish job with: checkout, docker/login-action@v3 (Login to GHCR), docker/build-push-action, docker/buildx-action, outputs (removed).\n- deploy job: appleboy/ssh-exec-action, needs build-and-publish, `docker compose up -d --no-deps broker` (changed to `docker compose up -d`).\n\nActually I don''t have the FULL content of deploy.yml. The read_file outputs were truncated in places. Let me note what I know:\n- Line 1: `# Deploy the Metered Web Broker to a small VPS.`\n- Comment block about GHCR publish and SSH deploy.\n- The build job has `Login to GitHub Container Registry` step using docker/login-action@v3 with `# needs a gh: login`.\n- The deploy job runs `docker compose up -d` now (was `up -d --no-deps broker`).\n\nI have partial content. I should note the file was read and edited, and give the excerpts I have. I shouldn''t fabricate the full content. The rule says: \"Do NOT carry full file contents as truth. Note THAT a file was read/edited; the coworker re-reads if it needs the content again.\"\n\nSo I''ll note paths, roles, and short excerpts of load-bearing content only.\n\nLet me also note the other files:\n- metered-web-broker-build-plan.md (build plan, modified \u2014 staged/committed)\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml (CI, only fires on push to main + PR; four steps: typecheck, test, demo-ish, conformance)\n- .github/workflows/deploy.yml (deploy to VPS via GHCR + SSH; broken dispatch being debugged)\n- docker-compose.yml\n- Caddyfile\n- DEPLOY.md (health + rollback path recorded here, keep IDENTITY_*/origin creds runtime only)\n- package-lock.json (regenerated to fix npm ci)\n- packages/conformance (conformance harness, Tier B upgrade is P3)\n- PACKAGES/.verify-step1.md (scratch, excluded from commit \u2014 stale)\n- metered-web-broker-talking-points.md (scratch, excluded)\n- PACKAGES/P4-P3-NOTES.md (session notes written)\n\nKey commits:\n- 4056904 \"Ship broker: rails, gateway, conformance, VPS deployment\" on master (then master renamed to main)\n- bca256e \"Fix npm ci: regenerate lock to register @mwb/conformance workspace\"\n- aa70da7 \"Fix deploy.yml dispatch failure + --no-deps bug\"\n- e9b024b \"Trivial test workflow to isolate deploy.yml dispatch failure\" (added zztest.yml)\n- 6d91dd4 \"Bisect: remove needs: block from deploy.yml\"\n\nRemote: origin https://github.com/iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker.git, tracked main.\n\nCI run ids and details:\n- CI test job green after bca256e (run 33222590458 success)\n- deploy.yml workflow databaseId 345012062\n- deploy runs all failing: 33222589926, 33222900776 (on aa70da7), etc.\n- check suites 90043726192 has 0 check runs\n\nDiagnostics:\n- No go toolchain, no pipx, pip needs --break-system-packages\n- actionlint/action-validator not installable in this environment\n- Raw GitHub file byte-identical to local (via gh api contents, ref=aa70da7)\n- Minimal deploy.yml works \u2192 problem is content-specific\n\nUser messages:\n1. The big planning message (\"The immediate next step: ship it...\")\n2. [\"Rename master -> main\"]\n3. [\"metered-web-broker (private)\"]\n\nThen the user didn''t say anything else after the assistant started the bisect investigation (the assistant went on a diagnostic tangent). Actually the last user-visible input is \"metered-web-broker (private)\". After that, the assistant drove the whole investigation. The ask_user calls returned answers via the [user] answer format.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The ask_user calls:\n- First ask_user: \"I''ve committed all the green work... but I can''t push \u2014 this workspace", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- .github/workflows/deploy.yml\n- .github/workflows/zztest.yml\n- PACKAGES/P4-P3-NOTES.md\nRecent shell commands:\n- gh run list --repo iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker --limit 6 --json name,status,conclusion 2>&1 | python3 -c \"import json,sys;[print(f\\\"{r[''name'']:28s} {r[''s  [ok]\n- gh api repos/iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker/check-suites/90043726192/check-runs 2>&1 | python3 -c \" import json,sys d=json.load(sys.stdin) for cr in d.get(''  [ok]\n- gh api repos/iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker/check-suites/90043726192 > /tmp/cs.json 2>&1; python3 -c \" import json d=json.load(open(''/tmp/cs.json'')) print(''  [ok]\n- which go 2>&1; go version 2>&1 | head -1; echo \"=== pip actionlint ===\"; pip install actionlint 2>&1 | tail -3  [ok]\n- pipx install actionlint --break-system-packages 2>&1 | tail -3; echo \"=== which actionlint ===\"; which actionlint 2>&1  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && cp .github/workflows/deploy.yml /tmp/deploy.yml.bak && python3 -c \" import re f=''.github/workflows/de  [ok]\n- git add .github/workflows/deploy.yml && git commit -q -m \"Bisect: remove needs: block from deploy.yml\" && git push 2>&1 | tail -2 && echo \"waiting...\" && sleep   [ok]\n- gh run list --repo iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker --limit 4 --json name,status,conclusion 2>&1 | python3 -c \"import json,sys;[print(f\\\"{r[''name'']:28s} {r[''s  [ok]\n- cat > .github/workflows/deploy.yml <<''EOF'' name: deploy on: push: branches: [main] jobs: build-and-publish: runs-on: ubuntu-latest steps: - uses: actions/checko  [ok]\n- gh run list --repo iconbaypark2900/metered-web-broker --limit 4 --json name,status,conclusion 2>&1 | python3 -c \"import json,sys;[print(f\\\"{r[''name'']:28s} {r[''s  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: ask_user, git_status, list_files, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["The immediate next step: ship it Everything green is currently uncommitted on the working tree \u2014 the only commit is 46082e4 Import\u2026; conformance, rails, and gateway are all untracked, and CI only fires on push to main. So the gate is real but inert on master. The highest-leverage, cheapest action is to stage and commit (rails, gateway, conformance) and push so the green CI becomes real history. Right now the thesis is proven in a tree that isn''t on any branch. After shipping \u2014 P4, then P3 The natural next work, in order: P4 \u2014 real VPS bring-up (metered-web-broker-build-plan.md \u00a75b). This is t\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787963665.1678545, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
