INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('8cc21757-c15','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','Where is this project at in the build?','fastchat',210,NULL,'[{"path": "/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack", "writable": false, "label": "agpack"}, {"path": "/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks", "writable": false, "label": "openworker-tasks"}]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Project Build Status',0,'2026-08-30 22:38:41','{}','{"boundary_index": 120, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully parse this conversation. This is a continuation of a previous compaction. The conversation since the last summary is primarily about building a multi-agent call-chain demo for agpack, driving agpack''s real delegation + audit API.\n\nLet me trace through the key events:\n\n1. The coworker confirmed API surfaces: `delegation.py` (`ChainHop`, `DelegationToken`, `verify`, `_hop_canonical`), `capabilities.py` (`Scope`, `CapabilityPolicy`), `limits.py` (`Budget`), `audit.py` (`AuditLedger`, `AuditRecord`, `replay`).\n\n2. Then it tried to build the demo in the primary scratch (read-write) since agpack is read-only.\n\n3. There was a lot of trouble with file paths \u2014 the `.scratch` path escape issues. Many tool errors:\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"path escapes the workspace\"}`\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"Path does not exist: /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/tests\", \"error_type\": \"ValueError\"}`\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"File does not exist: /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/agpack/trust/delegation.py\", \"error_type\": \"ValueError\"}`\n- etc.\n\n4. The coworker discovered the correct read mechanism: `read_file_lines` works on the read-only path, while `read_file` and `grep` and `read_file` don''t (escape error or not exist).\n\nLet me track the actual successful reads:\n- `read_file_lines` on `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` start 1-120 (total 486) \u2014 worked\n- `grep` on `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/trust` \u2014 \"path escapes the workspace\"\n- `read_file_lines` on delegation.py 121-250 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on limits.py \u2014 \"File does not exist\" error\n- `write_file` `call_chain_demo.py` \u2014 worked (first draft)\n- `read_file_lines` on audit.py 1-130 (total 441) \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on signing.py 1-90 (total 230) \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on signing.py 90-229 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on delegation.py 251-410 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on audit.py 130-249 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on audit.py 249-368 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on delegation.py 411-486 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on audit.py 368-427 \u2014 worked\n\n5. Key API corrections the coworker discovered:\n- Signing is `sign(message, seed_32_bytes) \u2192 SignatureBlock`; there''s no `Keypair`. Public keys for `verify` are raw 32 Ed25519 bytes.\n- `verify(token, *, logical_now_unix, keys: dict[str,bytes])` \u2014 `keys` maps agent_id \u2192 32 raw pubkey bytes.\n- Audit `replay(ledger, kind, ordinal_range)` is a pure view of records; delegate record detail is `{token_id, parent_token_id, hop_depth, scope, resource}`.\n- `_scope_in_closed_set` \u2014 Scope is a str-backed enum, bare string indistinguishable from member.\n- Budget narrowing: for each meter in `(\"fuel_max\", \"memory_pages_max\", \"wall_time_ms\")`, child budget must be \u2264 parent budget.\n- `AuditRecord` fields: ordinal, run_id, kind (`Literal[\"dispatch\", \"import_call\", \"delegate\", \"budget\"]`), ts_unix, subject, detail.\n\n6. Now the tool situation changed dramatically. The previous summary mentioned tools like `run_shell_command`, `run`, `replace_in_file`, `list_files`. But in THIS conversation, the actual tools are `read_file_lines`, `read_file`, `grep`, `write_file`, `brain_note`, `brain_recall`, `todo_write`. There were errors:\n- `{\"error\": \"tool call not executed\", \"reason\": \"unknown tool: run_shell_command\"}`\n- `{\"error\": \"tool call not executed\", \"reason\": \"unknown tool: run\"}`\n- `{\"error\": \"files.<locals>.replace_in_file() missing 1 required positional argument: ''path''\", \"error_type\": \"TypeError\"}`\n\nSo the coworker discovered it does NOT have a shell-execution tool (`run`, `run_shell_command`) and does NOT have `replace_in_file`. It only has file read/write tools, brain_note, brain_recall, todo_write.\n\n7. The coworker then wrote several files:\n- `call_chain_demo.py` \u2014 first draft (rejected/rewritten)\n- `conftest.py`\n- `call_chain_demo_test.py`\n- `run_demo.sh`\n- Rewrote `call_chain_demo.py` with corrected API\n- Rewrote `call_chain_demo_test.py` with corrected API\n- Final `call_chain_demo.py`\n- Final `call_chain_demo_test.py`\n\n8. Critical bug fixes during static review:\n- `ChainHop` is a frozen dataclass \u2014 no `.replace()` method; must use stdlib `dataclasses.replace(obj, \u2026)`.\n- `crypto_sign(...)` returns a `SignatureBlock`, but `ChainHop.sig` must be raw bytes \u2192 use `.signature_bytes`.\n- The forged-hop signature must be valid-length (64 bytes) but wrong content.\n- Timing bug: `verify()` requires `expires_at_unix > logical_now_unix` (strictly). Calling with `logical_now == exp` trips expiry. Need a separate \"current\" logical clock strictly before expiry (`verify_at`).\n\n9. Final state: The coworker did a final `read_file` on call_chain_demo.py to re-read its current demo to catch remaining inconsistencies. The conversation ends mid-thought during this review.\n\nWait \u2014 the last user message is empty `[]`. And then there''s a final read_file that shows the content of call_chain_demo.py. The system prompt is the compaction instruction.\n\nSo the current work is: the coworker has written all files (demo, test, conftest, run script) but could NOT run them (no shell tool). It''s doing a final static read/review of call_chain_demo.py to catch remaining inconsistencies.\n\nLet me now note the important constraints and facts:\n\n**Project: agpack** (continuing from previous summary)\n- Build status through Step 5 (metered access), 276 passed.\n- The task: pick Direction 2 (multi-agent call chain demo) \u2014 authority-diversity demonstration.\n\n**Workspace/paths:**\n- Primary scratch (read-write): `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/`\n- agpack source (read-only): `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/`\n  - Actually note: reads worked on `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` (via read_file_lines), and also the `list_files` returned `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/.scratch/agpack/__init__.py` etc.\n  - So the source layout is `.scratch/agpack/<module>/`. Note the earlier summary said `.scratch/agpack/agpack/` but the actual successful reads were on `.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` (single agpack). Let me reconcile: the list_files showed `.scratch/agpack/__init__.py`, `.scratch/agpack/artifact/__init__.py`. So the package root is `.scratch/agpack/` and modules like `trust/`, `sandbox/`, etc. are directly under it. Good \u2014 so the path is `.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` not `.scratch/agpack/agpack/trust/...`. The earlier summary''s double `agpack/agpack` was wrong or there were two views. I''ll go with what actually worked in this session: `.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py`.\n\n**Files created in this session:**\n1. `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/call_chain_demo.py` \u2014 the demo (rewritten multiple times, final version is \"authority-diversity\" demo)\n2. `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/conftest.py` \u2014 adds agpack read-only source to sys.path\n3. `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/call_chain_demo_test.py` \u2014 tests\n4. `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/run_demo.sh` \u2014 bash runner\n\n**API facts confirmed (authoritative, from reading actual source):**\n\ndelegation.py (486 lines):\n- `ChainHop` \u2014 frozen dataclass with fields including `sig` (raw bytes), `budget`, `scope`, `resource`, `depth`/`hop_depth`, token id, etc.\n- `DelegationToken`\n- `verify(token, *, logical_now_unix, keys: dict[str, bytes])` \u2014 keys maps agent_id \u2192 32 raw Ed25519 pubkey bytes\n- `_hop_canonical`\n- Budget narrowing: for each meter in `(\"fuel_max\", \"memory_pages_max\", \"wall_time_ms\")`, child.budget.meter \u2264 parent.budget.meter, else `Deleg*` exception (truncated: \"raise Dele\u2026\")\n- `_scope_in_closed_set(scope)` \u2014 Scope is str-backed enum\n\ncapabilities.py:\n- `Scope` (str-backed enum), `CapabilityPolicy`\n\nlimits.py:\n- `Budget(fuel_max=\u2026, memory_pages_max=\u2026, wall_time_ms=\u2026)`\n\naudit.py (441 lines):\n- `AuditLedger`, `AuditRecord`, `replay(ledger, kind, ordinal_range)`\n- `AuditRecord` fields: `ordinal: int`, `run_id: str`, `kind: Literal[\"dispatch\", \"import_call\", \"delegate\", \"budget\"]`, `ts_unix: int`, `subject: str`, `detail: dict[str, Any]`\n- `LedgerCorrupt` exception\n- `_DETAIL_SCHEMAS`\n- delegate record detail: `{token_id, parent_token_id, hop_depth, scope, resource}`\n- Ledger assigns `ordinal` at append time.\n\nsigning.py (230 lines):\n- `sign(message, seed_32_bytes) \u2192 SignatureBlock`\n- No `Keypair`. `verify(msg, block)`.\n- Ed25519; canonical serialization of public key: 32 raw bytes.\n- `SignatureBlock` has `.signature_bytes`.\n\n**Tool availability discovery (important for next step):**\n- Available tools this session: `read_file`, `read_file_lines`, `grep`, `write_file`, `brain_note`, `brain_recall`, `todo_write`.\n- NOT available: `run`, `run_shell_command` (both returned \"unknown tool\"), `replace_in_file` (returned TypeError \u2014 needs `path` too, or doesn''t exist as expected).\n- Read access to read-only agpack source works ONLY via `read_file_lines` (read_file and grep and read on `.scratch` paths give \"path escapes the workspace\" or \"File does not exist\").\n\nWait, let me double check. The coworker said: \"The tool is refusing all access to the read-only agpack path, even though the workspace header says it''s read-available.\" And list_files worked. And read_file_lines worked. And grep failed with escape. And read_file failed with \"File does not exist\". And list_files worked.\n\nHmm, this is a bit inconsistent. Let me re-read:\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"path escapes the workspace\"}` \u2014 grep on trust/\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"Path does not exist: .../.scratch/agpack/tests\", \"error_type\": \"ValueError\"}` \u2014 list_files on tests\n- `[tool result] {\"error\": \"File does not exist: .../.scratch/agpack/agpack/trust/delegation.py\", \"error_type\": \"ValueError\"}` \u2014 read_file (note: double agpack, wrong path)\n- `list_files` on `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack` \u2014 worked, returned the .scratch listing\n- `read_file_lines` on `.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` start 1-120 \u2014 worked\n- `grep` on `.scratch/agpack/trust` \u2014 \"path escapes the workspace\"\n- `read_file_lines` on `.scratch/agpack/trust/delegation.py` 121-250 \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on `.scratch/agpack/trust/limits.py` \u2014 \"File does not exist\"\n- write_file call_chain_demo.py \u2014 worked\n- `read_file_lines` on audit.py 1-130 \u2014 worked\n- read_file_lines on signing.py 1-90 \u2014 worked\n- read_file_lines on signing.py 90-229 \u2014 worked\n- read_file_lines on delegation.py 251-410 \u2014 worked\n- read_file_lines on audit.py 130-249 \u2014 worked\n- read_file_lines on audit.py 24", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/call_chain_demo_test.py\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/call_chain_demo.py\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/run_demo.sh\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/conftest.py\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_recall, grep, list_files, read_file, read_file_lines, replace_in_file, run, run_shell_command, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["Where is this project at in the build?", "Give me a prompt to begin the next task", "What is left to do: Step 4 (Portability Proof) is complete. Here''s the report. ## (a) Test count + pass/fail **231 passed** \u2014 up from the 203 baseline. The 28 new cases all live in `tests/test_portability_proof.py`. Run with the canonical command: ``` python -m pytest tests/ -q ``` (no env var needed \u2014 `pyproject.toml` has `pythonpath = [\"src\"]`). No `wasmtime`/`wasmer` installed, no `pip` installs, standard library + pydantic only. ## (b) Files added/changed - **`src/agpack/portability/driver.py`** (new) \u2014 the interface only: `RuntimeDriver`/`Instance` protocols, `ToolCall`/`RunResult` wire \u2026", "proceed", "Step 5 is complete and committed. ## What I did this session Picked up from fixing test-writing bugs in `tests/test_metered_access.py`. Three remaining failures, all test-only (the source was correct): 1. **`test_exhaustion_when_mixed_with_failures_keeps_count`** \u2014 the flaky tool raised `RuntimeError`, but the loop only caught `InsufficientFuel`. Added an `except RuntimeError: continue` branch so the flaky raise doesn''t escape (it''s not a billing event). 2. **`test_broker_reconcile_equals_initial_minus_remaining`** \u2014 the `remaining == 6` assertion was wrong (the exhaustion loop drains to 0); \u2026", "Sketch out both", "The `.bundle` is a runtime-generated artifact (written to CWD, not a committed source file) \u2014 that''s expected. The deliverables are complete. ## Done \u2014 Direction A deliverables **1. `examples/hello-agent/` \u2014 a runnable, real bundle** - `prompt.md`, `policy.yaml`, `maxcap.yaml`, `memory.yaml`, `evals/one.json`, `tools/greet_tool.py`, `tools/greet.wasm.yaml` \u2014 a genuine `pack()`-able agent dir. - `run_it.py` drives the full flow: `pack` \u2192 `verify` \u2192 portability proof, plus a bonus that runs the tool''s own `run` export through both engines. ``` step 1/3 pack : wrote hello-agent.bundle (3818 byte\u2026", "I rather this direciton: 2. A multi-agent \"call chain\" demo. agpack''s real crown jewel is per-hop scoped delegation (delegation.py) \u2014 a token that narrows as it passes hop to hop through a signed chain. A demo where an orchestrator delegates to a scorer, which delegates to a memoizer, each hop carrying a narrowing scope, replayed later from the audit ledger, shows the one thing nothing else in your stack does. It''s the portability proof''s conceptual twin (that one''s engine-diversity; this one''s authority-diversity)."], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788128814.6851225, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
