INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('0dfe1e25-a8f','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','Where is this project at?','fastchat',141,NULL,'[{"path": "/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker", "writable": false, "label": "metered-web-broker"}, {"path": "/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks", "writable": false, "label": "openworker-tasks"}]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Project status check',0,'2026-08-31 00:01:50','{}','{"boundary_index": 86, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully read through this conversation and understand what happened. This is a complex session where the coworker (AI) is working on the metered-web-broker TypeScript project, specifically P1 \u2014 Conformance Tier B.\n\nLet me trace the whole thing:\n\n1. User asked \"Where is this project at?\" \u2014 coworker checked memory and gave status on 3 projects (opensciencelab, metered-web-broker, Job search).\n\n2. User clarified \"I''m asking about the metered-web-broker. give me details about this project\" \u2014 coworker gave a detailed status report. Key facts:\n   - TypeScript npm-workspace, neutral \"one-contract\" Metered Web Broker\n   - One endpoint returns content + license + settlement receipt\n   - Positioned against 2026 agent protocols map (MCP, A2A, UCP, AP2, A2UI, AG-UI)\n   - 6+ packages: core, budget, identity, rails, license, audit, gateway, conformance\n   - stdlib-only Node (no Express)\n   - Verified as of 2026-08-28: npm ci, typecheck exit 0, npm test 58 passed, conformance exit 0\n   - Open gaps: no deployment surface/VPS bring-up tested, no live 402\u2192settle\u2192content loop, conformance still \"Tier A\", no finality flag, not pushed anywhere (git remote empty)\n\n3. User: \"give me a prompt to begin the next task\" \u2014 coworker wrote `metered-web-broker-next-task.md` to `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f/`. Full P0-P3 prompt.\n\n4. User posted a report of what THEY (or a prior session) did:\n   - P0 assumptions were already resolved upstream\n   - git remote was NOT empty \u2014 origin, forgejo, github configured. main pushed to origin and github, forgejo had latest commit.\n   - deploy.yml --no-deps bug already fixed by commit c0e4216 (2026-08-28)\n   - Re-ran gate stack: typecheck exit 0 (5 packages), 58/58, conformance 4/4 exit 0\n   - Pushed to forgejo: git push forgejo main \u2192 122ebb8..b38aff4\n   - Did NOT push github (public mirror) \u2014 asked user\n   - P1-P3 still open\n   - Actually wait, this report is from the USER or a prior agent session. It''s presented as a report. This is confusing. Let me re-read.\n\nActually this [user] message contains a report that reads like it''s from an agent (\"I did P0\"). This might be pasted from another agent session or the user relaying. Then the coworker responded by reading deploy.yml and .git/config to verify.\n\nWait, let me re-read the order. After the report, there''s:\n[assistant \u2192 read_file] deploy.yml\n[assistant \u2192 read_file] .git/config\n[assistant] \"Looking for a question? The last thing I did was write up the P0\u2013P3 next-task prompt...\"\n\nSo the coworker read those files and then gave a canned \"what would you like to do\" response. Hmm, but then the conversation continues.\n\n5. User: \"What is the next task?\" \u2014 coworker said next task is P0: unblock deployment.\n\n6. User: \"Give me the prompt to begin P1\" \u2014 coworker wrote `metered-web-broker-P1-conformance-tierb.md` with the full P1 prompt.\n\n7. User: \"Check the last session, it stopped because of max iterations\" \u2014 coworker checked memory. Found the session was P1: conformance Tier B. Listed what was done and what was cut off.\n\n8. User: \"proceed\" \u2014 coworker created a todo list (6 todos) and started reading the conformance package files.\n\n9. Then a LONG sequence of file reads and analysis. The coworker discovered the conformance package is in a broken half-built state:\n   - `validators.ts` is a stub re-exporting from `fetch.js`/`drift.js`, never exports `VALIDATORS`\n   - `registry.ts` imports VALIDATORS from validators.js \u2014 would throw\n   - `cli.ts` calls run() synchronously but run is now async\n   - No `.test.ts` files\n   - `types.ts` has different field names than `run.ts`\n   \n10. The coworker resolved spec URLs via web_fetch:\n    - A2A: https://a2a-protocol.org/v0.3.0/specification/ \u2014 200\n    - AP2: https://ap2-protocol.org/ap2/specification/ \u2014 200\n    - UCP: https://ucp.dev/2026-04-08/specification/overview/ \u2014 200\n    - Web Bot Auth: https://www.webbotauth.org/spec/directory-2026-07/ \u2014 404 (BLOCKER)\n\n11. coworker did more reads: PACKAGES/P4-P3-NOTES.md, package.json, scripts/demo.ts, audit ledger.ts, core/types.ts, core/index.ts, audit/index.ts, run.ts, registry.ts\n\n12. The last few actions were reading run.ts and registry.ts again (to recover the original contract validators from git).\n\nSo the session ends with the coworker about to begin fixing the broken conformance package to complete P1.\n\nImportant context: there''s a discrepancy in paths. The coworker says the repo is at `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker` and it''s read-only. Work should happen in writable scratch at `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f/`.\n\nAlso note: the grep for VALIDATORS returned \"path escapes the workspace\" error. And some greps returned the same error. This is because the workspace boundary doesn''t include dataScience? Interesting. But the read_file calls on files under dataScience/metered-web-broker succeeded. So the workspace must actually be /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker or the coworker can read those. The grep escaping is odd but let me note it.\n\nNow let me figure out the CURRENT state and what the next step should be.\n\nThe session just ended. The coworker has:\n- Read all the conformance package files\n- Confirmed A2A, AP2, UCP URLs work; Web Bot Auth returns 404\n- Confirmed the package is broken (validators.ts stub, CLI sync/async mismatch, no tests)\n- Was reading run.ts and registry.ts again to recover original contract validators from git\n\nThe immediate next step would be to recover the original contract validators (which existed before the Tier B upgrade) from git, since `validators.ts` was gutted. Then rewrite the whole conformance package: contracts validators + protocol validators + async CLI + tests + fixtures, and resolve the Web Bot Auth URL.\n\nLet me now structure the summary.\n\nKey facts to preserve:\n\n**Primary request and intent:**\n- User wants the metered-web-broker project worked on, specifically moving P1 (Conformance Tier B) forward. The overarching project: a TypeScript \"one-contract\" Metered Web Broker.\n- The immediate task: complete P1 \u2014 upgrade `@mwb/conformance` from Tier A to Tier B (live-spec fetch + draft-drift detection).\n- Standing constraint: repo is read-only; copy to writable scratch and work there. Don''t push to public github mirror without approval. Ask user before pushing anywhere.\n- P1 must NOT roll into P2 (real 402 round-trip) or P3 (finality flag).\n- The immediate blocker: resolve correct reachable spec URLs, especially Web Bot Auth (currently 404).\n\nWait \u2014 but the repo is read-only, and the coworker has been reading files directly from `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker`. The task prompt says to copy to scratch and work there. So the actual writing needs to happen in scratch. This is important \u2014 the coworker should NOT edit in place in read-only.\n\nLet me note the task folder: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f/` contains `metered-web-broker-next-task.md` and `metered-web-broker-P1-conformance-tierb.md`.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions:**\n- Metered Web Broker = one end