/protocols/drift.ts` \u2014 pure drift-detection (computeDiff)\n  - `src/protocols/fetch.ts` \u2014 live-spec provenance layer, network-free model, fetcher injected via ValidatorContext\n  - `src/types.ts` \u2014 SpecProvenance, ValidatorContext, ValidationResult.spec/detail, async ValidatorFn, contract types (ContractCard, SpendLineCard, IdentityCard, LicenseCard, LicenseClauseCard, TerminalKind)\n  - `src/run.ts` \u2014 async, imports registry and types. Returns contract/contractName. Renders provenance blocks. Has ANSI helpers CONFORMANCE_OK/WARN/NOTE.\n  - `src/registry.ts` \u2014 Registry class, imports VALIDATORS from validators.js\n  - `src/validators.ts` \u2014 STUB (gutted), re-exports from fetch.js/drift.js, does NOT export VALIDATORS. Broken.\n  - `src/cli.ts` \u2014 entry point: `tsx packages/conformance/src/cli.ts <fixturePath> <contractName>`; calls run() synchronously (BUG \u2014 run is async). Reads+parses JSON, resolves validators by name, runs, reports, exit 0 pass/1 fail.\n  - `src/index.ts` \u2014 re-exports\n  - `package.json` \u2014 name @mwb/conformance, scripts only typecheck (no test script!). peerDeps typescript. No deps.\n  - `tsconfig.json` \u2014 extends ../../tsconfig.base.json, include [\"src\"]\n  - `fixtures/a2a-card.json` \u2014 good fixture (fetchId demo-fetch-1, fulfilled)\n  - `fixtures/a2a-card-bad.json` \u2014 bad fixture (failureClass=''error'' invalid, spend lines on denied)\n- Root files:\n  - `package.json` \u2014 root, workspaces packages/*, scripts typecheck/test/test:web\n  - `vitest.config.ts` \u2014 include packages/*/src/**/*.test.ts\n  - `tsconfig.base.json` \u2014 target ES2022, strict, noUncheckedIndexedAccess, verbatimModuleSyntax, types node\n  - `.github/workflows/ci.yml` \u2014 jobs build: npm ci, npm run typecheck, npm test, npm run conformance packages/conformance/fixtures/a2a-card.json a2a-card\n\n**Errors and fixes:**\n- The whole conformance package is currently BROKEN: validators.ts is a stub without VALIDATORS export; registry.ts would throw at import; cli.ts calls async run() synchronously; types.ts/run.ts field name mismatch (contract vs artifact", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f/metered-web-broker-P1-conformance-tierb.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/0dfe1e25-a8f/metered-web-broker-next-task.md\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_recall, grep, list_files, read_file, todo_write, web_fetch, write_file", "user_messages": ["Where is this project at?", "I''m asking about the metered-web-broker. give me details about this project", "give me a prompt to begin the next task", "## P0 \u2014 unblocked \u2705 Here''s what I found and did: **The two P0 assumptions were already resolved upstream** (likely by the prior session on this box): | Assumption | Reality | |---|---| | \"git remote was empty \u2014 nothing ever pushed\" | **False.** `origin`, `forgejo`, and `github` are all configured. `main` was already pushed to `origin` and `github` (though `forgejo` had the latest commit). | | \"deploy.yml ~75 has `up -d --no-deps broker`\" | **Fixed already.** Commit `c0e4216` (2026-08-28, \"deploy up -d\") already removed `--no-deps broker`. Current line 86 is just `docker compose -f docker-comp\u2026", "What is the next task?", "Give me the prompt to begin P1", "Check the last session, it stopped because of max iterations", "proceed"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788132351.2875977, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('52b4435c-621','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/agpack','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','Continue the agpack build. Context: agpack is a portable, ve','builder',189,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Let me start by verifying the current state, then build Step',0,'2026-08-30 20:10:11','{}','{"boundary_index": 97, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation to produce a structured compaction summary. The context is a previous compaction summary plus the conversation since.\n\nThe user is working on \"agpack\" \u2014 a portable, verifiable agent runtime. The current task is Step 4: Portability Proof.\n\nLet me trace through everything load-bearing.\n\n**The task (single user message, from previous summary):**\n- Continue the agpack build.\n- Steps 1-3 implemented and tested. Baseline is 203 passed.\n- Command to run: `python -m pytest tests/ -q`\n- Do NOT widen schema or rewrite steps 1-3 unless a test genuinely requires it.\n- NEXT TASK \u2014 Step 4: Portability Proof (agpack/portability/).\n- Goal: prove the thesis \u2014 the SAME bundle executes UNCHANGED on two different runtimes and the observable behavior matches.\n- Constraints (folded from previous summary):\n  - Tests must run GREEN WITHOUT wasmtime/wasmer/pip-installing anything (stdlib + pydantic only).\n  - Keep the trust layer untouched.\n  - Reuse agpack/trust and agpack/sandbox only via existing protocols; import only under TYPE_CHECKING if it breaks no-extra-deps.\n  - Every test GREEN. Aim for 20+ tests.\n  - Report back: (a) test count + pass/fail, (b) files added/changed with one line each, (c) whether proof actually runs computation through both drivers.\n  - If a constraint makes the proof trivial/unfaithful, say so.\n\n**Step 4 components required:**\n1. portability/driver.py \u2014 RuntimeDriver Protocol (instantiate, dispatch(tool_call), shutdown) + `port()` function. Takes bundle''s compiled tool module + pair of drivers, runs SAME set of tool calls through each, returns RunResult objects per driver.\n2. portability/drivers.py \u2014 two concrete drivers:\n   - PurePythonDriver \u2014 interprets tool module in-process (real execution).\n   - DeterministicFingerprintDriver \u2014 second runtime whose observable OUTPUT bytes differ in wrapping/timestamping but whose SEMANTIC result is provably equal.\n3. portability/proof.py \u2014 `run_portability_proof(bundle)` runs small fixed script of tool calls, and `assert_equivalent()` compares SEMANTIC outputs. Raise PortabilityViolation on real divergence.\n4. A minimal fixture bundle.\n\n**Design decisions established:**\n- Design against PROTOCOLS (duck-typed), not real WASM.\n- Both drivers consume the same tool module bytes.\n- PurePythonDriver interprets a tool module in-process.\n- DeterministicFingerprintDriver models a different runtime whose output bytes are wrapped/timestamped differently but semantically equal.\n- The \"tool module\" is modeled as a serialized representation interpretable by pure Python (no wasmtime).\n\n**Key API facts established from reading driver.py, drivers.py, proof.py:**\n\ndriver.py:\n- Has `RuntimeDriver` / `Instance` Protocols.\n- `ToolCall` dataclass (has `.export`, `.args`).\n- `RunResult` dataclass (has `.engine`, `.call_index`, `.output`, `.ts`, `.fingerprint`). Wait, need to check. In the smoke test, they access `r.engine`, `r.call_index`, `r.output`, `r.ts`, `r.fingerprint`. Earlier they tried `r.raw_value`, `r.wrapped` which failed \u2014 those don''t exist.\n- `_unwrap` returns `Unwrapped` dataclass (not a 4-tuple).\n- `port()` returns `PortabilityResult` (not a 3-tuple). Has `.engines` and `.runs`.\n- `CompiledToolModule` \u2014 keyword-only, has `.entry` and exports.\n- `sha256_prefix16` function.\n- `PortabilityViolation` exception.\n- `portability_result` maybe a helper? The tests reference it in the rewritten version.\n- `_dispatch` uses `call.export` for multi-export.\n- `Instance` Protocol requires `name`, `call(export, args)`, `peak_memory_pages()`.\n\ndrivers.py:\n- `PurePythonDriver` / `PurePythonInstance` \u2014 real execution.\n- `DeterministicFingerprintDriver` / `DeterministicFingerprintInstance` \u2014 wraps output.\n- DFD envelope: `DFD#` decimal-ts envelope.\n- `instance._exports = None` cleanup in dispose.\n- `PeakPythonInstance`? No. The Instance requires `name` attribute set.\n- sha256 prefixing.\n- `import time` added (they moved it to top of file).\n\nproof.py:\n- `run_portability_proof(module, calls=None)` \u2014 fixture tool, runs fixed script.\n- `assert_equivalent(result)` \u2014 takes PortabilityResult, returns `tuple[bytes]` of common outputs.\n- `make_fixture_module()` \u2014 creates the fixture tool module (pure Python computing sum/filter/hex).\n- Imports `drivers` at top (`import drivers as _drivers`) rather than inline `agpack.portability.drivers` to fix the PYTHONPATH issue.\n- Fixture tool module source has exports: sum, filter-even, hex.\n\n**Errors and fixes:**\n1. `_dispatch` dispatched `module.entry` not `call.export` \u2014 fixed via replace_in_file.\n2. Instances lacked `peak_memory_pages()` \u2014 added.\n3. `Instance` Protocol requires `name` attribute \u2014 set in both instances.\n4. Circular-import smell: fixture source had dead `_emit` that imported `proof` \u2014 removed.\n5. `python -c` doesn''t bind `agpack` module name locally \u2014 fixed by importing `drivers` at top of `proof.py` (`import drivers as _drivers`).\n6. Missing `class DeterministicFingerprintInstance(Instance):` declaration line \u2014 the docstring ran directly onto previous `call` method. Fixed by adding the declaration.\n7. `RunResult` has no `wrapped`/`raw_value` attribute \u2014 switched to using `output`.\n8. `ts` showed `-1` for fingerprint driver because encoded as hex \u2014 changed to real decimal wall-clock timestamp so difference is genuine.\n9. Tests were written based on assumptions and didn''t match real API \u2014 had to re-read driver.py, drivers.py, proof.py, then rewrite tests to match actual implementation.\n10. `tests/test_portability_driver.py` \u2014 \"not a file\" error when trying to read a non-existent file.\n\n**Files:**\n- `src/agpack/portability/driver.py` \u2014 RuntimeDriver/Instance Protocols, ToolCall, RunResult, PortabilityResult, PortabilityViolation, port(), sha256_prefix16, _unwrap, Unwrapped, CompiledToolModule.\n- `src/agpack/portability/drivers.py` \u2014 PurePythonDriver/Instance, DeterministicFingerprintDriver/Instance.\n- `src/agpack/portability/proof.py` \u2014 run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module.\n- `src/agpack/portability/__init__.py` \u2014 docstring describes profiles.py/compat_harness.py but those are dead stubs.\n- `src/agpack/portability/compat_harness.py` \u2014 dead stub (raise NotImplementedError), describes old real-WASM design.\n- `src/agpack/portability/profiles.py` \u2014 dead stub (raise NotImplementedError).\n- `tests/test_portability_proof.py` \u2014 new test suite being written (final version).\n- `src/agpack/sandbox/__init__.py` line 40-57 references `portability.profiles.wasmtime` in docstring only (not runtime import).\n\n**Dead stubs:**\n- `compat_harness.py` and `profiles.py` are dead stubs (both `raise NotImplementedError`). Only `__init__.py` references them in docstring. The sandbox `__init__.py` line 40-57 references `portability.profiles.wasmtime` only in docstring text.\n\nNote: The assistant said \"I''ll clean them up after the tests pass.\" So removing the dead stubs is a pending cleanup task.\n\n**Current state at compaction:**\n- driver.py, drivers.py, proof.py are written and smoke-tested working end-to-end.\n- `run_portability_proof(make_fixture_module())` works, engines run, assert_equivalent returns common outputs.\n- Test suite `tests/test_portability_proof.py` is being rewritten to match the actual API (last action is the write_file of the rewritten test).\n- Still need to: run the full test suite, confirm GREEN, clean up dead stubs (compat_harness.py, profiles.py), update __init__.py docstring, report back.\n\n**Pending tasks:**\n- Finish/verify the rewritten `tests/test_portability_proof.py`.\n- Run `python -m pytest tests/ -q` \u2014 confirm all GREEN (should be 203 + new portability tests).\n- Clean up dead stubs: `compat_harness.py`, `profiles.py` (raise NotImplementedError) \u2014 remove them since they''re dead code; update `__init__.py` docstring which references them.\n- Report back: (a) test count + pass/fail, (b) files added/changed with one line each, (c) whether proof actually runs computation through both drivers, (d) note unfaithfulness constraint (no real WASM \u2014 pure-Python interpretation).\n\n**Report requirements (must report back):**\n(a) test count + pass/fail\n(b) files added/changed with one line each\n(c) whether proof actually runs computation through both drivers\n(d) if constraint makes proof trivial/unfaithful, say so \u2014 YES: no real WASM engines (wasmtime/wasmer unavailable), so the \"runtime\" is simulated via two pure-Python interpreters producing semantically-equal but envelope-different output. This is a known unfaithfulness the user must be told.\n\nLet me now structure all of this into the 8 required sections.\n\nLet me be careful about the exact API details since the coworker needs to continue and the tests are being written to match the actual API.\n\nKey API details to preserve:\n\n`portability/driver.py`:\n- `RuntimeDriver` Protocol / `Instance` Protocol.\n- `Instance` needs: `name` attr, `call(export: str, args: bytes) -> bytes`, `peak_memory_pages()`.\n- `ToolCall` dataclass: `.export`, `.args`.\n- `RunResult` dataclass: `.engine`, `.call_index`, `.output`, `.ts`, `.fingerprint`.\n- `_unwrap` free function returns `Unwrapped` dataclass (private).\n- `port()` returns `PortabilityResult` with attributes `.engines` and `.runs`.\n- `CompiledToolModule` \u2014 keyword-only construction, has `.entry` and exports dict.\n- `sha256_prefix16` helper.\n- `PortabilityViolation` exception.\n\nWait \u2014 I need to double check `port()` signature. The smoke test called `run_portability_proof(make_fixture_module())`. Let me look at what `port` was called with in the replace:\n```\nreturn port(\n module,\n _drivers.PurePythonDriver(),\n _drivers.DeterministicFingerprintDriver(),\n calls,\n)\n```\nSo `port(module, driver1, driver2, calls)`.\n\n`portability/drivers.py`:\n- `PurePythonDriver`, `PurePythonInstance`.\n- `DeterministicFingerprintDriver`, `DeterministicFingerprintInstance`.\n- DFD envelope prefix `DFD#`.\n- `import time` at top of file (they moved it).\n\n`portability/proof.py`:\n- `run_portability_proof(module, calls=None)` \u2014 if calls None, uses fixed script calling exports 1..N (or the fixture exports).\n- `assert_equivalent(result: PortabilityResult) -> tuple[bytes]`.\n- `make_fixture_module()` \u2014 returns a CompiledToolModule.\n- `import drivers as _drivers` at top (fix for PYTHONPATH binding).\n\nFixture module exports: sum, filter-even (filter even), hex. It computes sum/filter-even/hex of a JSON list of integers.\n\nLet me also note the test conventions: `from __future__ import annotations`, imports pytest.\n\nAlso the constraint: tests must run GREEN without wasmtime/wasmer/pip. And the `PYTHONPATH=src` was used for the smoke tests. For pytest, need to check whether pytest is run with PYTHONPATH=src. The baseline command was `python -m pytest tests/ -q`. Let me note that `agpack` is importable \u2014 possibly the project is installed or there''s a conftest. Actually in the smoke tests they used `PYTHONPATH=src`. For the pytest run, I should note the coworker may need PYTHONPATH=src or that the project uses src layout. Let me note this.\n\nActually, the test file is in `tests/` and imports `from agpack.portability...`. With src-layout, they''d need `PYTHONPATH=src` or the package installed. The baseline test run was `python -m pytest tests/ -q`. Hmm. This is worth noting as a potential issue \u2014 the coworker should verify the test command. Let me note it as a check.\n\nNow, the sandbox `__init__.py` reference to `portability.profiles.wasmtime` in docstring \u2014 the assistant read lines 40-57 and it''s docstring text only. The assistant''s note: \"It''s only docstring text, not a runtime import \u2014 the stubs are safe dead code.\"\n\nLet me also record the \"report back\" requirement clearly since that''s the user''s explicit deliverable.\n\nNow let me also record the unfaithfulness flag prominently. The user said: \"If a constraint makes the proof trivial/unfaithful, say so.\" The constraint (no wasmtime/wasmer available)", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- tests/test_portability_proof.py\n- src/agpack/portability/proof.py\n- src/agpack/portability/drivers.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- python -c \" from agpack.portability.proof import run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module res = run_portability_proof(make_fixture_module()  [exit 1]\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from agpack.portability.proof import run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module res = run_portability_proof(make_f  [exit 1]\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from agpack.portability.proof import run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module res = run_portability_proof(make_f  [exit 1]\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from agpack.portability.proof import run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module res = run_portability_proof(make_f  [exit 1]\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from agpack.portability.proof import run_portability_proof, assert_equivalent, make_fixture_module res = run_portability_proof(make_f  [exit 1]\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -c \" from agpack.port