u2014 at line 247 redefines `ValidatorFn = (card: ContractCard) => ValidationResult` which conflicts with the two-arg `ValidatorFn` in types.ts. This is a known bug to fix.\n- `run.ts` \u2014 error because validators.ts redefines single-arg ValidatorFn.\n- `cli.ts` \u2014 non-async; needs to be async for network fetch.\n\n**Current work state:**\nThe AI just re-wrote drift.ts (write_file at the end). The scaffold is present but half-compiled. The plan is to:\n1. Fix typecheck errors (validators.ts single-arg ValidatorFn, cli.ts non-async, drift.ts guards)\n2. Build live-spec fetch + provenance layer (fetch.ts)\n3. Build async protocol validators using computeDiff\n4. Add good/bad + older-drift fixtures + tests\n5. Wire CI\n\nLet me look at the todo list more carefully. From the tool results:\n- \"Establish baseline + typecheck fixes (editions path, drift engine, ValidatorFn)\" \u2014 in_progress\n- \"Build live-spec fetch + provenance layer (fetch.ts)\" \u2014 pending\n- \"Build async protocol validators (a2a/ap2/ucp/web-bot-auth) using computeDiff\" \u2014 pending\n- \"Add good/bad + older-drift protocol fix\u2026\" \u2014 pending\n\nThe very last action was writing drift.ts. The AI was about to address the typecheck errors and then build the next layers.\n\nWait, let me re-read the sequence. The last few actions:\n- read run.ts (1-93)\n- read drift.ts (1-138)\n- read registry.ts (1-46)\n- read cli.ts\n- write_file drift.ts (new content)\n- read run.ts (1-93) again\n- read drift.ts (1-138) again\n- write_file drift.ts (FINAL)\n\nSo the final action was a write_file of drift.ts. The AI was iterating on drift.ts to add field-path + presence support.\n\nActually, let me look at the flow more carefully. There seem to be two interleaved threads based on the tool results. Let me focus on the most recent.\n\nThe most recent sequence:\n1. read run.ts\n2. read drift.ts\n3. read registry.ts\n4. read cli.ts\n5. read types.ts\n6. read validators.ts (tail 244-258)\n7. run_shell