bot-auth) using computeDiff \u2014 pending\n4. Add good/bad + older-drift protocol fix[tures] + tests \u2014 pending\n5. (likely) Wire CI / full verification \u2014 pending\n\nThe current work: just wrote drift.ts (new version with field-path + presence support). Next: fix typecheck errors, particularly the `ValidatorFn` redefinition in validators.ts line 247, and the non-async cli.ts.\n\nNow, there''s an important detail. The \"38/38\" baseline. Let me note that the whole-repo test count \u2014 the find command showed test files but was cut off. The earlier compaction said 58/58 then corrected to 38/38. There''s ambiguity. I''ll note the discrepancy.\n\nActually, from the run_shell output: `=== test files ===` `packages/audit/src/ledger.test.ts` `packages/budget/src/engine.test...` \u2014 cut off. The baseline typecheck had errors. The baseline test count isn''t clearly established in this session''s results. I''ll note that the baseline needs to be captured and that conformance package has zero tests.\n\nLet me now write the summary. I need to be concrete and preserve load-bearing info.\n\nLet me structure the field sets carefully since these are important for the drift engine:\n\n**A2A card (group: `card` / capabilities):**\n- older capabilities: `[''agentExtensions'', ''messageTypes'']`\n- pinned capabilities: `[''agentExtensions'', ''messageTypes'', ''pushNotificationConfig'']`\n- live capabilities: `[''agentExtensions'', ''messageTypes'', ''pushNotificationConfig'', ...]`\n\n**AP2 mandate (group: `mandate`):**\n- older: `[''user'', ''agent'', ''shoppingIntent'', ''ttl'']`\n- pinned: `[''user'', ''agent'', ''shoppingIntent'', ''ttl'']`\n- live: `[''user'', ''merchant'', ''shoppingIntent'', ''ttl'']`\n- rename: agent \u2192 merchant (pinned\u2192live)\n\n**Key decision on drift engine:**\n- `computeDiff(artifact, manifest, pin=''pinned'')` \u2014 validates pinned fields required, reports drift vs reference edition\n- Needs field-path support (nested lookup) and presence sets\n- referenceFields", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker/packages/conformance/src/protocols/drift.ts\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker/packages/conformance/PHASE.md\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && node -e \"fetch(''https://a2a-protocol.org/v0.3.0/specification/'', {signal: AbortSignal.timeout(8000)})  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && find packages/conformance -type f | sort && echo \"---FIXTURES---\" && ls -la packages/conformance/fixt  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && echo \"=== CI files ===\" && ls .github/workflows/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== baseline typecheck ===\" && np  [ok]\n- echo \"todo tool test via shell\"  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && echo \"=== test files ===\" && find packages -name ''*.test.ts'' | sort && echo \"=== conformance index ==  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && echo \"=== BASELINE typecheck (workspace) ===\" && npx tsc -p packages/conformance/tsconfig.json --noEm  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && node -e \"fetch(''https://a2a-protocol.org/v0.3.0/specification/'', {signal: AbortSignal.timeout(6000)})  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_note, read_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["Task: P1 \u2014 Conformance Tier B (live-spec fetch + draft-drift detection) Scope: Upgrade @mwb/conformance from Tier A (re-validates the broker''s own generated card against its own rules \u2014 can''t catch external drift) to Tier B: fetch the live spec for each protocol, validate a real artifact against it, and flag version drift when a draft bumps a field. The metered-web-broker repo is read-only. Copy it to writable scratch, work there, run the gate stack, report exit codes. The gate stack (run all four, all green, report each exit code) npm ci npm run typecheck (exit 0) npm test (all pass \u2014 58/58 \u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788125732.370434, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('d2feffe4-a92','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/agpack','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','The Step 5 (metered access) prompt is drafted and saved at a','builder',249,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Metered Access Prompt Ready for Step 5',0,'2026-08-30 21:06:30','{}','{"boundary_index": 131, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation to produce a structured summary.\n\nThe context: This is a session history compacting task. The user is asking the AI to summarize a conversation so the \"coworker\" can continue working in a smaller context.\n\nLet me trace through the events. The conversation appears to be from an ongoing agpack project build. The user provided context about Step 5 (metered access) prompt, and the assistant proceeded to implement `agpack/tools/metered.py` and tests.\n\nKey facts from the previous compaction summary:\n- Project: agpack \u2014 \"Portable, verifiable agent runtime with a secure WASM tool sandbox.\"\n- Location: workspace root is /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack\n- The prompt file is at /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/8cc21757-c15/agpack-step5-metered-prompt.md \u2014 OUTSIDE workspace root, so cannot be read by the assistant.\n- Project state: Step 4 done, full suite 231 passed. Step 5 (metered access) is the next build.\n- pydantic 2.13.4 available, /usr/bin/python\n- No runtime deps yet.\n- .gitignore: __pycache__, etc.\n\nNow the NEW conversation since the last compaction:\n\nThe assistant wrote `src/agpack/tools/metered.py` (612 lines). Then did smoke tests. Found a critical bug: `MeterLedger` raised `TypeError: ''NoneType'' object is not callable` when constructed. Traced it down:\n- Line 299: `field(default_factory=None)` \u2014 the dataclass codegen called `None()`. Intent was to default `_balance` to `initial`.\n- Line 396: `succeeded=succeeded` \u2014 but `LedgerEntry`''s field is `success`, so this would raise `TypeError` on any real call.\n\nFixed both with `replace_in_file`.\n\nThen re-ran smoke test. Found my own counting assumptions were wrong (not the code):\n- fetch(3) + read(1) = 6 spent, boom raised without deducting, then 6 ticks exhaust it. call_count=8 successes, 9 total entries (1 failed).\n- The `InsufficientFuel` attribute is `available`, not `remaining` \u2014 my test was wrong.\n\nThen looked at existing test style:\n- Read pyproject.toml (43 lines) \u2014 pydantic 2.13.4, requires-python >=3.11\n- Read src/agpack/tools/__init__.py (15 lines) \u2014 \"Step 5 \u2014 built-in tool adapters... metered \u2014 the pay-per-tool-call adapter (the metered-web broker, folded in as a first-class scope). See metered.py.\"\n- Listed tests directory.\n- Read tests/test_sandbox_limits.py (60 lines) for style.\n\nThen wrote tests/test_metered_access.py. Fixed several mistakes:\n- Bogus `MeterBroker` import, broken `lambda _(_):`, misnamed test.\n- `test_tool_preserves_exception_type` had parse-time error.\n- `test_tool_check_is_fuel_before_call` called `tool.call()` which would raise \u2014 needs wrapping.\n- `test_settlement_property_invariant_fails_on_drift` badly designed.\n\nRan pytest: 35 passed, 9 failed. Analyzed:\n- Real source bug: `MeterLedger.__post_init__` rebalances `_balance` to `initial` on every construction... no. The real source issue: `MeteredTool.call` guard raises `InsufficientFuel` before recording a non-billed entry. But `LedgerEntry` docstring states \"A call that was rejected for insufficient fuel... is recorded with success=False\", and the module says \"every metered dispatch appends... a record\". The exception path records non-billed entries, but the guard path doesn''t \u2014 inconsistent with documented contract. That''s why `len(b.ledger.entries)==1` fails on the guard path.\n\nFixed the real source gap \u2014 made the guard record the non-billed entry.\n\nRan pytest again. 4 failures remain, all unguarded `.call()` invocations in the test. Let me fix each with proper try/except. First line 576...\n\nThe last command shows `replace_in_file` on `test_metered_access.py` replacing a section around a `def boom(_): raise ValueError(\"boom\")` with try/except wrapper. The output was cut off (truncated at \"\u2026\").\n\nSo the current state:\n- The assistant is in the middle of fixing test-writing bugs in `tests/test_metered_access.py`.\n- Last fix applied: wrapped an unguarded `.call(\"z\")` in try/except around a `boom` tool.\n- There are still 4 failures remaining to fix (the assistant said \"First line 576\" implying there are more to fix).\n\nWait, let me re-read. The last message sequence:\n- Assistant: \"4 failures remain, all unguarded `.call()` invocations in my test. Let me fix each with proper try/except. First line 576:\"\n- Then `replace_in_file` on test_metered_access.py wrapping boom call in try/except. Output cut off.\n\nSo we''re in the middle of fixing test bugs. The next step would be to fix the remaining 3 unguarded calls and re-run pytest, then run the full suite.\n\nLet me note the details of the failures found:\n- test_insufficient_fuel_payload \u2014 real source bug (guard path didn''t record non-billed entry) \u2014 FIXED\n- test_exhaustion_when_mixed_with_failures_keeps_count \u2014 test bug (unguarded .call)\n- test_broker_call_count_excludes_failed_calls \u2014 test bug\n- test_settlement_property_invariant_fails_on_drift \u2014 test bug (wrong drift field)\n- test_tool_check_is_fuel_before_call \u2014 test bug\n- test_tool_preserves_exception_type \u2014 test bug (parse-time error lambda _(_))\n- test_invariant_holds_every_step_of_the_way \u2014 test bug (unguarded .call)\n\nNow let me also note the important code details:\n\n**metered.py structure (612 lines):**\n- Class `InsufficientFuel(Exception)` at line 104 \u2014 has attribute `available` (not `remaining`)\n- Class `InvariantError(AssertionError)` at line 124\n- `_nonneg_int` at line 136 \u2014 mirrors sandbox.limits._nonneg_int, rejects bool\n- `Fuel` at line 159\n- `CostPolicy` at line 207\n- `LedgerEntry` at line 257 \u2014 field is `success` (not `succeeded`)\n- `MeterLedger` at line 279\n- `MeteredTool` at line 419 \u2014 `@final`\n- `MeteredBroker` at line 520\n- Also exports: `Receipt`, `Settlement`\n\n**Key API surface:**\n- `MeteredBroker(initial_fuel=..., costs={...})`\n- `broker.tool(callable, tool_id=...)` returns `MeteredTool`\n- `tool.call(*args)` \n- `broker.ledger.remaining`, `broker.ledger.entries`\n- `broker.call_count` \u2014 excludes failed calls\n- `broker.assert_invariant()`\n- `broker.reconcile()` returns a `Settlement`\n- `InsufficientFuel` has `.tool_id`, `.cost`, `.available`\n- `Settlement.invariant_holds` compares `total_charged` against sum of successful receipt costs\n- `CostPolicy({name: cost}, default_cost)`, `.price(name)`\n- `Fuel(amount)`\n- `LedgerEntry(success, tool_id, cost, balance_after, index)`\n\n**Tests written (tests/test_metered_access.py, ~599 lines):**\n- Covers: Fuel, CostPolicy, LedgerEntry, MeterLedger, MeteredTool, MeteredBroker, Receipt, Settlement\n- Required tests: 25+ including success-count assertions, invariant, exception-undeduct\n\n**Important decisions:**\n- The guard path now records a non-billed `LedgerEntry` with `success=False` for insufficient-fuel rejects (matches documented contract).\n- Package importable via `PYTHONPATH=src` or pytest''s pythonpath config in pyproject.toml.\n\n**Constraints from prompt:**\n- stdlib + pydantic only (no real broker, no runtime deps)\n- Faithfulness guards: real proofs not stubs\n- 25+ tests\n- Include honest caveat about what in-process metering models vs. real billing broker\n- Don''t overclaim (learned from Step 4 WASM gap)\n\nNow let me think about what''s still pending:\n1. Fix remaining test bugs (3-4 unguarded .call invocations)\n2. Run the metered test file to confirm all pass\n3. Run the FULL suite to confirm it''s still 231+ passed (no regression)\n4. The caveat section (honest question about what this in-process metering models vs. a real pay-per-call/billing broker) \u2014 likely a report, following Step 4 WASM gap pattern\n\nLet me also note the file read details so I can preserve:\n- metered.py line 104-135: InsufficientFuel docstring\n- metered.py line 45-104: module API surface docstring\n- metered.py line 1-45: module docstring + first part\n- metered.py line 136-257: Fuel, CostPolicy, _nonneg_int\n- metered.py line 257-286: LedgerEntry start\n- metered.py line 257-416: LedgerEntry, MeterLedger\n- metered.py line 415-612: MeteredTool, MeteredBroker\n\nNow let me structure the summary.\n\nFor the \"All user messages\" section \u2014 there''s really only one user message in this whole conversation (the one at the top describing the Step 5 prompt). Everything else is the assistant''s own tool calls and internal reasoning shown in the [previous compaction summary]. So the user message is the big one describing the prompt.\n\nWait, but the task is to summarize \"the conversation below\". The conversation below includes the [previous compaction summary] and then the new tool calls. The actual user message is just the one describing the prompt. The rest is assistant self-generated tool calls.\n\nActually, looking again \u2014 the [previous compaction summary] was provided by the user as context to fold in. Then there''s the new conversation which is all assistant tool calls (no new user messages). So the \"All user messages\" section should list the one user message about the prompt.\n\nLet me write the summary now.\n\nFor artifacts:\n- src/agpack/tools/metered.py \u2014 the main deliverable, 612 lines, just implemented and being verified. Modified multiple times (bug fixes).\n- tests/test_metered_access.py \u2014 test file, ~599 lines, being debugged.\n- Files read: pyproject.toml, src/agpack/tools/__init__.py, tests/test_sa