th todo is very likely a final verification step like \"Verify all docs/API examples match the real code (run example, re-run tests).\"\n\nLet me not fabricate. I''ll state it''s cut off but likely a final verification/finalize task.\n\n**Where did we stop?**\nThe last actions were reading host.py (lines 71-125, 126-255, 257-386) and imports.py (1-90). The assistant''s stated intent: \"I need the sandbox host''s RuntimeDriver/Instance/BundleFileReader protocol shapes precisely, so my example wasmtime driver is a drop-in match.\" Then reading imports.py to check `build_imports` output shape so the wasmtime example''s import surface is correct.\n\nSo the CURRENT work is: writing the real-engine migration guide, specifically the wasmtime RuntimeDriver example that needs the host protocol shapes (RuntimeDriver, Instance, BundleFileReader) and the imports surface from imports.py.\n\nThe most recent read was imports.py 1-90, which I have content for. It shows:\n- Host imports \u2014 the surface the guest module can call\n- Mapping from WAT/WASM import namespace to Python callable\n- This is the only door between guest and host\n- v0 imports only sandbox.capabilities, sandbox.limits, sandbox.imports\n\nThe assistant''s last words before the cut: \"Let me check `build_imports` output shape so the wasmtime example''s import surface is correct.\" \u2014 and imports.py content shows line 1-90 of the module docstring and start.\n\nSo the next step is: continue reading imports.py to get the `build_imports` output shape, then write the migration guide with the wasmtime RuntimeDriver + tar.gz BundleFileReader examples.\n\nLet me also note important domain facts:\n- `compile_exports(bytes)` executes tool source bytes in isolated namespace, returns exports (dict[str, Callable[[bytes], bytes]])\n- proof.py `run(data)` function: sum/count over JSON list of integers\n- RuntimeDriver protocol in driver.py\n- Instance protocol in host.py with: `name`, `peak_memory_pages`, etc.\n- BundleFileReader protocol in host.py with: read_wasm_bytes(tool_cid), declared_imports(tool_cid), get_entry_export(tool_cid), agent_id()\n\n**Host.py protocol methods:**\n- BundleFileReader: read_wasm_bytes(tool_cid) -> bytes, declared_imports(tool_cid) -> Sequence[str], get_entry_export(tool_cid) -> str | None, agent_id() -> str\n- RuntimeDriver: (protocol) \u2014 methods to instantiate a module\n- Instance: methods like `call`, `peak_memory_pages`, `name`\n\nLet me look at what I have. From the grep:\n- 122: read_wasm_bytes(self, tool_cid: str) -> bytes\n- 124: declared_imports(self, tool_cid: str) -> Sequence[str]\n- 126: get_entry_export(self, tool_cid: str) -> str | None\n- 128: agent_id(self) -> str\n\nAnd Instance protocol methods. The grep for Instance showed matches but the content cut off. I have from read of 126-255 showing Instance(Protocol) docstring starting.\n\nLet me now think about what the tool_cid format is: `tool/{stem}`. And imports come from declared_imports; entry export from sidecar.\n\n**Path context:**\n- Repo root: /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack\n- Source: /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack/src/agpack/\n- PYTHONPATH=src python ... used to run\n\n**Key technical note:** WASM engine (wasmtime) is NOT yet implemented. Drivers execute plain-Python tool source. The migration guide is about how to ADD real engines (wasmtime) as a RuntimeDriver. This is the \"migration story to real engines\" deliverable.\n\n**Makefile targets** (from prior): install, dev, test, lint, typecheck, format, bundle-verify, clean\n\nNow let me also note the .scratch files that exist:\n- .scratch/agpack (shadowing dir)\n- .scratch/plan.md\n- .scratch/probe_bind.py\n- .scratch/probe_contract.py\n- .scratch/probe_readable.py\n- .scratch/run/probe.py (copy of probe_readable.py)\n\nAnd there were other probes: probe_bind.py, probe_contract.py (mentioned in ls output).\n\nThe plan.md is in .scratch/ \u2014 let me note it exists but I don''t have its content in this 