INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('563e55d1-62a','/home/iconbaypark2900/jabCreative/dataScience/concordCircuit','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','P1 — Persona. ConcordCircuit composes the 3 read-only pillar','builder',158,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'ConcordCircuit Phase 0-3 read-only pillars',0,'2026-08-31 23:19:44','{}','{"boundary_index": 82, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me understand the situation. The user (compact AI coworker) is trying to work on the ConcordCircuit project. This is the beginning of the session \u2014 the workspace was empty, and I''ve been building out the `concord/` package.\n\nLet me review the conversation carefully to build the structured summary.\n\nThe user''s message is actually a single \"user\" turn that contains a bunch of tool results and assistant actions. Wait, let me re-read. The actual user message is:\n\n\"[user] P1 \u2014 Persona. ConcordCircuit composes the 3 read-only pillars under a new concord/ package; states the invariant, the STUB-vs-REAL reality checks, and the real importable code.\nP2 \u2014 Phase 0 (pure-math ERC-4626). The concord runtime that replaces the agpack CLI stub, the JSONL audit store to the exact LedgerCorrupt 4-record contract (verified from audit.py), the deterministic 140-partner / 5-chain corpus where attribution is by share (totalShares/totalShares \u00d7 totalAssets), the sum == delta to-the-wei invariant, and the 4 verify commands \u2014 all egress zero.\nP3 \u2014 the drift seed. Two by-construction anomalies (chain-3 Aave 0.0375 USDC gap, partner 117 rounding skew) fed into a reconciliation check written now, so Phase 1 has real drift to catch before it exists. reconcile exits clean on the base, exits non-zero on the seed.\"\n\nWait, that''s actually a task specification given by the user. This is the primary request. Let me treat that as the primary request.\n\nThen there''s a series of assistant actions and tool results. Let me parse through them carefully.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the format is:\n- [user] \u2014 the task spec (P1, P2, P3)\n- [assistant \u2192 brain_recall] \u2014 recall query\n- [assistant \u2192 list_files] \u2014 list files\n- [assistant] \u2014 text\n- [tool result] \u2014 results\n- etc.\n\nSo the \"user messages\" section should just be the P1/P2/P3 spec. The rest is assistant tool calls.\n\nWait, but the task says \"All user messages \u2014 a chronological list of every user message\". In this case, there''s really only one user message: the P1/P2/P3 spec. The rest is all assistant actions and tool results.\n\nLet me carefully trace through what happened:\n\n1. User gives the task: P1 (Persona/Composition), P2 (Phase 0), P3 (drift seed).\n\n2. Assistant starts:\n   - brain_recall query for ConcordCircuit project structure\n   - list_files returns [] (empty)\n   - assistant realizes list_files swallowed\n   - run_shell pwd; ls -la \u2192 workspace concordCircuit is empty\n   - assistant notes design docs live outside workspace\n   - list_files again empty\n   - run_shell ls on consortium-agent, agpack, metered-web-broker \u2192 consortium-agent has content\n   - read_file on DESIGN.md \u2192 path escapes workspace\n   - read_file on audit.py \u2192 path escapes workspace\n   - assistant decides to read via shell\n   - head DESIGN.md, sed audit.py \u2192 read successfully\n   - sed audit.py 200-420, sed PHASES.md \u2192 read\n   - sed audit.py 200-420, sed PHASES.md 1-120 \u2192 read\n   - sed REUSE.md, sed PHASES.md 120-320 \u2192 read\n   - assistant notes it has complete picture of design and audit contract\n   - todo_write: 5 todos set up\n   - run_shell find agpack src\n   - run_shell find sentinel\n   - run_shell python version check in agpack venv\n   - find sentinel, openworker-tasks root\n   - python import agpack test\n   - ls sentinel-local, metered layout\n   - pro