INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-e27d165427','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Apply — file the shortlist','cowork',142,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 20:43:22','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "browser_click", "browser_close", "browser_get_text", "browser_open_url", "browser_read_url", "browser_screenshot", "browser_select", "browser_snapshot", "browser_submit", "browser_type", "browser_upload_file", "browser_wait", "grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 94, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation and produce the structured summary as required.\n\nThe task is a scheduled \"Apply\" run. The user (via an automated scheduled run prompt) asked the AI to file job applications that have been shortlisted. Let me identify all the key elements.\n\nLet me trace through:\n\n**Primary request and intent:**\n- Scheduled run to file (apply to) job/grant applications that have been shortlisted by other automations\n- Do NOT create or modify scheduled tasks (schedule already exists)\n- File applications using staged files in workspace\n- Constraints: never use run_shell, ls, cat, curl, or Python script\n- Must write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md as final action every time, even if everything blocked\n- Hard rule on unknown fields: don''t answer questions not in facts.md/resume.txt; park them\n- Never invent answers for legal documents (work authorization, salary, education, background check)\n- Never TODO in facts.md as permission to improvise\n- Park on login walls, CAPTCHA, government ID/SSN/DOB/bank details, etc.\n- Never create accounts\n- For grants: don''t attempt NSF/DOE/NIH/SBIR (need SAM.gov, UEI); only fellowships/residencies/accelerators/private foundations via web form\n\n**Key concepts and decisions:**\n- The automation pipeline: job automation \u2192 shortlist (targets.md) \u2192 cover letters/resume tweaks (drafts/) \u2192 this apply run files them\n- ATS types: Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday\n- The tricky browser dynamics\n- Facts.md as the \"answer bank\"\n- Ledger.md continuity \u2014 never double-apply\n\n**Continuity findings from ledger.md:**\n- Sprinter Health = sent (skip)\n- ERA:AI = \"do not re-attempt\" (skip)\n- Hyro = closed (skip)\n\n**The 6 fresh ON-FOCUS jobs from targets.md:**\n1. Valtech \u2014 Forward Deployed Engineer, Google Cloud, AI Expert\n2. Further \u2014 Senior AI Engineer (via Miragely)\n3. Stellar Consulting \u2014 Senior AI Engineer\n4. ICONMA \u2014 Agentic AI / AI Engineer (via Workflowza)\n5. Bybit \u2014 Senior Recommendation / Growth ML Engineer\n6. GCP Engineer \u2014 Senior GCP Engineer: AI Platforms & Development (via Flexsenior) \u2192 actually Concentrix\n\n**Actions taken:**\n- Listed files\n- Read FOCUS.md, ledger.md, applied-2026-09-01.md\n- Read targets.md, facts.md, resume-path.txt\n- grep for URLs\n- Read cover-letter drafts (Valtech, Further, Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit, GCP Engineer)\n- Read resume-tweaks (Valtech, ICONMA, Bybit)\n- Read grants.md\n- Web searches to find ATS links\n- Found Valtech and Further Greenhouse links\n- Opened Valtech Greenhouse board \u2014 posting closed (only Forward Deployed Product Manager remains), marked as skipped\n- Opened Further Greenhouse form \u2014 started filling it\n\n**Current state at end:**\n- Further application form, Greenhouse, comboboxes not resolving (country, years-of-experience, sponsorship)\n- Was trying to click #question_35188043002 (the 12+ years question)\n- Need to see options for legally-sensitive sponsorship question\n- The run is NOT finished \u2014 no applied-2026-09-02.md written\n\nWait \u2014 what''s today''s date? The prior run was applied-2026-09-01.md. The targets.md is 2026-09-01. Let me think about what date to use for the output file. The system prompt says apply-YYYY-MM-DD.md. The task is being run presumably on 2026-09-01 still or 2026-09-02. Actually the prompt references \"today''s shortlist\" in targets.md dated 2026-09-01. The continuation run... Let me note that the filename should be applied-2026-09-XX.md but I should flag the date determination.\n\nActually, looking carefully, the previous file is applied-2026-09-01.md. This appears to be a continuation/later run on the same day or next day. I should note the date question. Let me use 2026-09-01 as the likely date since that''s the current run date, but I''ll flag it.\n\nActually, I shouldn''t fabricate. Let me note the applied file needs today''s date, which I should confirm. Given the context (targets dated 2026-09-01, prior applied file 2026-09-01), I''ll note 2026-09-01 as the working date but flag it needs confirmation if this is a different day.\n\nHmm, actually the prompt for the current run doesn''t state the date. Let me just flag that the applied file date needs to be set to today''s date, and I''ll tentatively use 2026-09-01.\n\n**Key browser technique learnings (errors and fixes):**\n- Greenhouse comboboxes (#question_..., #country) are react-comboboxes (role=combobox), NOT native <select>. browser_select fails on them. Must click then select from dynamic option list, but option lists aren''t appearing in snapshots.\n- Need to wait 3-4s after navigation\n- \"Apply for this Job\" button click then snapshot\n- resume upload is input type=file, target input directly\n- browser_submit for send buttons\n\n**Facts.md details:**\n- Email: jonaston015@gmail.com\n- Phone: (954) 494-0671\n- LinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale\n- Location: Fort Lauderdale\n- Candidate: Jonathan Beale\n- ~2.5 years production ML\n- EEO/ demographic: decline to self-identify\n\nLet me now write the structured summary.\n\nLet me be careful about the exact paths. The workspace is:\n/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51/\n\nFiles:\n- FOCUS.md\n- ledger.md\n- applied-2026-09-01.md\n- targets.md\n- facts.md\n- resume.txt (read? Not explicitly, only resume-path.txt. Actually resume.txt was listed in the todo but I see read_file only for targets.md, facts.md, resume-path.txt. Let me check... The assistant read targets.md, facts.md, resume-path.txt. resume.txt wasn''t explicitly read via tool result shown, but the drafts reference resume content. Actually the todo said read resume.txt but I don''t see it executed. Let me note it may not have been read. Actually the grep used glob *.md so resume.txt wouldn''t be caught. Let me note resume.txt content is referenced but may not have been directly read.)\n\nDrafts:\n- drafts/cover-letter-Valtech.md\n- drafts/cover-letter-Further.md\n- drafts/cover-letter-Stellar.md\n- drafts/cover-letter-ICONMA.md\n- drafts/cover-letter-Bybit.md\n- drafts/cover-letter-GCPEngineer.md\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Valtech.md\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-ICONMA.md\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Bybit.md\n- (others exist per file listing but not all read)\n\n- grants.md\n- resume-path.txt \u2192 /home/iconbaypark2900/Documents/Jonathan_Beale_Resume_2026.pdf\n\nATS links found:\n- Valtech: https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/valtech/jobs/4878748101 (but the specific FDE posting is closed \u2014 only Forward Deployed Product Manager remains)\n- Further: https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002\n\nNote: the web search result showed Valtech LinkedIn and Further Greenhouse. The assistant opened https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/valtech/jobs/4878748101 which errored, then opened the board. Actually the job id 4878748101 \u2014 the search result was a LinkedIn link. The assistant may have guessed the greenhouse URL. Anyway, Valtech FDE posting is closed.\n\n- Bybit: https://job-boards.eu.greenhouse.io/bybit (board exists, specific job id not found)\n\nNow let me write the summary.\n\nLet me also note the key decision: the assistant decided NOT to fabricate the 12+ years and would fill years screener truthfully (~2.5 years per facts.md), flag the gap for user decision at the tap. But the run ended before resolving the combobox.\n\nActually, I need to re-examine \u2014 the assistant''s internal monologue got somewhat confused but the key actionable state is:\n- Further form opened, identity + contact mostly filled (name, email, phone, location, LinkedIn, country via combobox)\n- Comboboxes for country, years-of-experience (#question_35188043002), sponsorship (#question_35188042002 area) not resolving\n- Sponsorship is legally sensitive \u2014 need to see options\n\nLet me note the exact field targets:\n- #first_name, #last_name, #preferred_name, #email, #country, #phone, #question_35188042002 (LinkedIn), #candidate-location, #question_35188043002 (12+ years?)\n\nWait, #question_35188042002 was used for LinkedIn? Let me recheck. \n\n```\nbrowser_type {\"clear\": true, \"target\": \"#question_35188042002\", \"text\": \"https://linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale\"}\n```\nYes LinkedIn was #question_35188042002.\n\nThen:\n```\nbrowser_click {\"target\": \"#question_35188043002\"}  -- the 12+ years question\n```\nSo #question_35188043002 is the years-of-experience question.\n\nAnd #country is country combobox.\n\nOK.\n\nNow pending tasks:\n1. Resolve Further form (comboboxes: country, years-of-experience, sponsorship) \u2014 the legally-sensitive sponsorship especially\n2. File remaining 5 (well, Valtech closed/skipped; so Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit, GCP Engineer/Concentrix) \u2014 but none have confirmed direct ATS links except maybe Bybit board\n3. Find direct ATS links for Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit (specific job), Concentrix GCP Engineer\n4. Write applied-2026-09-01.md (or correct date)\n5. Append rows to ledger.md\n\nLet me now think about the date. I''ll flag that the applied file date should be today''s date; the most recent applied file is 2026-09-01, targets dated 2026-09-01. Given it''s a continuation, today is likely 2026-09-01. But I''ll note to confirm current date. Actually the safest is to note \"applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md \u2014 set YYYY-MM-DD to today; tentatively 2026-09-01.\"\n\nNow let me write it all out concisely but completely.\n\nFor \"All user messages\" \u2014 there''s really only one user message: the big scheduled run prompt. The assistant''s todo writes and tool results aren''t user messages. The only actual user message is the scheduled run instruction block. Let me include that, trimmed.\n\nLet me write the summary now.\n\nI need to be careful with the \"Artifacts and files\" \u2014 note what was read vs edited. Nothing was created yet (no applied-*.md written, no ledger appended). So files read: list. Files to create: applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md (final), ledger.md rows appended.\n\nLet me draft.\n\nFor the resume-upload note: The Further form has resume + cover-letter FILE uploads. The cover letter drafts are in markdown (.md), not as a .docx or plain text file the form could take. Per the rules: \"If it wants a file and only the markdown exists, say so in the output and treat the application as blocked.\" This is important for the output later. Actually wait \u2014 Greenhouse allows paste or file. Let me note that cover letters exist only as markdown, which may block cover-letter filing or require paste. The assistant didn''t resolve this yet. Flag it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider \u2014 Greenhouse often has a \"Cover Letter\" field that accepts paste OR a file upload. The assistant noted \"resume + cover-letter file uploads.\" If it''s a file upload only, then markdown-only is a blocker. This is a pending decision. I''ll flag it.\n\nLet me write.\n\nOne more: facts.md EEO = decline to self-identify. Good.\n\nLet me also capture the FOCUS.md content briefly: focus on agpack build, the live center of gravity. Actually FOCUS.md is about project focus (agpack), not directly job focus, but it''s referenced for ON-FOCUS ranking. The assistant read it. I''ll note it''s the week''s focus doc referencing agpack as the build of the week \u2014 but its role here is \"prefer ON-FOCUS targets.\" I''ll keep it brief.\n\nNow writing the final summary", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: browser_click, browser_open_url, browser_select, browser_snapshot, browser_type, browser_wait, grep, list_files, read_file, todo_write, web_search", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Apply \u2014 file the shortlist This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. File the applications the job and grant automations have already shortlisted. The discovery side of this pipeline works \u2014 eighteen runs of shortlists and tailored drafts. What it has never produced is a sent application. That is this job: take what is already researched and drafted, and put it into the employer''s form. Everything you need is staged in your own workspace by plain filename\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788292298.624311, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
