INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-1b8854d2a3','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Apply — file the shortlist','cowork',157,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 21:29:27','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "browser_click", "browser_close", "browser_get_text", "browser_open_url", "browser_read_url", "browser_screenshot", "browser_select", "browser_snapshot", "browser_submit", "browser_type", "browser_upload_file", "browser_wait", "grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 91, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation to produce a structured summary. This is an automated \"Apply\" run for a job/grant application pipeline. The AI coworker is executing a scheduled run to file one application into an ATS (Applicant Tracking System).\n\nLet me work through the sections required.\n\n**Context:**\n- This is a \"Scheduled run \u2014 Apply \u2014 file the shortlist\" automation.\n- Workspace: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51`\n- Candidate: Jonathan Beale\n- The task is to file EXACTLY ONE application per run \u2014 the highest-priority target from targets.md not already in ledger.md.\n\n**What happened so far:**\n1. The coworker read FOCUS.md, ledger.md, applied-2026-09-01.md, targets.md, facts.md, resume.txt, resume-path.txt, drafts/cover-letter-Further.md, drafts/resume-tweaks-Further.md.\n2. Determined that the top pick is Further (via Miragely) \u2014 Senior AI Engineer. Wait, actually the earlier runs covered ERA:AI (skipped), Sprinter (sent), Hyro (skipped), and Valtech (closed). So the next pick is Further.\n3. Set up todos.\n4. Found the direct Further apply link: `https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002` (Greenhouse board, real ATS).\n5. Opened the page, waited 4s, snapshotted.\n6. Filled text fields: First Name (Jonathan), Last Name (Beale), Preferred Name (Jonathan), Email, Phone, LinkedIn.\n7. Uploaded resume via `browser_upload_file` with `#resume` target.\n8. Target salary field: `#question_35188044002` = \"$100,000+, negotiable for the right role\".\n9. Then got stuck on the comboboxes \u2014 Country, Years of Experience, Sponsorship, Relocation, consent questions. The Greenhouse React combobox flyouts aren''t captured by browser_snapshot, browser_get_text, or the screenshot tool (media file access denied because /tmp is outside allowed dirs).\n\n**The key technical problem now:**\nThe Greenhouse comboboxes are React comboboxes (`[role=combobox]`), and their flyout option lists are not exposed to the accessibility tree \u2014 so browser_snapshot, browser_get_text, and browser_screenshot all fail to reveal the options. The coworker has been trying various approaches:\n- Clicking the combobox\n- Type-ahead typing (\"United States\" persisted in Country)\n- Clicking \"Toggle flyout\" buttons\n- browser_get_text (fails)\n- Inspecting page structure (attempted but snapshot didn''t show the flyout)\n\nThe last message shows the coworker is still struggling with the comboboxes. The most recent action was clicking `#question_35188043002` (which is likely the \"Years of Experience\" field), and then snapshot showed nothing new.\n\n**Important rules to preserve:**\n- ONE target per run, then log and stop.\n- Hard wall-clock limit: ~6 minutes before giving up on a control.\n- If a control fails twice, record blocked, name the field, move on.\n- Don''t answer unknown fields (park instead of guess).\n- browser_submit pauses for the user (that means \"parked\").\n- browser_click refuses \"Submit\"/\"Send\" buttons \u2014 use browser_submit.\n- Never use run_shell, ls, cat, curl, Python script.\n- Write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md as final action, always.\n- The output file and ledger append are REQUIRED.\n\n**The screenshot path issue:** `/tmp/coworker-browser-screenshot.png` was denied because it''s outside allowed directories (`/data/home/dcode-stack`, `/data/home/LibreChat`, `/data/home/liaison-agent`). This is an error/fix to note.\n\nNow let me think about what the current state is. The run is ongoing. The coworker has hit the combobox problem and hasn''t submitted. Given the 6-minute limit and the \"if the same control fails twice, stop trying\" rule, the coworker may be at risk of hitting the wall. But at the moment of this summary, the run is still in progress \u2014 the coworker is mid-way through trying to drive the Greenhouse comboboxes.\n\nLet me now write the summary.\n\nLet me note the key facts:\n- Candidate: Jonathan Beale\n- Resume PDF: `/home/iconbaypark2900/Documents/Jonathan_Beale_Resume_2026.pdf`\n- Resume text: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51/resume.txt`\n- facts.md: answer bank\n- targets.md: 2026-09-01 PM shortlist, 6 ON-FOCUS roles\n- FOCUS.md: focus doc\n- ledger.md: application ledger (was empty before earlier runs today, now has 4 rows)\n- applied-2026-09-01.md: earlier run''s output (already has entries from morning + PM runs)\n- drafts/cover-letter-Further.md\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Further.md\n\nKey facts from resume.txt:\n- Jonathan Beale, Fort Lauderdale, FL\n- jonaston015@gmail.com\n- (954) 494-0671\n- linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale\n- github.com/iconbaypark2900\n- 2.5 years ML engineering, GCP, etc.\n\nKey facts from facts.md \u2014 need to note the \"decline to self-identify\" default.\n\nThe Greenhouse job URL: `https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002`\n\nLet me recall the field selectors used:\n- `#first_name`, `#last_name`, `#preferred_name`, `#email`, `#phone`, `#question_35188042002` (LinkedIn), `#resume`, `#question_35188044002` (target salary), `#country`, `#question_35188045002` (sponsorship), `#question_35188043002` (years of experience)\n\nWait, let me re-read. The LinkedIn was `#question_35188042002` = \"https://linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale\". Target salary `#question_35188044002` = \"$100,000+, negotiable for the right role\". Sponsorship `#question_35188045002`. Years of experience `#question_35188043002`.\n\nActually, let me double check: The last click was on `#question_35188043002`. Earlier there was `#question_35188045002` which was typed \"No\" then cleared with \"\". Let me re-read.\n\nReading carefully:\n- `#question_35188045002` was typed \"No\" for sponsorship\n- Then `#question_35188045002` was typed \"\" (cleared) \u2014 \"browser_type {\"target\": \"#question_35188045002\", \"text\": \"\"}\"\n- Then click `#question_35188043002` \u2014 this is the combobox being inspected.\n\nHmm, actually the order: sponsorship was `#question_35188045002`. Let me not over-specify which exact field is which since I''m not 100% certain of the mapping for all the question_ fields. But I''ll note the ones I''m confident about.\n\nActually let me reconsider. The user said sponsorship must be \"No\". The field `#question_35188045002` was typed \"No\" and then cleared \"\". That''s a bit odd \u2014 maybe the coworker realized it wasn''t working and cleared it. Actually, looking again \u2014 the coworker typed \"No\", then cleared it, then was trying to inspect the page structure. So sponsorship state is uncertain.\n\nLet me focus on what I can reliably state.\n\n**Comboboxes remaining to fill:** Country (persisted \"United States\"), Years of Experience, Sponsorship (should be \"No\"), Relocation, and consent questions (privacy notice consent, data-disclosure consent, near-office).\n\nAlso pending:\n- Cover letter \u2014 Greenhouse form had an optional Cover Letter \"Enter manually\" box. The tailored draft needs to go in.\n- EEO/demographic fields \u2014 decline to self-identify per facts.md.\n- Re-verify and submit.\n\n**Errors and fixes:**\n- The screenshot file `/tmp/coworker-browser-screenshot.png` access denied \u2014 outside allowed dirs. Fix: noted, tried alternate approaches (browser_get_text). Still stuck on combobox flyouts.\n\n**The core unsolved problem:** Greenhouse React combobox flyouts (`[role=combobox]`) aren''t captured by browser_snapshot, browser_get_text, browser_screenshot, or the \"Toggle flyout\" buttons. The options list is `aria-hidden`. This is the active blocker.\n\nNow, the \"hard rule\" about wall-clock: ~6 minutes. And \"if the same control fails twice, stop.\" The coworker is still trying, so it hasn''t given up. But it''s at risk.\n\nFor the summary''s \"Current work\" \u2014 the coworker is actively trying to drive the Greenhouse React comboboxes for the Senior AI Engineer role at Further. Specifically, the most recent action was clicking `#question_35188043002` and snapshotting (nothing new appeared).\n\n\"Next step\" \u2014 need to find a way to drive the combobox options. Options: browser_snapshot may not capture aria-hidden flyouts. The instructions say to click the combobox, snapshot to read options, click option by visible text. But the snapshot isn''t showing options. The coworker needs to either find another way to read the options (maybe the flyout options are reachable via snapshot with a different target, or the type-ahead approach where typing filters and the field value updates) or, if truly blocked after 2 attempts, record the specific field as blocked and either move to submit-with-partial (not allowed \u2014 required fields) or, given the wall-clock, mark blocked and write output.\n\nActually \u2014 the critical thing: many required combobox fields are still unfilled (Years of Experience, Sponsorship, Relocation, consent checkboxes). Without those, the form can''t be submitted. So if the combobox problem persists, the run should be marked blocked per the rules (record reason, write applied file, append ledger as blocked, end run). But the run isn''t finished yet.\n\nFor next step: try to reveal the flyout options another way. One idea: the instructions say to snapshot after clicking \u2014 maybe need to click the field to focus, then the options should appear in snapshot. But that''s been tried. Alternatively use browser_type to type-ahead and rely on the field value persisting (Country worked that way \u2014 \"United States\" persisted). The coworker could try typing the option text for each combobox and verify the value persists in the field, then proceed.\n\nLet me write this concisely.\n\nLet me make sure I capture the standing constraints:\n- Do NOT use run_shell, ls, cat, curl, Python script (shell stops the run).\n- Do NOT create or modify scheduled tasks.\n- Write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md as final action every run, even if all blocked.\n- ONE target per run then stop.\n- Never use browser_click on \"Submit\"/\"Send\"/\"Finish\" \u2014 use browser_submit.\n- browser_submit pauses for user = parked (good outcome).\n- Don''t answer unknown fields \u2014 park/record.\n- Never create accounts, never invent passwords.\n- ~6 minute wall clock; if control fails twice, stop and record.\n\nLet me also note: this run is on 2026-09-01 (based on applied-2026-09-01.md already existing from earlier runs today). So output file is `applied-2026-09-01.md` (append/update).\n\nWait \u2014 there''s already an applied-2026-09-01.md from earlier runs today. The continuation rule says read the 1-2 most recent applied-*.md. So this run updates/appends to applied-2026-09-01.md.\n\nLet me write the summary now.\n\nFor user messages \u2014 this is a scheduled run, so the \"user\" is actually the scheduler/driver. The only user message is the big instruction block at the start. I should note it as a single user message (the system/scheduled prompt). Let me list it.\n\nActually the task says \"All user messages \u2014 a chronological list of every user message\". Here there''s just one initial user message (the big run prompt). I''ll list it.\n\nLet me write everything out now.\n\nLet me be concrete and precise.\n\nFor the excerpt of load-bearing content, I''ll pull key quotes.\n\nLet me draft.\n\n---\n\nActually, let me reconsider the field mappings to be accurate:\n\nFrom the turn:\n1. `#first_name` = Jonathan\n2. `#last_name` = Beale\n3.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: browser_click, browser_get_text, browser_open_url, browser_screenshot, browser_snapshot, browser_type, browser_upload_file, browser_wait, grep, list_files, mcp__filesystem__filesystem-read_media_file, read_file, todo_write, web_search", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Apply \u2014 file the shortlist This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. File the applications the job and grant automations have already shortlisted. The discovery side of this pipeline works \u2014 eighteen runs of shortlists and tailored drafts. What it has never produced is a sent application. That is this job: take what is already researched and drafted, and put it into the employer''s form. Everything you need is staged in your own workspace by plain filename\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788297914.186017, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-2e25d033a1','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Apply — file the shortlist','cowork',149,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 21:54:32','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "browser_click", "browser_close", "browser_get_text", "browser_open_url", "browser_read_url", "browser_screenshot", "browser_select", "browser_snapshot", "browser_submit", "browser_type", "browser_upload_file", "browser_wait", "grep", "list_files", "playwright-browser_click", "playwright-browser_close", "playwright-browser_file_upload", "playwright-browser_fill_form", "playwright-browser_find", "playwright-browser_navigate", "playwright-browser_press_key", "playwright-browser_select_option", "playwright-browser_snapshot", "playwright-browser_take_screenshot", "playwright-browser_type", "playwright-browser_wait_for", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 100, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation and produce the structured summary in all 8 required sections.\n\nLet me first understand the context. This is a scheduled \"Apply\" automation run. The assistant is Jonathan Beale''s job/gant application filing automation. The workspace is at `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51`.\n\nThe task is to file exactly ONE application per run \u2014 the highest-priority target from targets.md not already in ledger.md.\n\nLet me extract the key facts:\n\n**Primary request and intent:**\n- Scheduled run \u2014 file the shortlist. Carry out the task immediately and produce the result.\n- Do NOT create or modify scheduled tasks.\n- File applications the job and grant automations already shortlisted.\n- Use file tools and browser tools (playwright MCP). Do NOT use run_shell, ls, cat, curl or Python script.\n- Do NOT narrate \u2014 work, don''t narrate.\n- The run is not finished until `applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md` exists \u2014 write it as final action every time, even if all blocked.\n- Take EXACTLY ONE application per run: highest-priority target from targets.md not already in ledger.md. Do it, log it, stop.\n- Priority order: 1. deadline inside 14 days, 2. highest-ranked ON-FOCUS match with draft in drafts/, 3. next best.\n- Skip ledger.md entries with status `sent` or `parked`.\n- Various hard rules on unknown fields, dropdowns, grants.\n- Stop-and-recind conditions.\n- Write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md with per-attempt details, append row to ledger.md.\n- Continuity first: list files, read ledger.md and 1-2 recent applied-*.md.\n- Read FOCUS.md before choosing what to file.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions:**\n- The candidate is Jonathan Beale \u2014 ML Solutions Architect at Hewani (Apr 2025\u2013Present), former AI/ML Engineer at Mutual of Omaha (Jan 2024\u2013Feb 2025). ~2.5 yrs production ML. No degree.\n- Facts: Jonaston015@gmail.com, (954) 494-0671, Fort Lauderdale FL. LinkedIn linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale, github.com/iconbaypark2900.\n- Resume PDF path: `/home/iconbaypark2900/Documents/Jonathan_Beale_Resume_2026.pdf`\n- The Greenhouse React combobox issue: dropdowns are NOT `<select>`, they are React comboboxes. Country-list trap.\n- browser_submit tool is separately approved \u2014 expects a pause.\n- Playwright MCP tools preferred over built-in browser tools.\n\n**Target chosen:**\n- Further (via Miragely) \u2014 Senior AI Engineer. Ranked #2 in targets.md. Valtech was closed/ledgered so Further is next.\n- Direct URL found: Greenhouse board `https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002`\n\n**Errors and fixes:**\n- Snapshot path error: `/playwright-mcp/...` escapes allowed roots. Fix: used browser_snapshot tool directly instead of reading the snapshot file.\n- ref-based selector engine: `ref=e90` format not recognized \u2014 \"Unknown engine ref while parsing selector\". Fix: used CSS attribute selectors `input[aria-label=''...'']`.\n- browser_fill_form failed with ref target. Fixed using CSS selectors.\n- Combobox clicking timeouts \u2014 used browser_run_code_unsafe with getByRole(''option'', ...) approach.\n- Country-list trap: opened dropdown shows 244 countries. Need to filter by typing.\n- Years of experience: \"Less than 4 years\" clicked successfully.\n\n**Current state at the end:**\n- Working on the phone Country dropdown. Typed \"United States\" to filter. 2 matches: \"United States +1\" and \"United States+1\".\n- Just about to select the right country option.\n\nWait, let me re-check the priority. The task says pick highest-priority target. The assistant chose Further because:\n- targets.md order: Valtech is closed/ledgered so Further #2 is next.\n- But wait \u2014 priority is deadline first. Let me check. The applied-2026-09-01.md mentioned Cambridge ERA:AI Fellowship with deadline 13 Sep 2026 (~12 days). That was from the previous run. \n\nActually, let me re-read. The targets.md is the 2026-09-01 PM shortlist. The assistant determined the priority. Let me not over-specify since I only have partial content. The assistant explicitly chose Further and explained: \"Per the rules: exactly one application per run \u2014 the highest-priority targets.md target not already in ledger.md. ledger.md already has Valtech (closed), so the next-highest ON-FOCUS target with a present draft is Further \u2014 Senior AI Engineer.\"\n\nSo the priority reasoning: deadline first, then highest ON-FOCUS with draft, then next. The assistant determined Further is the highest-priority not-yet-attempted. Actually the assistant said \"the next-highest ON-FOCUS target with a present draft is Further\". Hmm, but that''s priority rule 2. Let me just report what the assistant decided and its stated reasoning, noting that the deadline-first rule would apply if a deadline-target existed. Actually I should be careful \u2014 the assistant''s todo said \"Choose Further (via Miragely) \u2014 Senior AI Engineer (rank #2, not in ledger)\". So it''s ranked #2 in targets.md.\n\n**Files:**\n- Workspace: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51`\n- ledger.md \u2014 application ledger, already had Valtech entry (closed). Empty-ish before prior run.\n- FOCUS.md \u2014 derived focus for week of 2026-08-31. Mentions agpack \"build\".\n- targets.md \u2014 2026-09-01 shortlist. Jonathan Beale candidate.\n- applied-2026-09-01.md \u2014 previous run output, mentions Cambridge ERA:AI Fellowship deadline 13 Sep 2026.\n- resume-path.txt \u2014 `/home/iconbaypark2900/Documents/Jonathan_Beale_Resume_2026.pdf`\n- facts.md \u2014 answer bank. Rule: if answer not here and not on resume, doesn''t answer. TODOs in facts.md are NOT permission to improvise.\n- resume.txt \u2014 extracted resume text.\n- drafts/cover-letter-Further.md \u2014 cover letter for Further.\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Further.md \u2014 resume tweaks for Further.\n- drafts/app-imachines.md and many cover-letter drafts.\n- .playwright-mcp/ snapshot files (can''t read directly due to path escaping).\n\n**Pending tasks:**\n- Finish filling the Further application form: remaining required fields (Location City, target salary, how did you hear, relocation, data consent, EEO, Privacy Notice checkbox), resume upload, cover letter paste.\n- Handle remaining comboboxes.\n- Re-verify form, submit (browser_submit, which pauses for user).\n- Write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md (today is 2026-09-01 per the snapshot timestamps \u2014 wait, the task date is 2026-09-01, and the applied file is applied-2026-09-01.md already written from previous run). Hmm. Actually the current run \u2014 what date? The snapshots show 2026-09-01T21-41. So today is 2026-09-01. But applied-2026-09-01.md already exists from an earlier run today. \n\nWait, this is interesting. The applied-2026-09-01.md already exists. So what filename should the new run write? The rule says \"applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md exists in this workspace \u2014 write it as your final action\". If it already exists from an earlier run today, we might need to overwrite or the output already partially exists. Hmm. Actually, this is a subtle point. The existing applied-2026-09-01.md was from the prior run (Cambridge ERA:AI). This current run is ALSO 2026-09-01. \n\nActually, let me reconsider \u2014 maybe the current run overwrites/extends applied-2026-09-01.md, or the continuity rule says \"read ledger.md and the 1-2 most recent applied-*.md\" and \"Anything already sent or parked is done.\" The prior run wrote applied-2026-09-01.md. This run should probably append its result or the file gets updated. This is a decision point for the next step \u2014 I should flag the filename question.\n\nHmm, but actually maybe I''m overthinking. Let me note that the output filename already exists (applied-2026-09-01.md from today''s earlier run), so the next step should consider whether to append or use a new timestamped file.\n\nActually, given the driver fires repeatedly, and each run writes applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md, there''s potential overwrite. The safest is to note this ambiguity as a pending decision. But actually, re-reading: \"The run is not finished until applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md exists in this workspace \u2014 write it as your final action, every time.\" If it already exists, the requirement is satisfied in a sense, but the run should still record its result. Given the existing file is from today''s earlier run covering Cambridge, the new run likely needs to either append or create a dated file. I''ll flag this.\n\nLet me also reconsider the date. The task says \"targets.md \u2014 today''s shortlist\". The snapshot filenames say 2026-09-01. So today = 2026-09-01.\n\n**Next step:**\n- Continue filling the Further Greenhouse application form. Currently on the phone Country dropdown \u2014 typed \"United States\" filtering to 2 matches. Next: click/select the correct \"United States+1\" option to complete the country selection.\n\nLet me also note the specific facts used in form filling so far:\n- First Name: Jonathan\n- Last Name: Beale\n- Email: jonaston015@gmail.com\n- Phone: 9544940671\n- LinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale\n- Sponsorship: No (via unsafe code, getByRole option)\n- Years of career experience: Less than 4 years\n\nLet me now check facts.md content details I can extract. From the excerpt: \"Every field an application form asks for that is NOT on your resume gets its answer from this file, verbatim.\" Rule: if the answer is not here and not on the resume, it does not answer. It stops.\n\nI have limited detail on facts.md contents beyond the sponsorship (No) and data-consent. The assistant used:\n- work authorization: authorized to work in US\n- sponsorship: No\n\nLet me now also record the resume upload requirement and cover letter paste requirement for Further.\n\nLet me write the summary. I need to be concrete and preserve load-bearing details.\n\nLet me note the exact URL, exact field values, exact selectors that worked vs failed.\n\nLet me structure:\n\n### 1. Primary request and intent\n### 2. Key concepts and decisions\n### 3. Artifacts and files\n### 4. Errors and fixes\n### 5. All user messages\n### 6. Pending tasks\n### 7. Current work\n### 8. Next step\n\nFor user messages: The only user message is the big scheduled-run prompt. There''s also the assistant''s own todo_write but that''s assistant, not user. The \"user\" message is the scheduled run block. Actually the prompt says \"All user messages \u2014 a chronological list of every user message\". In this conversation, there''s one user message: the big scheduled run instruction. Let me list that (trimmed). Actually there''s only the one big instruction. The assistant''s actions are not user messages. So I list the one big scheduled-run prompt.\n\nWait \u2014 the todo_write was `assistant \u2192 todo_write`, so that''s assistant. The user message is just the big block. Let me note it''s a single large scheduled-run instruction.\n\nLet me be careful about dates. The filename is applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md. Today appears to be 2026-09-01.\n\nNow, one concern: the existing applied-2026-09-01.md \u2014 this run should produce output. Since it already exists, the next step needs to decide filename. I''ll flag it. Actually, thinking about it more \u2014 the run writes applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md as final action. If it already exists from today''s earlier Cambridge run, then the requirement is technically already met, but the run must record its result. I''ll note: either overwrite/extend applied-2026-09-01.md or the driver may expect a fresh file; flag as decision point. Given the file already exists, safest is to update/append it with the Further result, preserving the earlier Cambridge entry. I''ll note this.\n\nLet me write it concisely but completely.\n\nFor the resume upload \u2014 resume-path.txt has the PDF path. browser_upload_file to target resume input.\n\nCover letter \u2014 drafts/cover-letter-Further.md; paste the body (not markdown headers).\n\nEEO \u2014 decline to self-identify per facts.md.\n\nLet me also capture the important domain knowledge about comboboxes and", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, mcp__playwright__browser_click, mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate, mcp__playwright__browser_fill_form, mcp__playwright__browser_navigate, mcp__playwright__browser_run_code_unsafe, mcp__playwright__browser_snapshot, mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for, mcp__tavily__tavily-tavily_search, read_file, todo_write, web_fetch, web_search", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Apply \u2014 file the shortlist This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already e