INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-74dee9f835','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Apply — file the shortlist','cowork',136,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 22:46:02','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "browser_click", "browser_close", "browser_get_text", "browser_open_url", "browser_read_url", "browser_screenshot", "browser_select", "browser_snapshot", "browser_submit", "browser_type", "browser_upload_file", "browser_wait", "grep", "list_files", "playwright-browser_click", "playwright-browser_close", "playwright-browser_file_upload", "playwright-browser_fill_form", "playwright-browser_find", "playwright-browser_navigate", "playwright-browser_press_key", "playwright-browser_select_option", "playwright-browser_snapshot", "playwright-browser_take_screenshot", "playwright-browser_type", "playwright-browser_wait_for", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 78, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me analyze this conversation carefully to produce a structured summary.\n\nThe context: This is a scheduled automation run to file job applications. The AI coworker is working through applying to a job called \"Further \u2014 Senior AI Engineer\" via a Greenhouse ATS form.\n\nLet me trace through what happened:\n\n1. User (scheduled run) instructed to file the shortlisted application. Key constraints and rules established.\n\n2. The assistant explored the workspace:\n- Files found: FOCUS.md, applied-2026-09-01.md, drafts/, ledger.md, targets.md, facts.md, resume.txt, resume-path.txt, grants.md\n- FOCUS.md: state changed, agpack is the build focus, live center of gravity moved\n- ledger.md: records ERA:AI (skipped by applicant \u2014 \"do not re-attempt\"), Sprinter (sent), Hyro (skipped/closed), Valtech (closed)\n- targets.md: ranks 6 ON-FOCUS roles; only Valtech attempted\n- Next target: #2 Further \u2014 Senior AI Engineer (draft present, not in ledger)\n\n3. Staging files read:\n- facts.md: answer bank rule \u2014 if answer not here and not on resume, don''t answer\n- resume.txt: Jonathan Beale, Fort Lauderdale FL, jonaston015@gmail.com, (954) 494-0671, linkedin.com/in/jonathan-beale, github.com/iconbaypark2900. ML Engineer, 2.5 yrs GCP.\n- resume-path.txt: /home/iconbaypark2900/Documents/Jonathan_Beale_Resume_2026.pdf\n- drafts/cover-letter-Further.md\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Further.md\n- grants.md\n\n4. Discovery: Tried browser_url (unknown tool), web_search (multiple), found Greenhouse URL: https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002\n\n5. Navigated with mcp__playwright__browser_navigate\n\n6. Snapshot issues: snapshot files stored outside workspace, filesystem MCP access denied (path outside allowed directories: /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51 not in /data/home/dcode-stack, /data/home/LibreChat, /data/home/liaison-agentSystem). Had to use inline browser_snapshot tool with REF IDs.\n\n7. Form filling progress:\n- Tried browser_fill_form with \"#e90\" \u2014 failed (# prefix wrong). Retried with bare \"e90\" refs \u2014 succeeded.\n- browser_file_upload failed (modal state not present). \n- Filled textboxes: Jonathan, Beale, jonaston015@gmail.com, (954) 494-0671, LinkedIn, etc.\n- Years of career experience: \"Less than 4 years\" (e445) \u2014 candidate has ~2.5 yrs\n- Sponsorship: \"No\" (e457)\n- Relocation: \"Yes\" (e465)\n- Country: \"United States +1\" (e474)\n- Now working on Location (City), near offices, consent, EEO\n\n8. Location (City) combobox opened \u2014 \"Fort Lauderdale\" not in list. Search for \"Florida\" \u2014 no matches.\n\nSo the run was in progress, blocked on finding the right city from a limited Greenhouse location dropdown list.\n\nLet me note important technical details:\n- Tool naming: built-in `browser_*` tools are unknown here (browser_url, browser_navigate all return \"unknown tool\"). Must use `mcp__playwright__browser_*` tools.\n- browser_fill_form: refs must be bare (no # prefix). Error: \"#e90 does not match any elements.\"\n- browser_file_upload: can only be used when modal state present \u2014 needs the file input active first.\n- Snapshot files (.playwright-mcp/*.yml) stored outside workspace \u2014 read_file fails, filesystem MCP access denied. Use inline browser_snapshot.\n- Greenhouse: combos are React [role=combobox] \u2014 click-open, snapshot, click option by text.\n- browser_click refuses \"Submit\"/\"Send\"/\"Finish\" buttons \u2014 must use browser_submit.\n\nLet me note the important rules from the prompt:\n- Do NOT use run_shell, ls, cat, curl or Python script\n- Take EXACTLY ONE application per run\n- Priority order: deadline inside 14 days, then highest-ranked ON-FOCUS with draft, then next best\n- Skip already in ledger with status sent or parked\n- Open DIRECT application link, never aggregator\n- HARD RULE on unknown fields: if required field answer not in facts.md and not in resume.txt, don''t answer \u2014 stop, record, move on\n- Never treat TODO in facts.md as permission to improvise\n- Demographic/EEO: \"decline to self-identify\" unless stated otherwise\n- browser_snapshot and browser_screenshot before sending\n- browser_submit \u2014 expect it to pause for user; if it does, application is parked\n- FORBIDDEN during form fill: browser_run_code_unsafe, browser_evaluate, web_search/tavily\n- REQUIRED shape: ~8 tool calls\n- Use Playwright MCP tools not built-in browser tools\n- Dropdowns: Greenhouse/Ashby are React comboboxes, not <select>. Click open, snapshot, click option by visible text. For genuine <select> use browser_select.\n- If same control fails twice, stop.\n- ONE target, hard wall-clock limit. ~6 minutes to submit or stop.\n- Park and record reasons for: sign-in wall, CAPTCHA, timed assessment, TODO question, form wants non-existent document, government ID/SSN/DOB/bank details.\n\nOutput:\n- Write applied-YYYY-MM-DD.md\n- Append rows to ledger.md\n\nNow let me structure the summary.\n\nCurrent work: Filling the Greenhouse Further form. Textboxes filled. Comboboxes: years experience, sponsorship, relocation, country done. Currently stuck on Location (City) \u2014 Fort Lauderdale not in Greenhouse''s limited city list.\n\nNext step: Need to find the right city from Greenhouse''s dropdown options, or park/blocked if Fort Lauderdale isn''t available (considering the hard rule \u2014 but the city field isn''t a \"hard\" legal question like work auth; still, need an honest answer from resume/facts. Candidate is in Fort Lauderdale, FL. If it''s not available, could pick a nearby metro or a general FL option, or record as needs answer). Actually \u2014 city is contact info from facts/resume. If Greenhouse doesn''t have Fort Lauderdale, the assistant needs to find the closest option or check what options are available.\n\nLet me write the summary now.\n\nLet me capture the key ref IDs:\n- e90 First Name, e95 Last Name\n- e150 Resume/CV attach input\n- e200 years of career experience (combobox)\n- e222, e247, e247... (various combos)\n- e200 \"How many years of career experience\"\n- Sponsorship combobox \"Will you now, or in the\" \u2014 option e457 \"No\"\n- Relocation \"Are you open to relocation?\" \u2014 option e465 \"Yes\"\n- Country combobox e120 \u2014 option e474 \"United States +1\"\n- Location (City) combobox e141\n\nLet me note the successful fills were done via browser_click with role matching (e.g. `page.getByRole(''option'', { name: ''Less than 4 years'' }).click()`), not by clicking the ref. Actually the assistant used mcp__playwright__browser_click with target being a ref, but then the underlying code used getByRole. Interesting \u2014 the browser_click tool with target=e445 actually triggered `page.getByRole(''option'', {name:''Less than 4 years''}).click()`. So the tool maps ref to element. Actually looking closer, when clicking options it used getByRole name matching. When clicking combos it used getByRole name matching too. So the ref targeting works but the tool translated to role-based selection.\n\nActually, I should be careful. The assistant called `mcp__playwright__browser_click` with `{\"target\": \"e445\"}` and the result ran JS `page.getByRole(''option'', { name: ''Less than 4 years'' }).click()`. So the tool resolved e445 to the option element and clicked it. Good.\n\nLet me note this: the mcp browser tools accept ref targets and execute appropriate Playwright selectors.\n\nImportant: The resume upload (browser_file_upload) has NOT been completed yet \u2014 it failed with \"modal state present\" error. This is still pending.\n\nLet me also note the constraints on tools:\n- Built-in browser tools (browser_url, browser_navigate) return \"unknown tool\" \u2014 must use mcp__playwright__browser_*\n- The assistant tried mcp__playwright__browser_navigate successfully\n- list_files works in workspace; filesystem MCP scoped elsewhere (access denied)\n\nLet me write all sections.\n\nFor \"All user messages\" \u2014 this is a scheduled run, so the user message is the big prompt. I''ll list it as one user message (the full system/scheduled instruction). Plus there were no other user messages in this turn really \u2014 the assistant was acting autonomously. Actually the only user message is the scheduled run prompt. Let me represent it.\n\nWait, there''s the assistant todo_write items \u2014 those are assistant actions, not user messages. The only user message is the initial scheduled run instruction.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nFor pending tasks:\n- Resume upload still pending (browser_file_upload failed)\n- Fill remaining combos: Location (City), \"near our offices\", consent, EEO\n- Cover letter \u2014 need to figure out how Greenhouse accepts it (text box vs