ter\n- drafts/resume-tweaks-Further.md\n- ledger.md \u2014 existing rows\n- targets.md \u2014 shortlist\n- FOCUS.md\n- .playwright-mcp/ snapshots \u2014 stored outside workspace, inaccessible via read_file (filesystem MCP scoped to /data/home/...), so use inline browser_snapshot.\n\nLet me be concrete about the ledger rows that matter:\n- ERA:AI \u2014 skipped by applicant (\"do not re-attempt\")\n- Sprinter \u2014 sent\n- Hyro \u2014 skipped/closed\n- Valtech \u2014 closed\n\nAnd the fact that only Valtech among the 6 ON-FOCUS targets has been attempted.\n\nLet me write.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the \"needs an answer from me\" angle. The candidate''s city \u2014 Fort Lauderdale \u2014 is on the resume, so it IS known. The issue is just Greenhouse''s dropdown doesn''t list it. So this isn''t a hard-rule block; it''s a UI limitation. The assistant should pick the closest available option (e.g., a Miami metro area, or a \"Other\" + type, or select a FL city). This is a decision point for next step.\n\nLet me finalize.\n\nOne more: the browser_fill_form success used", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: browser_navigate, browser_url, list_files, mcp__filesystem__filesystem-search_files, mcp__playwright__browser_click, mcp__playwright__browser_file_upload, mcp__playwright__browser_fill_form, mcp__playwright__browser_find, mcp__playwright__browser_navigate, mcp__playwright__browser_snapshot, mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for, read_file, todo_write, web_search", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Apply \u2014 file the shortlist This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. File the applications the job and grant automations have already shortlisted. The discovery side of this pipeline works \u2014 eighteen runs of shortlists and tailored drafts. What it has never produced is a sent application. That is this job: take what is already researched and drafted, and put it into the employer''s form. Everything you need is staged in your own workspace by plain filename\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788301053.2556477, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
