INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-931c3f3e93','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-fe38324f51','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Apply — file the shortlist','cowork',51,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 23:42:57','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "browser_click", "browser_close", "browser_get_text", "browser_open_url", "browser_read_url", "browser_screenshot", "browser_select", "browser_snapshot", "browser_submit", "browser_type", "browser_upload_file", "browser_wait", "grep", "list_files", "playwright-browser_click", "playwright-browser_close", "playwright-browser_file_upload", "playwright-browser_fill_form", "playwright-browser_find", "playwright-browser_navigate", "playwright-browser_press_key", "playwright-browser_select_option", "playwright-browser_snapshot", "playwright-browser_take_screenshot", "playwright-browser_type", "playwright-browser_wait_for", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-4763542dd1','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c6cf366b90','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Fellowship & residency finder','research',87,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-01 23:57:37','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 70, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me carefully analyze this conversation to produce the structured summary. The user is an AI coworker running a scheduled automation. Let me trace through everything.\n\nThe task: A scheduled \"Fellowship & residency finder\" run. The user wants the coworker to find fellowships, residencies, and programmes worth applying for based on the resume, with a strong emphasis on fellowships/grants over standard jobs. Standard openings are now secondary (at most three, only if strong fit).\n\nLet me extract all the load-bearing details.\n\n**User''s request and intent (from the initial scheduled run prompt):**\n- Find fellowships, residencies, and programmes worth applying for, based on resume. Standard job openings secondary \u2014 at most 3, only if unusually strong fit.\n- Emphasis changed: fellowships close on a date. Six (actually 7 listed) fellowships already have tailored drafts on file and NOT ONE has had its deadline checked.\n- The resume is in workspace as resume.txt \u2014 read it.\n- Constraints: DO NOT use run_shell, ls, cat, curl or a Python script, do NOT reach into ~/Documents/. Web search allowed, needs no approval.\n- Work, don''t narrate \u2014 carry each step through. Produce output file as final action every time even if a step failed.\n- FIRST, before any new search \u2014 check the 7 already-drafted programmes (GovAI, AIAF, ADF, CTEC, CSC Generation, Lila Sciences, MATS Residency Winter 2027). For each find official page, report OPEN (with deadline + apply URL), CLOSED (closed date + next cycle), or UNVERIFIABLE.\n- The drafts are in drafts/: cover-letter-govai.md, cover-letter-aiaf.md, cover-letter-ADF.md, cover-letter-CTEC.md, cover-letter-csc-generation.md, cover-letter-lilasciences.md, cover-letter-MATS.md.\n- WHAT TO SEARCH FOR \u2014 two categories:\n  1. Standard openings matching profile (seniority, domain, technical strengths).\n  2. Fellowships and residencies that function as jobs: AI/ML residencies, research fellowships with salary/stipend, industry fellowships, government/think-tank technical fellowships. Include even when title says \"fellow\" not \"engineer\".\n- Do NOT include funding-only fellowships (grants that pay for own independent work, no employer) \u2014 those belong to separate weekly grant digest. Test: if you work FOR an organisation \u2192 here; if receiving money for own project \u2192 not.\n- Search openings posted in last ~7 days, plus every fellowship/residency/programme whose window is OPEN now regardless of posting age.\n- For each match record: organisation, role title, standard vs fellowship/residency, location + remote policy, salary/stipend if stated, link, fit assessment naming specific resume evidence + gaps. Record deadline when exists.\n- Rank by fit, keep plausible matches, report EVERY open+plausible match \u2014 aim 10-15. Don''t pad with bad fits; don''t withhold real matches.\n- For top 6 matches: create drafts/ subfolder with per role: cover-letter-<organisation>.md (tailored, real evidence, referencing what org does) and resume-tweaks-<organisation>.md (edits to strengthen: which bullets to lead with, rephrase, cut).\n- Never invent experience, credentials, dates.\n- Save shortlist as jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md, fellowships and standard roles clearly labelled. Do NOT submit application or contact anyone \u2014 produce files only.\n- CONTINUITY \u2014 FIRST before searching:\n  1. list_files, read 1-2 most recent prior outputs (same file-naming pattern).\n  2. Carry forward live items, mark closed/resolved, spend search budget on what''s NEW.\n  3. If something reported before changed state, say so explicitly with date.\n  4. Never re-report unchanged item as fresh.\n- FOCUS \u2014 before anything else:\n  1. read_file FOCUS.md.\n  2. Tag every item ON-FOCUS or ADJACENT.\n  3. Lead with ON-FOCUS, cap ADJACENT at three, put last.\n  4. If FOCUS.md missing, say so, treat all as ADJACENT.\n\n**Key state from prior runs (in memory / brain_note):**\n- Candidate: Jonathan Beale. ML Solutions Architect at Hewani (remote, Apr 2025\u2013Present), former AI/ML Engineer at Mutual of Omaha (Jan 2024\u2013Feb 2025). ~2.5 yrs production ML: GCP Vertex AI end-to-end, RAG over insurance docs, SLM-agent ETL, REST inference APIs, Python/PyTorch/LangChain/Docker. No degree (important \u2014 Lila requires degree).\n- Sprinter Health: SENT 2026-09-01 (first application ever, ends August 10 drafts/0 sends era).\n- Prior runs: jobs-2026-09-01.md and jobs-2026-09-01-PM.md exist.\n- Drafts folder has many cover letters: app-imachines, ADF, Bybit, CHEQ, CTEC, Clover-Health, ERA, EvolutionIQ, Further, GCPEngineer, Grid-Dynamics, and govai, MATS, lilasciences, csc-generation, aiaf.\n\n**Verified states at end of this turn:**\n- GovAI Research Fellowship 2026: CLOSED, deadline Aug 16 2026 (AoE).\n- AIAF Fellowship 2026: CLOSED, deadline Aug 17 2026 (AoE).\n- ADF (Applied Data Fellowship, Harris School UChicago): OPEN, rolling (start Oct/Nov 2026).\n- CTEC (CyberMedia Technologies) AI/ML Engineer: OPEN, rolling, Greenhouse 5102656008, remote US, OPM Public Trust required (US citizen).\n- CSC Generation Sr ML Engineer Causal & Decision Systems: OPEN, hybrid Austin TX, FL eligible, in-person interview required, Greenhouse/Lever.\n- Lila Sciences AI Residency 2026 Cohort: OPEN (rolling until 10/27/2026) but requires a degree he lacks \u2014 caveat. Cambridge MA, 6-12 months.\n- MATS Residency Winter 2027: OPEN, deadline Oct 31 2026 (11:59pm AoE). In-person Berkeley/London, Jan 19\u2013Apr 10 2027.\n- Cambridge ERA:AI Fellowship 2027: OPEN, deadline Sep 13. (from memory note \u2014 actually \"Sep 13\" but I should note the search result just said applications opened; the memory note said Sep 13.)\n\nActually wait \u2014 the ERA deadline. In the prior memory note it says \"Cambridge ERA:AI OPEN (Sep 13)\". But the actual web fetch for erafellowship.org just showed nav. The search result said \"applications have opened for in-person paid 10-week Winter Research Fellow...\". Let me note the deadline as Sep 13 per the memory, but flag uncertainty. Actually the instructions for this run say to verify, and the assistant is the one doing it. I''ll record ERA OPEN with the deadline being Sep 13 per memory but uncertain \u2014 need to confirm exact deadline. Hmm, actually the run requires reporting exact deadline. The memory says Sep 13. I''ll record that.\n\n**Errors encountered:**\n- governance.ai returns HTTP 403 Forbidden for research-fellowship-2027 and /careers/ pages. Tried web.archive.org and it timed out.\n- AI Residency Program search returned OpenAI 2026 Residency, OpenAI Safety Fellowship, Anthropic Fellows Program \u2014 these may be bucketed to grant digest or reported.\n- Some web_fetch failed (403, timeout).\n\n**Tools available/used:**\n- read_file, list_files, todo_write, brain_recall, brain_note, mcp__tavily__tavily-tavily_search, web_fetch.\n- Do NOT use: run_shell, ls, cat, curl, Python scripts.\n\n**State at end of turn / what''s left:**\n- The turn ended mid-search. After the last search results (GovAI closed confirmed, ADF/CTEC/CSC/Lila open, plus new finds: OpenAI 2026 Residency, OpenAI Safety Fellowship 2026-2027, Anthropic Fellows Program, AI Policy Fellowship). The assistant is still in the \"Search for NEW fellowships, residencies, standard roles\" phase (in_progress). The output file jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md (today''s date = 2026-09-01) has NOT been written yet.\n- Todo list shows 4 todos; the search todo is in_progress.\n\nSo pending: complete fresh searches, compile the shortlist, write jobs-2026-09-01.md (today''s file) with fellowships + standard roles labelled, create drafts/ cover letters + resume-tweaks for top 6 (though some already drafted \u2014 the top 6 of THIS run need to be created; need to figure out which are new).\n\nLet me be careful: The top 6 matches need cover-letter and resume-tweaks per role. Many already exist from prior runs. The new ones to potentially draft this run: the ones that are open and new \u2014 ADF, CTEC, CSC Generation, Lila, and the fresh finds (OpenAI Residency, OpenAI Safety, Anthropic Fellows, AI Policy Fellowship, maybe Forward Deployed Engineer Google Cloud).\n\nLet me note the date. Today is 2026-09-01 (PM run). FOCUS.md is week of 2026-08-31.\n\nNow, one important nuance: The task says produce jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md. Given the prior runs already produced jobs-2026-09-01.md and jobs-2026-09-01-PM.md, this third run should probably produce jobs-2026-09-01-PM2.md or jobs-2026-09-01-2.md or similar. But the instructions say \"jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md\". I''ll note the filename needs a qualifier to avoid clobbering.\n\nLet me also note the \"work, don''t narrate\" and \"always write the file even if steps failed\" constraints.\n\nNow let me structure the summary.\n\nLet me think about the artifacts:\n\n**Files read:**\n- FOCUS.md (week of 2026-08-31, rewritten 2026-08-31; state change: agpack \"build\" is live center of gravity, 08-30 sessions).\n- resume.txt (Jonathan Beale, Fort Lauderdale FL, ML Solutions Architect, Hewani remote Apr 2025\u2013Present, former AI/ML Engineer Mutual of Omaha Jan 2024\u2013Feb 2025, ~2.5 yrs production ML GCP Vertex AI, RAG, SLM-agent ETL, REST inference APIs, Python/PyTorch/LangChain/Docker, no degree).\n- jobs-2026-09-01.md and jobs-2026-09-01-PM.md (prior runs today) and jobs-2026-08-31.md referenced.\n- Drafts: cover-letter-govai.md, cover-letter-aiaf.md, cover-letter-ADF.md, cover-letter-CTEC.md, cover-letter-csc-generation.md, cover-letter-lilasciences.md, cover-letter-MATS.md, plus others in drafts/ folder.\n- 2026-09-01 PM run already drafted 9 items: ERA:AI, Sprinter, Hyro, Valtech, Further, Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit, GCP Engineer.\n\nWait \u2014 let me re-read. In one of the tool results, the assistant said: \"The morning and PM runs already drafted 9 items (ERA:AI, Sprinter, Hyro, Valtech, Further, Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit, GCP Engineer).\" But wait, Sprinter was SENT. Hmm, and there''s also the memory note listing 6 fresh GCP/RAG/agentic remote roles drafted (Valtech FDE $125-225k, Further Senior AI Engineer, Stellar Senior...). Let me reconcile.\n\nActually the memory note: \"09-01 PM run: 6 fresh GCP/RAG/agentic remote roles drafted (Valtech FDE $125\u2013225k, Further Senior AI Engineer, Stellar Senior...)\" and \"Sprint Health ML Engineer application SENT 2026-09-01 (first application ever \u2014 ends August 10 drafts/0 sends).\"\n\nAnd \"drafts/app-imachines.md, drafts/cover-letter-ADF.md, drafts/cover-letter-Bybit.md, drafts/cover-letter-CHEQ.md, drafts/cover-letter-CTEC.md, drafts/cover-letter-Clover-Health.md, drafts/cover-letter-ERA.md, drafts/cover-letter-EvolutionIQ.md, drafts/cover-letter-Further.md, drafts/cover-letter-GCPEngineer.md, drafts/cover-letter-Grid-Dynamics.md, drafts/cover-l...\"\n\nSo drafts/ has a lot. The list_files output was truncated (\"drafts/cover-l...\"). Let me note what''s confirmed visible: app-imachines", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_note, brain_recall, list_files, mcp__tavily__tavily-tavily_search, read_file, todo_write, web_fetch", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Fellowship & residency finder This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Find FELLOWSHIPS, RESIDENCIES AND PROGRAMMES worth applying for, based on my resume. Standard job openings are now SECONDARY \u2014 report at most three, and only if they are an unusually strong fit. The applicant has redirected this pipeline at fellowships and grants. WHY THE EMPHASIS CHANGED: fellowships close on a DATE, not when a role is filled, so a missed window cannot be recovered. \u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1788307021.9455445, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
