INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-1763f06a88','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/__task__task-ecad448aa3','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Knowledge base — ingest yesterday''s findin','repo-ops',96,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-09-02 10:16:04','{"tools": ["brain_note", "brain_recall", "grep", "list_files", "mcp__qdrant__qdrant-qdrant-find", "mcp__qdrant__qdrant-qdrant-store", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "run_shell", "todo_write", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 52, "summary_text": "[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\n\nLet me analyze this conversation carefully to produce the structured summary. This is an AI coworker''s session history for a scheduled knowledge base ingestion job.\n\nLet me trace through what happened:\n\n1. **Primary request**: A scheduled automation job to ingest yesterday''s findings into a Qdrant knowledge base. The task is very detailed with specific constraints.\n\n2. **Key concepts**:\n   - Qdrant KB ingestion job\n   - The two filesystem bases: `~/OpenWorker` and `~/openworker-tasks`\n   - The dedup mandate (store-direct for today''s files, only run find for older restatements)\n   - The budget constraints (25 stores, 25 finds, 10 files max, 6 per file)\n   - FOCUS.md for ON-FOCUS/ADJACENT tagging\n   - The ledger format\n   - The shell rules (no heredocs, write scripts to files, small commands)\n   - The store script pattern (payload key `document`, 384-dim Cosine vector `fast-all-minilm`, fastembed HTTP path)\n   - `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge` is a writable root\n\n3. **Errors and fixes**:\n   - `read_file` refused paths outside workspace sandbox (\"path escapes the workspace\")\n   - The assistant read non-workspace files via shell instead\n   - Transient timing issues where files appeared \"MISSING\" then appeared\n   - Two parallel trees: `openworker-tasks` vs `OpenWorker` \u2014 the 09-02 files actually live under `OpenWorker` (mtime today), while `openworker-tasks` has only older copies\n   - The batch `sed` display was offset \u2014 read files individually\n   - The `/data/home` vs `/home/iconbaypark2900` shell vs filesystem MCP path difference\n\n4. **Files/artifacts**:\n   - Workspace: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/__task__task-ecad448aa3/`\n   - FOCUS.md \u2014 week of 2026-08-31\n   - Prior ingest outputs: ingest_2026-09-01b.md, report_2026-09-01b.md\n   - Source files to read: 09-02 dated files under OpenWorker\n   - store_2026-09-01.py, ingest_kb.py \u2014 prior scripts to study\n   - NEW: store_2026-09-02.py \u2014 written (the store script)\n   - Need: ledger-2026-09-02.md (or similar naming) \u2014 NOT yet written\n   - Need: report \u2014 NOT yet written\n\nLet me note the current state: The assistant just finished writing `store_2026-09-02.py` with 12 planned stores (9 ON-FOCUS + 3 ADJACENT). The next step is to run the script, then write the ledger, then check the collection count via curl, then update brain threads.\n\nWait, let me re-read the task. There''s also the THREADS section \u2014 the assistant needs to do brain_recall and brain_note for subjects that moved. But that''s a follow-up step.\n\nLet me also note the prior knowledge base state: from brain_recall, the KB `default` collection holds 41 points at 2026-08-31, and report_2026-09-01b.md says it grew 51\u219260. So the current total before this run should be 60 (from the 09-01 second PM run).\n\nLet me note the file paths carefully:\n- Source files read (via shell):\n  - `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-1b2c4d3f13/papers-2026-09-02.md`\n  - `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-f471043f3e/breakage-2026-09-02.md`\n  - `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c6cf366b90/jobs-2026-09-02.md`\n  - `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea/repo-activity