t, actually the assistant in the previous turn said \"Read DESIGN.md\" \u2014 maybe it read it via a different mechanism, or maybe it didn''t actually exist. Let me flag this.\n\nLet me trace what the assistant learned:\n\nFrom the Scope enum investigation:\n- The previous summary said \"Scope enum confirmed closed - 8 members, no payout capability\" \u2014 this is consistent.\n- But the assistant''s own PROJECT_MAP.md says \"9 members\" (doc error). The assistant noted: \"My own `PROJECT_MAP.md` says ''9 members'', which is a doc error to fix.\"\n\nSo this is a new finding: PROJECT_MAP.md has a doc error saying \"9 members\" when there are actually 8. This needs to be fixed.\n\nFrom the shell command output:\n```\n=== all Scope members ===\nfs.read\nfs.write\nnet.fetch\nclock.now\nrandom\nmemory.get\nmemory.set\nemit.text\n```\n8 members confirmed.\n\nThe enum length from python command was cut off, but the assistant already established 8 members.\n\nFrom railrouter.py and P4_TASK.md:\n- Phase 2 (P4) settlement routing is DONE\n- P4_TASK.md line 3-4: \"When done, add a `## P4 (Phase 2) \u2014 DONE` block to `concord/PHASES.md` and stop \u2014 the next phase (P5, the payout/risk apex...)\"\n\nFrom invariant.py, reality.py, pillars.py:\n- The one invariant: \"Every move of partner value is signed, scoped, budgeted, and recorded before it is final \u2014 and never final until it reconciles.\"\n- Facets: signed, scoped, budgeted, recorded, reconciled\n\nFrom runtime.py, __main__.py:\n- Phase 0 settlement runtime (pure-math ERC-4626)\n- Command surface: check, build, and others (8-verb surface from before)\n\nSo the assistant''s reasoning:\n- Settlement progression complete through Phase 2\n- Phase 3 payout genuinely blocked (closed agpack Scope enum + no P5 prompt)\n- The real next step likely lives in the one invariant''s five facets: signed, scoped, budgeted, recorded, reconciled\n- budgeted (Phase 2) and reconciled (Phase 0/1) are wired\n- Need to check whether signed (trust.signing) and scoped (trust.delegation) are consumed by concord settlement or merely declared as REAL symbols\n\nSo the assistant was about to examine the runtime, the verify-invariant command, and DESIGN.md \u2014 but DESIGN.md read failed.\n\nLet me now build the summary.\n\n**1. Primary request and intent:**\n\nThe user''s request throughout: the user is the ConcordCircuit project lead. The intent is to get the composition layer (`concord`) working correctly by composing read-only pillars, grounded in real source. Recent turns: \"Write up in detail what is next\" and \"proceed with the next steps.\"\n\nStanding constraints:\n- No egress: no network/subprocess/socket. Deterministic (fixed seeds, no RNG).\n- Pillars are READ-ONLY: `agpack`, `sentinel-local`, `metered-web-broker` cannot be modified by `concord`.\n- The unifying invariant must be preserved.\n- Verify verbs must be run to confirm work.\n- Docs must stay accurate (no stale \"PENDING\" markers). Actually \u2014 the docs accuracy constraint: the unifying invariant must be preserved; docs must be accurate.\n\nWait, let me be careful about what the standing constraints actually are. Let me reconstruct from the previous summary:\n- No egress: no network/subprocess/socket. Deterministic (fixed seeds, no RNG).\n- Pillars are READ-ONLY: `agpack`, `sentinel-local`, `metered-web-broker` cannot be modified by `concord`.\n- The unifying invariant must be preserved.\n- Verify verbs must be run to confirm work.\n- Docs must stay accurate (no stale \"PENDING\" markers).\n\nThese all still hold. Plus new: the Scope enum member count in PROJECT_MAP.md is wrong (says 9, actually 8) \u2014 needs fixing.\n\n**2. Key concepts and decisions:**\n\n- ConcordCircuit: composition layer over 3 read-only pillars.\n- The one invariant (concord/invariant.py:5): \"Every move of partner value is signed, scoped, budgeted, and recorded before it is final \u2014 and never final until it reconciles.\" Facets: signed, scoped, budgeted, recorded, reconciled.\n- Phases:\n  - Phase 0: concord.runtime \u2014 pure-math ERC-4626 settlement \u2014 DONE\n  - Phase 1: drift seed \u2014 DONE\n  - Phase 2 (P4): settlement routing railrouter.py \u2014 DONE\n  - Phase 3 (P5): payout/risk apex \u2014 PENDING, blocked\n- The closed Scope enum: `agpack/sandbox/capabilities.py` \u2014 `Scope(str, Enum)` with 8 members: fs.read, fs.write, net.fetch, clock.now, random, memory.get, memory.set, emit.text. No payout capability. `agpack/trust/delegation.py` `verify()` hard-fails unknown scope.\n- Doc error: PROJECT_MAP.md says \"9 members\" but there are 8.\n- The real next step: check whether the two agpack-derived facets `signed` (trust.signing) and `scoped` (trust.delegation) are actually consumed by the concord settlement or merely declared as REAL symbols.\n\n**3. Artifacts and files:**\n\n- `concord/railrouter.py` \u2014 Phase 2 settlement router. (from prior)\n- `concord/PHASES.md` \u2014 phase record. Line 97 Phase 2 \u2192 DONE. (from prior)\n- `concord/PROJECT_MAP.md` \u2014 179 lines. Project map. Has doc error (says 9 members).\n- `concord/invariant.py` (63 lines) \u2014 the one invariant. Facets: signed, scoped, budgeted, recorded, reconciled.\n- `concord/reality.py` (212 lines) \u2014 STUB-vs-REAL reality checks, probes real source.\n- `concord/pillars.py` (128 lines) \u2014 pillar symbol table.\n- `concord/runtime.py` (515 lines) \u2014 Phase 0 settlement runtime.\n- `concord/__main__.py` (496 lines) \u2014 command surface.\n- `P4_TASK.md` (355 lines) \u2014 Phase 2 spec.\n- `concord/DESIGN.md` \u2014 previously read (per prior summary, 97 lines, P1 composition doc). BUT the read just now FAILED with \"not a file: concord/DESIGN.md\". Flag as discrepancy \u2014 either path wrong or file moved/deleted.\n- `phase1_NOTES.md` (77 lines) \u2014 Phase 1 notes.\n- `agpack/sandbox/capabilities.py` \u2014 Scope enum (read, 8 members).\n- `agpack/trust/delegation.py` \u2014 verify hard-fails.\n- `metered-web